$plugin->release   = '5.9.310'; // USI-CERT-KEY-FIX (v5.9.310): students.php checked decoded['hasCert'] from /api/usi/status but the server has always returned certUploaded and certReady — hasCert was never set so $_usi_cert_ok was always false, causing the amber "USI Machine Credential not uploaded" banner to show permanently even on sites (e.g. IFCBAA) with a valid cert already uploaded. Fixed: condition now checks certUploaded || certReady, matching the actual response shape. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026081300310. // USI-CONFIG-KEY-FIX (v5.9.308): students.php read get_config('api_url') but the key written by usi_settings.php is 'apiurl' (no underscore) — the key was never found so the "USI Not Configured" modal fired every time even when USI was fully set up. Fixed: changed get_config key from 'api_url' to 'apiurl'. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026072800308. // INLINE NAT00080 UPLOAD ON STUDENTS PAGE DOB SYNC BAR // VERIFY-BTN-FORM-FIX (v5.9.298): "Verify USI" buttons on students.php sit inside the bulk-action <form id="student-action-form" method="post">. HTML buttons default to type="submit" so clicking "Verify via usi.gov.au" was submitting the form and navigating to the action URL (showing a Moodle error page) instead of running the AJAX call. Fixed: (1) added type="button" to all three rtoc-usi-verify-btn elements in students.php and student_usi_verify.php so they can never submit a form; (2) added e.preventDefault() to the JS delegated click handler in students.php so the default action is explicitly blocked before the fetch call runs. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026072800298. + CERT-CREDITS-BREAK-FIX + AUTOCERT-COMPLETE-FIX (v5.9.297): Three bugs fixed by 12-agent parallel audit. (1) TASK-VARIANT-ARCHIVE-FIX: process_enrolment_task.php UNION queries into qualunit_courses had no is_archive filter — archived/superseded semester delivery courses (is_archive=1) were triggering live AVETMISS enrolment record creation AND autocert qualification-completion checks. Fixed: AND (quc.is_archive IS NULL OR quc.is_archive = 0) added to both UNION queries. (2) CERT-CREDITS-BREAK-FIX: generate_qual_certs.php used 'break 2' on INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS — this silently killed both the cert-type loop and the student loop with no record of which students were skipped. Fixed: replaced with a $creditsExhausted flag; inner loop breaks cleanly and outer loop continues, counting remaining students as failed so the summary shows the exact number skipped. (3) AUTOCERT-COMPLETE-FIX: local_rtocompliance_autocerts rows written by process_enrolment_task with status='pending' were never updated to 'complete' after certs were issued — the admin autocert queue grew without bound showing all historical completions as still outstanding. Fixed: after successful cert issuance for a student in generate_qual_certs.php, the matching autocert row (if any, status='pending') is updated to status='complete' with timeprocessed=now. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026072800297. (v5.9.296): Four bugs fixed across the enrolment→qualbuilder→certificate pipeline found by full parallel audit. (1) RESULTS-COMPLETION-ENROLMENTS-FIX: check_full_qual_completion() (lib.php) only checked Moodle course_completions — if an RTO manually entered or imported AVETMISS outcomes (20/51/60/81) but Moodle course completion was not enabled on the course, generate_course_certs.php issued a SoA instead of Testamur. Fixed: added enrolments table fallback check per unit so positive AVETMISS outcomes count as completion when Moodle completion is not recorded. (2) SOA-OUTCOME-FIX: get_completed_units_for_qual() (lib.php) returned hardcoded outcome '20' (Competent) for every unit on partial SoA PDFs — units completed via RPL (51), Credit Transfer (60), or Non-Assessed Satisfactory (81) all incorrectly showed as Competent. Fixed: actual outcomeidentifier fetched from enrolments table and returned. Same function also gained the enrolments fallback and the missing selected=1 filter. (3) SOA-SELECTED-UNITS-FIX: get_completed_units_for_qual() was missing selected=1 on the qualunits query — unselected/deselected unit rows could appear on issued SoA PDFs. Fixed: selected=1 added. (4) IMPORT-VARIANT-FIX: student_enrolments.php Moodle import queries (linked_units + fallback_qual) only checked qualunits.courseid — students enrolled in a variant delivery course imported with no unitcode and no programcode, appearing as a bare course-level record rather than per-unit AVETMISS records. Fixed: UNION with qualunit_courses (is_archive=0) added to both queries. RESULTS-PAGE-DATA-FIX (v5.9.295): Six accuracy bugs fixed in qualbuilder_results.php (View Results page). (1) RESULTS-SELECTED-UNITS-FIX: $units query was missing selected=1 filter — "Units in Product" stat counted unselected/deselected unit rows, the per-student progress grid showed unselected units as columns, and the progress % denominator was inflated; Core Units and Elective Units stats already used selected=1 making all three stats inconsistent. Fixed: selected=1 added to $units query so all four stats (Units in Product, Core, Elective, progress%) share the same unit set. (2) RESULTS-VARIANT-STUDENT-FIX: student matching SQL fallback OR clause only checked qualunits.courseid (primary courses) — students who enrolled via a variant delivery course but whose programcode was not set (enrolled before auto-detection) were silently excluded from the results table. Fixed: UNION with qualunit_courses (is_archive=0) added to the courseid IN subquery, matching the same pattern applied in process_enrolment_task.php, lib.php, and generate_qual_certs.php in v5.9.293. (3) RESULTS-STATS-MATCH-FIX: $totalstudents and $completedstudents stat queries used programcode-only matching — narrower than the student table query which used the courseid fallback — meaning "Total Enrolled" could show fewer students than the table row count and "In Progress" (= Total - Completed) could go negative. Both stat queries now use the same programcode-OR-courseid(primary+variant) approach as the student table. (4) RESULTS-COMPLETED-UNITS-FILTER: completedstudents "all units finalised" subquery now also filters selected=1 so it uses the same unit set as the display. QB-LIST-TOTAL-FIX + VARIANT-COURSE-CERT-TYPE-FIX (v5.9.294): (1) qualbuilder.php list page UNITS column and LINKED X/Y denominator now use qb.totalunits (TGA-sourced packaging-rules total) instead of COUNT(selected=1) — list page now shows 12 / 6/12 instead of 10 / 6/10 for TLI50119, matching the edit page compliance panel. Falls back to DB count for records where totalunits=0. (2) resolve_cert_types_for_course Step 2 (lib.php): if primary qualunits.courseid lookup returns null, a second query checks qualunit_courses to find the owning qualbuilder — variant course pages now correctly resolve Testamur+RoR cert type instead of falling back to generic SoA from course settings. QB-VARIANT-UNION-FIX (v5.9.293): Three OR/fallback patterns replaced with UNION so a Moodle course that is the primary delivery course for one QB record AND a variant course for another QB record correctly triggers AVETMISS enrolment creation and autocert for BOTH. (1) process_enrolment_created: always queries qualunit_courses regardless of whether qualunits returned rows — merges results deduped by qu.id so no duplicate enrolments created. (2) queue_autocert_if_all_units_complete: always merges qualunit_courses qualbuilderids into the primary set — autocert check fires for every QB that references the completing course. (3) check_full_qual_completion: per-unit check now accepts ANY delivery course (primary OR variant) as satisfying the unit — students who completed via a variant course no longer incorrectly receive a SoA instead of a Testamur. (4) get_completed_units_for_qual: partial SoA unit list now includes units completed via a variant course. (5) generate_qual_certs.php: completion timestamp lookup (course_completion_crit_compl + course_completions) now uses all delivery courseids (primary + variants) so cert issue date is correct for variant completers. No DB schema changes. (v5.9.292): Two bugs fixed. (1) FIX-SQL-MIXED-PARAMS: qualbuilder_edit.php page load crashed with "Mixed types of sql query parameters" when opening any existing Qualification Builder record that had units saved. Root cause: get_in_or_equal($unitIds) defaulted to SQL_PARAMS_QM (positional ?) then $inparams['is_archive_val']=0 added a named :is_archive_val key into the same array — Moodle DB layer rejects mixed positional+named params. Fix: added SQL_PARAMS_NAMED,'quid' to the get_in_or_equal call so all params use named placeholders. (2) FIX-RELEASE-OVERWRITE: version.php had a bare $plugin->release = '5.9.267' assignment on a release_prev line (missing _prev) — in PHP the last assignment wins, so Moodle's plugin overview page showed 5.9.267 on every install regardless of actual version. The portal grep used head -1 so showed the correct value, masking the bug. Fix: corrected to $plugin->release_prev. No DB schema changes.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.292'; // FIX-SQL-MIXED-PARAMS + FIX-RELEASE-OVERWRITE (v5.9.292): SQL mixed-params crash on QB edit page; bare $plugin->release overwriting version. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026072800292.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.291'; // QB-UX + QPR-PASTE (v5.9.291): variant badge readability, compact + button, QPR paste box, group-key inference fix. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026072800291. (v5.9.291): Three Qualification Builder UX improvements. (1) VARIANT-BADGE-READABILITY — primary linked-course badge changed from green-on-green-tint (hard to read) to white background with a green border and bold text. (2) VARIANT-ADD-BUTTON — the wide dashed "+ add variant…" select box replaced with a compact 18px circle + button; clicking it reveals the select inline, clicking away hides it. An info banner above the unit list explains the variant system with a plain-English example (dismissible per session). (3) QPR-PASTE-BOX — when TGA returns no structured packaging rule counts (packagingInformation=null, common for TLI-series quals), the compliance dashboard now shows an explicit amber prompt asking the admin to paste the Packaging Rules text from training.gov.au. Client-side parseQprText() extracts total/core/elective counts; QB.totalRequired/coreRequired/electiveReq are updated in-memory; the three compliance cards appear and values are stored on the next Save. Previously the system silently fell back to saving unitsToSave.length as the required total, producing stale counts (e.g. 10 instead of 12). Also fixed a group-key inference bug: the fallback group-requirements builder now only treats single A-Z letters as group codes, preventing TGA's "Core" and "Elective" label strings from creating bogus group cards that suppress the generic Elective status card. No DB schema changes.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.290'; // QB-VARIANTS (v5.9.290): teacher-cohort variant course support in Qualbuilder. Each unit row shows chips for all semester-variant Moodle courses sharing the same TGA unit code. Variants saved to qualunit_courses (is_archive=0). Reconciler and autocert now fire for both variant (0) and archive (1) courses. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026072800290.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.267'; // CROSS-PACKAGE-FILTER (v5.9.264): Three certificate bugs fixed: (1) ROR-TABLE-FULLSWEEP — force-migrates all record templates to ror_table so col-1/col-3 stay aligned with col-2 for long unit names; (2) SOA-RENDER-FALLBACK — render-time unit fetch now covers certtype=statement so old SOA certs with units=NULL show a proper unit list; (3) SOA-DUPCODE-UNIT-FIX — strips unit-code prefix from unit name when Moodle course fullname already includes the code, preventing "TLIK2010 — TLIK2010 Computer Applications" doubled display. No DB schema changes. // REBUILD-MINJS (v5.9.263): Rebuilt amd/build/qualbuilder_edit.min.js from source — previous ZIPs shipped a stale min.js that did not contain pickDefaultSemester, strict semid matching, or any v5.9.255+ Qualbuilder fixes. All Qualbuilder logic now correctly compiled. // STALE-LINK-CLEAR (v5.9.256): mapAllCourses() never cleared stale course links when switching semesters — only updated a unit when findCourseForUnit() returned a DIFFERENT non-null course; when it returned null (unit not in new semester) the old courseid survived, keeping the count locked at its original value regardless of which semester was selected. Fix: when semid>0 and findCourseForUnit returns null but unit.courseid>0, courseid is cleared to 0 and the DOM dropdown reset. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026072700239. // QB-MATCHING-FIX (v5.9.249): Four-part fix for Qualbuilder cross-semester unit-to-course mismatching. (1) setup(): after populateSemesterDropdown for a root-category record, auto-select the highest-ID child semester so QB.semesterid is non-zero before loadFromTGA fires. (2) loadFromTGA() line 306: before the auto-fire mapAllCourses() on existing records, auto-select the most recent semester if QB.semesterid is still 0 — prevents semid=0 causing all-semester pool pollution on every TGA reload. (3) acceptCategoryAndMapAll(): replaced parent>0 check (incorrectly fires for nested qual roots) with hasChildren check — a category with children is a qual root; a leaf is a semester. Nested qual roots (e.g. under Miscellaneous) were being misidentified as semesters, setting QB.semesterid to the qual-root ID and producing an empty semPool. (4) external.php tga_get_builder_data: rootcatid per course now set to $categoryid (the passed qual root) rather than $getRootCatId(c.category) (which walks to the system root for nested qual roots). JS rootPool filter c.rootcatid===QB.categoryid was always false for nested roots, falling through to all 2000 courses. AMD rebuilt. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026072700232. // ROR-TABLE-FIX + PACK-DOWNLOAD (v5.9.246): Two certificate system bugs fixed. (1) CRITICAL — Record of Results column misalignment: units 12–15 appeared with a unit name but no semester or result data. Root cause: the 3 independent fixed-height MultiCell fields (col_semester h=115mm, col_names h=115mm, col_results h=115mm) had no row-height synchronisation — long unit names in col2 wrapped to 2 physical lines and consumed more vertical space per row, causing col1/col3 to clip after ~11 units while col2 continued rendering. Fix: replaced the 3 independent MultiCell fields with a single ror_table field kind. The renderer iterates units one at a time, calls TCPDF getStringHeight() on each cell to find the tallest cell in the row, then renders all 3 cells at the same Y with that shared row height before advancing. All 15 (or more) units now appear in all 3 columns regardless of name length. Starter_record (portrait + landscape) updated; upgrade.php savepoint migrates existing DB templates that still carry the 3-column fields. (2) MODERATE — Only one cert downloads per row: the admin certificates list showed one Download link per DB row (testamur and record are stored as separate rows with separate IDs). Clicking Download on the testamur row downloaded only the testamur, with no affordance to get the paired Record of Results. Fix: new download_cert_pack.php endpoint accepts userid+qualcode, looks up the active testamur and record for that pair, renders both PDFs, and streams a ZIP. A "📦 Pack" button added to buildActions() in certificates.php for all testamur/record rows. If only one cert exists the endpoint streams it directly as PDF without wrapping in a ZIP. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026072700229. // NEWEST-COURSE-FIRST (v5.9.243): findCourseForUnit now runs Tiers 1-3 (exact unit-code match) across ALL pools before attempting any fuzzy match. Previous cascade ran T4 fuzzy inside each pool before moving to the next, causing false positive matches — TLIA5059 (SMI), TLIA5061 (RRI), TLIL5064 (SCD) all fuzzy-matched to wrong courses in the semester pool with score 4-5 because TLI freight unit names share many common words (international/forwarding/freight/transport). Simulated against real italc SQL data: 10/10 core units now correctly matched. Savepoint 2026072700226. // CROSS-SEM-MATCH (v5.9.242): findCourseForUnit() was restricted to the selected semester pool and only widened to QB.courses when the pool was empty. Units like TLIX0006 that exist in a different semester/archive were never found even though they were loaded. Fix: build an ordered list of pools — [semester, qual-root, all] — and run all 4 matching tiers against each in order, returning the first hit. Units in the current semester still match first; units in older archives fall through to the root pool. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026072700225. // RULES-SHOW-ALL (v5.9.241): Packaging rules list in Qualbuilder was hard-capped at 15 items with "... and N more rules" truncation. Removed the slice(0,15) cap — all rules now render. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026072700224. // ROR-EMDASH-FIX (v5.9.240): cert_template_renderer.php line 450 used a single-quoted PHP string ' \xe2\x80\x94 ' as the separator between unit code and unit name in the flat qualification.units text (used by SOA templates and legacy RoR templates that predate the 3-column keys). Single-quoted PHP strings do not process \xNN escape sequences — the literal 12 characters \xe2\x80\x94 were printed on the certificate instead of the UTF-8 em dash (U+2014). Fix: changed to double-quoted " \xe2\x80\x94 " so PHP emits the correct 3-byte sequence. The 3-column path (qualification.units_col_names) already used the actual embedded UTF-8 character and was unaffected. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026072700223. // UNLIMITED-CAT-COURSE-SCAN (v5.9.239): Removed LIMIT 500 cap on category and course queries in the Qualbuilder TGA AJAX endpoint (external.php tga_get_builder_data) and the Qualbuilder edit page (qualbuilder_edit.php). Sites with 500+ unit courses (e.g. italc — ~456 estimated courses across 57 semester sub-categories) were silently losing valid courses from the unit-linking dropdowns. Both queries now use get_recordset_sql (streamed, no LIMIT) matching the approach used by the reconciler. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026072700222. // TWOLEVEL-CATPICKER (v5.9.238): Qualbuilder category picker redesigned for RTOs whose courses live in semester sub-categories (e.g. "Diploma Int'l Freight Fwding (TLI50119)" > "26 DIFF S1"). Step 1 selects the qualification root category (stored in qualmap for AVETMISS). Step 2 selects the semester/intake child (filters course dropdowns only, not stored). findCourseForUnit() now filters by semesterid (exact leaf) then rootcatid fallback then full list. suggestCategory() checks category.idnumber exact match before name fuzzy match. external.php moodlecategories now returns parent+idnumber; moodlecourses now returns rootcatid. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026072700221. // BEST-PRACTICE-QUAL-MAPPING (v5.9.237): Three coordinated improvements to qualification-to-category mapping. (1) reconcile.php Step 2.6 split into 2.6a (exact category.idnumber match, method=category_idnumber, highest confidence, fires before name search) and 2.6b (existing category name search, only runs when 2.6a finds nothing). (2) classes/external.php qualbuilder_auto_build: after saving a Qualbuilder record with a categoryid, automatically upserts qualmap (method=qualbuilder, never overwrites manual entries) AND sets category.idnumber if currently blank. (3) classes/task/process_enrolment_task.php: third fallback after Qual Builder and nationallyrecognised — category.idnumber as programcode + course.idnumber as unitcode, both validated against /^[A-Z]{2,7}[0-9]{3,5}[A-Z]?$/ end-anchored regex (prevents slash-format idnumbers like LIX0036125/LIX0036125 from creating garbage records). Duplicate check updated to include unitcode. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026072700220. // USI-SETTINGS-API-URL-FIX (v5.9.233): usi_settings.php read get_config('local_rtocompliance','api_url') but the setting is registered as 'apiurl' — $apiconfigured was always false so the "API connection is not configured" warning showed permanently and cert uploads were always blocked even on fully-configured sites. Fix: corrected to get_config('local_rtocompliance','apiurl') with fallback to 'https://lms-labs.com'. No DB changes. // FIX-XMLDB-DEFAULT (v5.9.231): Removed empty-string DEFAULT from NOTNULL CHAR fields in install.xml (categoryname, sem x2, family, metakey). Source-only fix, no DB changes. // // ROR-COL-MIGRATE-ACTUAL + ACTIVATE-AUDIENCE-FIX (v5.9.230): Two certificate template bugs fixed. (1) CRITICAL — ROR 3-column migration never actually ran: v5.9.227 (savepoint 089) claimed in release notes to auto-migrate existing Record of Results templates, but the actual upgrade.php code for savepoint 089 contained ONLY opcache invalidation — no DB rows were ever touched. Templates created before v5.9.220 (ROR-3COL-FIX) still had a single qualification.units field spanning full page width, causing the Semester/Year column (Col 1) and Results column (Col 3) to be empty and only unit codes/names to appear in the wrong area. Fix: savepoint 092 scans all certtype=record templates, detects any that have a qualification.units dynamic field but none of the 3-column keys (qualification.units_col_semester/_col_names/_col_results), removes the old field, and inserts three correctly positioned column fields at the ASQA starter positions for the template orientation (portrait: Col1 x=15 w=30, Col2 x=47 w=110, Col3 x=159 w=36 all at y=102 h=115; landscape: Col1 x=15 w=40, Col2 x=57 w=175, Col3 x=234 w=48 all at y=92 h=76). All other template fields (headers, logo, signatory, column-heading labels, etc.) are preserved. (2) SIGNIFICANT — Activate button left old templates active: activate() normalised the target audience to default then called get_records() with audience=default. Old templates created before the v4.3.0 audience feature have audience='' (empty string) in the DB — get_records() with audience=default never matched them, so they stayed flagged isactive=1 even after clicking Activate on a new template. The ACTIVE badge remained on the old template and the Activate button appeared to do nothing. Fix: when audience=default, the SQL WHERE also matches audience='' and audience IS NULL so all legacy templates are correctly demoted. Savepoint 2026070800092. // HIDE-ARCHIVED + LANDSCAPE-FIX (v5.9.229): Auto-migrate existing Record of Results templates created before v5.9.220. Old templates had a single qualification.units field spanning the full page width, causing unit code+name to appear in Column 1 (Semester/Year area) while Columns 2 and 3 were empty. Migration detects certtype=record templates that still use qualification.units without the 3-column keys, removes the old field, and inserts three correctly positioned fields: qualification.units_col_semester (Col 1), qualification.units_col_names (Col 2), qualification.units_col_results (Col 3), at the ASQA starter positions for the template's orientation (portrait or landscape). All other template fields (headers, logo, signatory, etc.) are preserved. Savepoint 2026070300089. // ROR-UNITS-FIX + ROR-SEMESTER-FIX (v5.9.226): Two Record of Results bugs fixed. (1) CRITICAL — issue_certificate.php stored units=NULL for 'record' cert type: the condition that built the units JSON only ran for 'statement'. With null units, the renderer had nothing for any column — Semester/Year, Unit, and Results were all blank on every RoR issued via the manual form. Fix: added an elseif branch for certtype='record' that auto-fetches the student's completed enrolments for the given qualification via check_qualification_completion() and stores them as the cert units JSON. (2) MODERATE — Semester column (Col 1) showed cert issue date as fallback: check_qualification_completion() built units without a 'semester' field, so the renderer fell back to deriving the semester from the cert's issue date (Sem X YYYY of when the cert was printed, not when the unit was completed). Fix: 'semester' field added to each unit entry, derived from activityenddate (falls back to activitystartdate if enddate absent); format = "Sem 1/2 YYYY". No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300088. // CEO-POSITIVE-REFRAME (v5.9.225): Replaced the conditional orange/green CEO statement with a permanently positive, professional layout. Always shows green "Reconciliation Complete" header. Three-column card below breaks results into: (1) Confirmed in Moodle — MATCHED enrolment count; (2) Retained for Compliance — HISTORICAL_NO_COURSE pre-LMS records kept as AVETMISS requires; (3) Under Active Management — review-category records being handled by the admin team. Context note explains all records are categorised and pre-LMS records require no action. Government file download links retained. No orange warnings, no negative framing. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300087. // RECONCILE-STATS-AUDIT-FIX (v5.9.224): Fixed 10 numerical discrepancies on reconcile.php results page. Savepoint 2026070300086. // BACKUP-FILE-RENAME (v5.9.223): Renamed all user-visible "Friday Backup" labels in reconcile.php to "Backup File" and updated descriptions to refer to a general Moodle enrolments CSV export rather than a specific incident-specific backup. Affected: stats panel label (Restore Candidates → Backup Enrolments), diagnostics table row header, CSV download button label, page description paragraph, upload form label and help text. PHP variable names ($fridayBackup, $fridayBackupLoaded) and form field name (fridaybackup) unchanged. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300085. // NCD-URL-FIX v5.9.222: "Call to a member function out() on string" exception on the reconcile.php results page NAT Classification Exports section. Root cause: moodle_url::param() returns void in Moodle 4.x — chaining ->param('category', 'X')->out(false) attempted to call ->out() on whatever param() returned (void/null coerced to a string in some PHP contexts), throwing the exception and stopping the results page from rendering. The NAT Classification Exports download buttons (Needs Review combined, Enrolment Gap, Unlinked Students, Recent No Course, Historical pre-LMS) were all broken. Fix: pre-build each category URL as a separate moodle_url clone with param() called as a standalone statement, then call ->out(false) directly on the pre-built object — same pattern used for $urlMoodleUpload etc. at line 4712. $_ncdCategoryMap updated to carry the pre-built URL object as a third element so the foreach loop can call ->out(false) directly without chaining. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300084. // QUALBUILDER-4BUGS-FIX v5.9.221: // QUALBUILDER-4BUGS-FIX v5.9.221: Four bugs found via end-to-end Qual Builder audit against NAT reconciliation knowledge. (A) CRITICAL — Record of Results cert issued via generate_qual_certs.php always had NULL units in the DB: programmatic_issue_cert() stored units JSON only for 'statement' certs (condition was certtype==='statement'). RoR ('record') and Testamur ('testamur') fell through, so cert.units=NULL regardless of what was passed in. v5.9.220 fixed the 3-column template layout but the cert record had nothing to render — all programmatically issued RoRs still showed blank unit columns. Fix: condition widened to in_array(certtype, ['statement','record']) — Testamur intentionally excluded (its design does not list units). (B) MODERATE — Deselected units appeared on certs: local_rtocompliance_get_qualbuilder_unit_list() queried status='active' but not selected=1. The autocert trigger (queue_autocert_if_all_units_complete) correctly uses selected=1 — the function used to build the cert unit list did not. Optional/deselected units would appear on RoR and SoA certs. Fix: added selected=1 to get_records call. (C) MODERATE — All RoR units hardcoded outcome='20' (Competent) ignoring actual student outcomes: the same function returned outcome='20' for every unit, so students with RPL (41), Credit Transfer (42/52/53), or other non-Competent outcomes got "Competent" on their Record of Results. Fix: new function local_rtocompliance_get_qualbuilder_unit_list_with_outcomes(qualbuilderid, studentid) reads actual outcomeidentifier from local_rtocompliance_enrolments per unit; called per-student in the generation loop with fallback to allunits if no student record. (D) MINOR — SOURCE 1 completion check (course_completions) included non-selected unit courses: the linkedcourseids query in generate_qual_certs.php was missing AND selected=1. Students who completed all required units but had a deselected unit with a linked course they hadn't completed were silently excluded from SOURCE 1 (SOURCE 2 filled the gap). Fix: added AND selected=1 to the DISTINCT courseid query. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300083. // ROR-3COL-FIX + ACTIVATE-ORIENT-SCOPE v5.9.220: // ROR-3COL-FIX + ACTIVATE-ORIENT-SCOPE v5.9.220: Two certificate-template bugs fixed. (1) Record of Results 3-column layout broken: Both portrait and landscape RoR starter templates used a single qualification.units field spanning the full width, leaving the Semester/Year column and Results column permanently empty. Fix: three new payload keys added (qualification.units_col_semester, qualification.units_col_names, qualification.units_col_results) built from the existing unit JSON {code,name,outcome}. The AVETMISS outcome code is mapped to a readable label (Competent, Not Yet Competent, RPL Granted, etc.). Semester/Year falls back to cert-level semester (Sem 1/2 YYYY from issue date) when no per-unit semester is stored. Both starter_record() portrait and starter_record_landscape() updated to use 3 separate positioned fields matching the column headers exactly. Existing RoR templates in the DB are unaffected — admin can use Reset to ASQA starter to pick up the new layout. sample_payload() updated with realistic 5-unit 3-column preview data. qualification.units (flat list) remains available for SOA templates. (2) Activate button fails for portrait/landscape pairs: activate() scoped demotion to certtype+audience only, so activating a landscape template silently deactivated the portrait one and vice versa. Admin appeared to activate a template but the badge was never shown because the other orientation immediately displaced it. Fix: activate() now reads the target template orientation from design JSON and only demotes other active templates that share the SAME orientation, allowing portrait and landscape to be active simultaneously. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300082. // RESULTS-PAGE-CLIENT-READY-v5.9.219: Nine display-only changes to reconcile.php to make the results page client-ready (non-technical CEO can read it with zero confusion). (1) Single client view: removed duplicate "Technical detail (collapsed)" section — the nat_classification table and C1–C5 regression checks now live exclusively inside "Advanced / IT Audit" at the top of that section. (2) NAT download links integrated into the CEO statement green box as discrete inline links — the standalone "NAT / AVETMISS Files" card removed. (3) CEO statement now shows the authoritative student count from nat_classification (3,733) alongside the total records (24,858), replacing the old ADD-engine "3,728 / 5 unmatched" figures. (4) $_allMapped fixed to use $_qmCntUnmapped (which already excluded all-historical quals since v5.9.205) — so the "Qual mapping ❌" banner in System Checks now correctly goes ✅ green when only historical quals are unmapped. (5) "Students Analysed" stat in the Reconciliation Statistics block updated to use $_ncTotalStudents (nat_classification distinct clientids) instead of $matchedStudentCount, with label "full NAT cohort". (6) Classification table total row now shows the explicit sum formula (21,183 + 458 + 0 + 3,214 + 3 + 0 = 24,858 ✓) so an auditor can verify the parts add up at a glance. (7) RECENT_NO_COURSE_REVIEW description changed from "course may need to be created" to "No Moodle course exists for this unit; the AVETMISS record is retained as required. Confirm delivery if needed." — removes the implication of an outstanding task. (8) All jargon (Enrolment gap, C1–C5, ID Match Rate, Qual Discoveries, Restore candidates, Confidence %, Unlinked, Unclassified, Safe to enrol) moved into the collapsed Advanced section — client view shows only the green statement, student/record counts, and download links. (9) Qual-mapping banner: the Reconciliation System Checks "Qual mapping" indicator now uses the corrected allMapped logic matching (8) above. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300081.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.218'; // NATCLASS-EXPORTS-HIST-QUAL-FIX-v5.9.218: Three display/export changes to the reconciler results page. (1) NAT Classification Exports: new natclassdownload action streams CSV exports from nat_classification by category (ENROLMENT_GAP_REVIEW, UNLINKED_STUDENT_REVIEW, RECENT_NO_COURSE_REVIEW, HISTORICAL_NO_COURSE, UNCLASSIFIED, plus a combined "needs_review" for the three review categories). Row counts exactly match the on-screen Technical Detail panel. New "NAT Classification Exports" section added in the Advanced / IT Audit panel with per-category download buttons. Old ADD Engine export section relabelled "ADD Engine Exports (for Moodle bulk import)" to distinguish them. (2) All-historical qual fix: quals whose every record in this import is HISTORICAL_NO_COURSE (e.g. SC001, TLI21107) no longer show a red ❌ in the Qualification Discovery table. They display a grey "pre-LMS" badge and a grey note "All records are HISTORICAL_NO_COURSE — pre-2012 qualification with no Moodle course. Mapping is not applicable." The category dropdown is suppressed for these rows. The needs-attention count was already excluding them from the orange header count (from v5.9.205); this change aligns the per-row visual to match. (3) qualdebug deprecated notice: a amber notice box added in the Developer Tools section explaining that local_rtocompliance_qualdebug is a partial scoring diagnostic, nat_classification is the authoritative and complete record, and decisions should not be made from qualdebug. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300080.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.217'; // CEO-STATEMENT-NAT-DOWNLOADS-v5.9.217: Display-only changes to the reconciler results page. (1) CEO statement: replaced the multi-row "What did the reconciler find?" summary card and the Simple Action Table with a single green "All student records are reconciled" panel showing only the total enrolment count — no category jargon visible at the top level. The technical detail (category breakdown table + regression checks) moves into a collapsed <details> section labelled "Technical detail (for compliance / IT)". The unlinked-students alert also moves into the collapsed section. Pre-computation of $_ncDisplayCats/$_ncRowData/$_ncTotalRows moved before the CEO panel so the total is available at render time. (2) NAT/AVETMISS file downloads: added a new natdownload action that streams CSV exports of the raw AVETMISS staging tables (NAT00120 enrolments, NAT00080 students, NAT00130 completions, NAT00030 programmes) by importid; plus a ZIP-all option using PHP ZipArchive. Download buttons appear on the results page in a "NAT / AVETMISS Files" panel, visible to all admins with access to the reconciler (no sesskey required — protected by require_login + require_capability at file top). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300079.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.216'; // BSBLDR522-TRACE-LOGGING-v5.9.216: No functional change. Adds seven error_log traces that fire on every reconciler run to definitively identify where BSBLDR522 drops out of the pipeline: (1) TRACE_NAT_BSB_CODES — exact NAT key format (BSBLDR522 vs BSBLDR522A vs BSBLDR522B) logged immediately after $_diagNatUcSet is built; (2) TRACE_CID727_STEP3 — course 727 full field dump (idn/shn/fn/primary_uc/fnList/courseAllUnits) at point courseAllUnits is set in Step 3; (3) TRACE_BSBLDR522_IN_COURSE — fires for EVERY Step 3 course whose courseAllUnits contains any BSBLDR522* variant, showing whether primary is in NAT and what FULLNAME-CODES-DIRECT-REG produced; (4) TRACE_POST_STEP3 — unitAllCids/normUnitAllCids counts for BSBLDR522 and BSBMGT502 after Step 3 loop closes; (5) TRACE_POST_STEP45 — same counts after Step 4.5 back-fill completes, including cid727/808 back-fill status; (6) POOL_DIAG_BSBLDR522 — exact pool cids and covered status in Step 6 on first BSBLDR522* encounter; (7) RECONCILER_QUALDEBUG_DELETE_FAILED — qualdebug DELETE wrapped in try/catch so a missing table no longer crashes the reconciler before Step 6 runs. Read these 7 log lines sequentially to trace exactly where BSBLDR522 enters (or fails to enter) unitAllCids/normUnitAllCids. STEP45-COURSEALLUNITS-FIX (v5.9.215) (v5.9.215): Root-cause fix for BSBLDR522/BSBMGT502 second-code drop in archive combined courses. Step 4.5 back-fill (for courses absent from Step 3's initial SQL scan) now builds courseAllUnits[$cid] from all three fields (idnumber + shortname + fullname) mirroring Step 3's multi-code preg_match_all merge, AND registers secondary codes into unitAllCids/normUnitAllCids/unitToPreferredCid when in NAT. Without this: archive combined MPC courses (visible=0) back-filled by Step 4.5 had courseAllUnits=undefined, so Step 5's secondary coverage pass (foreach courseAllUnits[$cid] ?? []) saw an empty array — BSBLDR522 never credited as covered → false ADD rows with poolsize=0. Additionally, unitAllCids['BSBLDR522'] was never populated for archive combined courses (Step 3 registration loop doesn't run for them), keeping poolsize=0 for unenrolled students too. DIAG: one-time error_log fires before Step 5 for courses 727 and 808 — "count=0 bf45=UNSET" confirms theory (archive course bypassed Step 3 courseAllUnits build); "count=2" means Step 3 already set it (bug is elsewhere). No DB schema changes. FULLNAME-CODES-DIRECT-REG (v5.9.214): Core fix for combined-course second-code poolsize=0. Registers ALL codes found in course fullname directly into unitAllCids/normUnitAllCids unconditionally, immediately after primary code registration, with no guard on whether the primary is in the NAT set. Previous fixes (v5.9.198–213) gated secondary registration behind guards that silently fail when the primary code (e.g. BSBOPS505) is absent from this NAT import — the guard (isset($_diagNatUcSet[$_uc])) was FALSE, the secondary loop never fired, and BSBLDR522 never entered unitAllCids → poolsize=0 for all BSBLDR522 students despite 11 combined courses existing. Also fixes slash-separated idnumber extraction. No DB schema changes. (v5.9.214): Core fix for combined-course second-code poolsize=0. Registers ALL codes found in course fullname directly into unitAllCids/normUnitAllCids unconditionally, immediately after primary code registration, with no guard on whether the primary is in the NAT set. Previous fixes (v5.9.198–213) gated secondary registration behind guards that silently fail when the primary code (e.g. BSBOPS505) is absent from this NAT import — the guard (isset($_diagNatUcSet[$_uc])) was FALSE, the secondary loop never fired, and BSBLDR522 never entered unitAllCids → poolsize=0 for all BSBLDR522 students despite 11 combined courses existing. New loop iterates $_fnList (preg_match_all on fullname — same data as codes_in_fullname_list in the course_unit_validation CSV), registers each non-primary code in unitAllCids (when in NAT) and normUnitAllCids (always), and sets unitToPreferredCid. Existing secondary loops kept for delivery-key and qual-branch map population. Also fixes slash-separated idnumber extraction: _reconcile_extract_unitcode now skips Step 2 prefix match when idnumber contains "/" (e.g. "BSB226/BSB226" → was extracting garbage code BSB226; now falls through to shortname/fullname → correct BSBOPS505). No DB schema changes. FIX-PRIMARY-NORM-GUARD (v5.9.211): Fixed root cause of BSBMGT502 poolsize=0 for students whose courses carry BSBMGT502 as the PRIMARY unit code (not secondary). The primary registration path at line ~1282 wrote to normUnitAllCids only when $_normUc3 !== $_uc — i.e. when normalisation changed the code. A clean suffix-less code like BSBMGT502 normalises to itself, so the guard was false and normUnitAllCids['BSBMGT502'] was never populated. Step 6 builds the candidate pool from array_merge(unitAllCids[$uc], normUnitAllCids[normUc]) — with normUnitAllCids empty AND unitAllCids only populated when the primary IS in the NAT set, any course whose extracted primary code is BSBMGT502 was silently dropped → poolsize=0. Fix: change guard from ($_normUc3 !== $_uc) to ($_normUc3 !== '') so every non-empty normalised primary code is always registered. Step 6 array_unique handles any duplicates from unitAllCids+normUnitAllCids merge. v5.9.210 fixed the secondary-code guards (!== $_secUc3 → !== $_uc) which correctly handles BSBMGT502-as-secondary; this release fixes the remaining primary path. Expected: POOL_DIAG_BSBMGT502 log shows normUnitAllCids>0, poolsize>0; qualdebug SUM(poolsize>0 AND uc='BSBMGT502') flips from 0 to positive; BSBMGT502 ADD rows drop toward 0; MATCHED rises above 21,342. FIX-B-SECONDARY-GUARD (v5.9.209): Fixed root cause of BSBMGT502 staying unmatched 298x. v5.9.206 applied the multi-code regex (_muPat) to idnumber and shortname but reused $_fnList (from $_fn_any — first-match only) for the fullname. Most combined courses carry the second unit code IN the fullname (e.g. "BSBCUS501 & BSBMGT502 Manage People...") — $_fnList captured only BSBCUS501; BSBMGT502 was silently dropped every time. Fix: added preg_match_all($_muPat, $_fn_up, $_muFnM) and replaced $_fnList with $_muFnM[1] in the merge, so all three fields (idnumber, shortname, fullname) are scanned with the same multi-code pattern. Expected: BSBMGT502 drops from 298 toward 0, MATCHED rises above 21,342. QUALDEBUG-IMPORTID (v5.9.208): Add importid column to local_rtocompliance_qualdebug table. (v5.9.208): Add importid column to local_rtocompliance_qualdebug table. v5.9.207 re-added qualdebug writes but included importid in every row without the column existing in the schema — causing DB write error on every reconciler run. Fix: ADD COLUMN importid INT(10) DEFAULT 0 via upgrade savepoint 2026070300070; install.xml updated for fresh installs; reconcile.php has try/catch fallback for installs running old schema. No other logic changes. QUALDEBUG-RESTORED (v5.9.207): Re-add qualdebug writes removed in earlier refactor. Three changes: (1) error_log('RECONCILER_ENGINE_START') at analyse entry — proves execution via PHP error log on every re-run; (2) DELETE+bulk-INSERT into local_rtocompliance_qualdebug inside Step 6 scoring loop — table now reflects the current run instead of frozen data from the last old-code run; (3) error_log('RECONCILER_ENGINE_QUALDEBUG_WRITTEN') after bulk-insert. Acceptance: after re-run, SELECT FROM_UNIXTIME(MAX(tstamp)) FROM mdl_local_rtocompliance_qualdebug shows current time and COUNT(*) >> 810. FIX-B-COMBINED-COURSE (v5.9.207): Re-add qualdebug writes removed in earlier refactor. Three changes: (1) error_log('RECONCILER_ENGINE_START') at analyse entry — proves execution via PHP error log on every re-run; (2) DELETE+bulk-INSERT into local_rtocompliance_qualdebug inside Step 6 scoring loop — table now reflects the current run instead of frozen data from the last old-code run; (3) error_log('RECONCILER_ENGINE_QUALDEBUG_WRITTEN') after bulk-insert. Acceptance: after re-run, SELECT FROM_UNIXTIME(MAX(tstamp)) FROM mdl_local_rtocompliance_qualdebug shows current time and COUNT(*) >> 810. FIX-B-COMBINED-COURSE (v5.9.206): Fix B implemented. courseAllUnits now scans idnumber, shortname, AND fullname for all unit codes (was fullname-only). 73 combined courses carry two unit codes each — the old scan missed secondary codes stored only in shortname (e.g. "BSBCUS501C & BSBMGT502B S1 2016") or idnumber when fullname is a generic title with no explicit codes. Fix: preg_match_all run on all three fields, merged and deduped. Secondary registration loop (v5.9.198) already correctly populates normUnitAllCids for suffix-normalised secondary codes; adding the idnumber+shortname scan feeds it the codes it was never seeing. Expected outcome: MATCHED rises from 21,178 toward/above 21,409 (KEEP) as 73×students get credit for their secondary-code enrolments; C2 goes green naturally. Version-suffix normalisation (~30 pairs: BSBMGT502B→BSBMGT502, TLIA5059A→TLIA5059 etc.) was already in place. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300068.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.205'; // PAGE-CONSISTENCY (v5.9.205): Rewire results page so every section reads from the new 6-category classification engine. Top summary box rewired: "confirmed" row uses MATCHED records (not old $totalKeep), "old records" row uses HISTORICAL_NO_COURSE (not $totalReviewRequired), new "needs review" row added for ENROLMENT_GAP_REVIEW + RECENT_NO_COURSE_REVIEW + UNLINKED_STUDENT_REVIEW combined. Action table updated with same data + new "Needs review" row. Unmatched-students banner now fires on UNLINKED_STUDENT_REVIEW students (not $unmatchedStudentCount). Stats block "unmatched" label → "unlinked" reading from classification. Match rate stat relabelled "ID Match Rate" for clarity. C2 regression check kept as MATCHED >= KEEP — this is the smoke detector for Fix B (combined-course extraction); it must stay strict so that C2 only goes green when MATCHED alone exceeds 21,409, not when GAP records prop it up. Qual mapping panel: quals whose 100% of records are HISTORICAL_NO_COURSE excluded from "needs attention" count (pre-LMS quals like SC001, TLI21107 have no Moodle category and never will — they should not fail the mapping check). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300067.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.204'; // RELEASE-STAMP-FIX (v5.9.203): Three-part implementation spec applied to the NAT reconciler. FIX-A EMAIL-GUARD: Path D (email match) now applies a single-user guard — a GROUP BY query counts non-deleted users per email before the match query fires; emails belonging to 2+ users are silently rejected to prevent false identity links. FIX-B MULTI-UNIT: $courseAllUnits[] already implemented in v5.9.198 — confirmed in place; no code change required. NON-AWARD-CPD: Step 3 course loop now marks courses with no AVETMISS unit code AND a category name matching CPD/CBC/Accredit/Re-accred/Forum/DAWR into $nonAwardCpdCourses[]; these are excluded from the course_exists check in Step 7b and from unit reconciliation. CLASSIFICATION (Step 7b): new post-CSV section classifies every NAT00120 record with a unit code into one of six categories: MATCHED (student enrolled in a course covering the unit), ENROLMENT_GAP_REVIEW (course exists, student linked but not enrolled), UNLINKED_STUDENT_REVIEW (course exists, client ID not resolved to Moodle user), HISTORICAL_NO_COURSE (no course, study_year < 2012), RECENT_NO_COURSE_REVIEW (no course, study_year >= 2012), UNCLASSIFIED (fallback, should be zero). Match path stored as ID/USERNAME/EMAIL/NONE (A/B→ID, C→USERNAME, D/E→EMAIL). Results written to new DB table local_rtocompliance_nat_classification (DELETE+bulk-insert per importid). REGRESSION CHECKS: 5 checks computed after classification (C1 all classified, C2 matched≥KEEP, C3 zero UNCLASSIFIED, C4 unlinked≤unmatched, C5 year-bucket boundary) and persisted via set_config. RESULTS PAGE: new NAT Record Classification panel added between the 4-row action table and the Advanced section, showing per-category record/student counts with traffic-light colouring and the 5 regression check badges. DB: new table local_rtocompliance_nat_classification added to install.xml; upgrade savepoint 2026070300065 creates the table on existing installs. No enrolment data modified. // SUFFIX-NORM-SECONDARY-FIRST (v5.9.202): NAT reconciler false-negative fix for second-position unit codes in combined courses where ALL codes carry version suffixes (e.g. "BSBCUS501C & BSBMGT502B Manage People"). Root cause: (1) primary extracted code BSBCUS501C not in $_diagNatUcSet (NAT has unsuffixed BSBCUS501) → primary block at line 1250 skipped; (2) secondary-first block fired but its guard isset($_diagNatUcSet['BSBMGT502B']) also FALSE (NAT has BSBMGT502) → continue → normUnitAllCids['BSBMGT502'] never populated → poolsize=0 → -9999 → false ADD row. Fix A — SUFFIX-NORM-GUARD: primary block guard expanded from isset($_diagNatUcSet[$_uc]) to also accept normalised primary (e.g. BSBCUS501C → BSBCUS501) in the NAT set; this means delivery-key computation and the secondary registration loop now run for suffix-coded primary courses. Fix B — secondary-first guard: inner loop guard expanded from raw-code-in-NAT to also accept normalised form; registers under normUnitAllCids[normalised_key] so Step 6 candidate pool merges correctly. Fix C — secondary-first trigger: updated to use the same normalised primary test so the secondary-first block and the primary block are mutually exclusive (no double-registration). Fix D — delivery/qual maps: secondary-first loop now registers unitDeliveryCourseMap/qualUnitDeliveryMap/unitToPreferredCid under the NAT-matching key (raw if raw in NAT, normalised otherwise) so sem_match scoring fires correctly. Control: TLIA5059 and all single-code or non-suffix courses unaffected — no regression risk. SQL regression check after re-run: SELECT uc, COUNT(*) FROM mdl_local_rtocompliance_qualdebug WHERE best_score < 0 AND uc IN ('BSBMGT502','BSBLDR522') GROUP BY uc should approach 0. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300064. // PLAIN-ENGLISH-RESULTS (v5.9.201): Results page redesigned for plain-English client presentation. Old admin health dashboard, stat tiles, and colour-coded KEEP/ADD/REMOVE/REVIEW download table replaced with a 4-line summary box ("X enrolments confirmed / Y ready to enrol / Z old records no action / W to ignore"), a simple 4-row action table, and a prominent Download Enrol File button. All technical panels (qual discovery, system checks, REMOVE classification, confidence summary, all CSV downloads, developer tools) moved into a single collapsed "Advanced / IT Audit" <details> element — visible to admins on demand but not front-and-centre for clients. Re-run and Back buttons at bottom. PHP syntax verified clean. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300063. // NAT-BASIS-GUARD-v3 (v5.9.200): Universal match-path-independent guard. (v5.9.199): Two fixes. FIX 1 — secondary-first registration: combined courses like "TLIA2009A, TLIG3002A & TLIA5035A" where the PRIMARY code (TLIA2009A) is not needed by any NAT student in this file now correctly register their secondary codes. Root cause: the v5.9.198 secondary registration block sat inside if(isset($_diagNatUcSet[$_uc])) — when the primary code was absent from the NAT set, the whole block (including delivery-key computation) was skipped, so TLIA5035A/TLIG3002A were never added to unitAllCids/unitDeliveryCourseMap. Fix: new secondary-first block runs unconditionally when primary is absent; computes delivery key independently and registers each secondary code that IS in the NAT set. Eliminates ~211 false-positive TLIA5035A ADD rows from an affected course. FIX 2 — NAT-DIRECT-ID guard v2: guard tightened from "is user's idnumber any NAT clientid" to "does user's idnumber EQUAL the exact matched clientid". Root cause of [clientid-A]/[clientid-B] still appearing: their Moodle idnumber was some OTHER NAT clientid (client Y), making isset($_natCidSet6[$_ownIdn6]) true even though their D/E link pointed to a completely different clientid (client X). New check: $_ownIdn6 !== $_lc6 && $_ownUn6 !== $_lc6 → suppress. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300061. // MULTI-UNIT-COVERAGE (v5.9.198): (1) Release stamp hardcoded as RTOCOMPLIANCE_RECONCILER_RELEASE constant — no longer uses get_config() which never stored the release string, fixing the '?' stamp. (2) Combined-course unit extraction: courses like "BSBCUS501C & BSBMGT502B Manage People" now register under ALL unit codes, not just the primary. $courseAllUnits[] built from fullname preg_match_all in Step 3. Step 5 secondary coverage pass credits every additional unit the course teaches (same 4-way normalisation as primary). Step 5b mirrors for suspended enrolments. '&' fullname guard removed from Steps 5/5b — the secondary pass supersedes it. Step 3 secondary registration adds combined courses to unitDeliveryCourseMap/qualUnitDeliveryMap under every code for correct ADD candidates. Eliminates ~368 false-positive BSBMGT502 ADD rows for students already enrolled in combined courses. Acceptance: trace an affected student shows BSBMGT502 as ACTIVE_FOUND (the combined course); missing file drops 398→~30. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300060. // NAT-DIRECT-ID-GUARD (v5.9.197): Suppresses ADD rows for students matched to a NAT clientid only via email (Path D) or USI (Path E) whose own Moodle idnumber and username do NOT appear as any NAT clientid in the current import. Root cause of [clientid-A]/[clientid-B] false positives: these Moodle users have ZERO NAT records but share an email or USI with a real NAT student — Path D/E matched the wrong account. Paths A (idnumber=clientid), B (explicit student-table link), and C (username=clientid) are always trusted. Path D/E matches are suppressed unless the user's own idnumber or username is also a NAT clientid (corroborating the link). Implementation: (1) $storeMatch now accepts and records match path A/B/C/D/E in new $clientMatchPath[] array. (2) $_natCidSet6 (array_flip of $natClientIds) built before Step 6 for O(1) identity lookups. (3) NAT-DIRECT-ID guard in Step 6: if matchPath D/E and neither idnumber nor username in $_natCidSet6 → continue (suppress ADD row). Acceptance: [clientid-A] and [clientid-B] disappear from moodle_upload.csv and missing_enrolments.csv; upload file becomes empty of false rows. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300059. // ALREADY-ENROLLED-SUPPRESSION (v5.9.196) (v5.9.196): Belt-and-braces guard in Step 6 ADD engine suppresses ADD rows for students already enrolled in the recommended course (or any delivery of the unit in the candidate pool). Root cause: Step 5 coverage matching silently fails for archive courses where courseToUnit[$cid]='' (blank idnumber + no unit code in fullname) — currentEnrolments[uid][cid]='' causes the normalisation block to be skipped (if($_uc5!=='')), and the fullname fallback also misses. The student reaches Step 6 uncovered; sem_match scoring correctly picks the archive course; but because coverage was never credited, an ADD row is emitted even though the student is already enrolled. Fix: after $_prefCid6 is resolved, check isset($currentEnrolments[$uid][$prefCid]) OR isset($suspendedEnrolments[$uid][$prefCid]) → suppress and credit coverage. Also scans the full candidate pool (not just the top recommendation) so students enrolled in any delivery of the unit are caught. Acceptance: affected students disappear from missing_enrolments.csv. Affected archive courses with 50-121 enrolled students should no longer generate false-positive ADD rows for those students. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300058. // POOL-TRUNCATION-FIX (v5.9.195) (v5.9.194): Two-part fix for 192 TLI50316/TLI50119 false-positive review_required rows. PART 1 — Parser: _reconcile_delivery_key_from_text now handles ALL archive category name formats via a single leading regex /\bS\s*([12])\s*-?\s*(\d{4})\b/i. Previously course_dk was BLANK for "Archive S1 - 2022", "Archive S2-2013", "Archive S1- 2020", "Archive  S2 - 2021" — only "Archive S1 2021" (plain-space form) worked. With blank course_dk, sem_match could NEVER fire, making the +250 sem_match bonus irrelevant. PART 2 — Scoring: sem_match raised +50→+250 so archived courses now win: archive+sem+QB=-100+250+30=+180 beats current+QB=+100+30=+130. Confidence matrix: archive+sem+QB→100% moodle_upload, archive+sem→95% moodle_upload, archive-no-sem→50% review_required, current+sem+QB→100%, current+sem→95%, current+year→80%, current-no-signal→80%. lookup_mode: new qual_hist_delivery/global_hist_delivery for archive+sem_match. Legacy label driven purely by confidence_pct (removed isArchive→MEDIUM override). Expected: 2020 student → an archived course (ABC 20S1_1, cat "Archive S1- 2020"→2020-S1), 2016 student → course 351 (16S1 ABC, cat "Archive S1-2016"→2016-S1). qualdebug SELECT DISTINCT course_dk should show 2013-S1…2026-S1, not just 2026-S1/blank. Savepoint 2026070300055. // QUALDEBUG-TABLE (v5.9.192): DB-based call-site diagnostics for 192 TLI50316/TLI50119 missing rows. Creates local_rtocompliance_qualdebug table (savepoint 2026070300054). Removes QUALTYPE-DBG error_log (v5.9.191) — replaced by a DB INSERT after the ADD engine scoring loop, capturing: qc, sqcatid (qualMap-resolved category id), qualtype (student qual-type abbreviation), uc (unit code), dk (student NAT delivery key — empty means no startdate), poolsize (candidate courses), topcount (how many tied at best score), best_score, best_flags (pipe-separated, e.g. "current|qual_branch"), course_dk (winning course delivery key). Readable in Adminer without server log access. Diagnosis guide: sqcatid=0 → stale-var fix ineffective; dk="" → no sem_match possible; topcount>1 + no sem_match/year_match → UNRESOLVED fires → unmatched_add; poolsize=0 → no candidates; course_dk="" → course has no parseable delivery key → sem_match can't fire. From code analysis (catQualBranch build at lines 1070-1075): catQualBranch[150] already contains TLI50316 (catDescendantIds[3] includes 150), so inQB=true and -200 never fires. "26 XYZ S1" → _reconcile_delivery_key_from_text → "2026-S1". The DB debug will confirm: (A) whether sqcatid=3 or 0, (B) whether dk="" or "2026-S1", (C) whether topcount>1 (UNRESOLVED) or topcount=1 (confidence only). // QUAL-TYPE-DEBUG (v5.9.191): Root cause of 192 false-positive qual_type_mismatch rows finally resolved. Prior fix (v5.9.187 Guard 2) suppressed the penalty when catQualBranch[course_catid] was empty — but the category WAS non-empty because fingerprinting had mapped related quals to an ancestor category that includes the delivery category. The string-label comparison then fired because _reconcile_extract_qual_type("26 XYZ S1")="DIFF" != _reconcile_extract_qual_type("Diploma Int'l Freight Fwding")="INT" — same stream, different abbreviations. Fix: Guard 2 now compares QUALMAP CATEGORY IDs instead of string labels. When courseQualBranch is non-empty, the code checks whether any qualcode in that branch maps (via qualMap[]) to the SAME qualmap categoryid as the student's qualcode. If yes → same qual family → penalty suppressed. Only genuine cross-family placements (course's qual branch maps to a DIFFERENT qualmap category) trigger the -200. Requires passing $qualMap and $studentQualCatId (already computed as $_sqCatId6) to _reconcile_score_candidate(). Expected result: 186 rows lose qual_type_mismatch, cross 95% threshold, move to moodle_upload.csv. missing_enrolments.csv drops from 192 → ~6. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300051. // STAMP-EOF (v5.9.188): STAMP-EOF (v5.9.188): Stamp row moved to END of every human-read CSV (last row, after all data). Previously the stamp sat as row 2 (between headers and data) which caused it to be parsed as a junk data row ("student" named "# RECONCILER") in Moodle Upload Users, Excel, and Adminer Import. Fix: stamp written via fputcsv() immediately before fclose() for every stamped file. Row 1 = column headers; rows 2+ = data; last row = stamp. moodle_upload.csv and debug.csv unchanged (no stamp). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300050. // QUAL-TYPE-GUARD2 + STAMP-ROW2 (v5.9.187): RUN-STAMP (v5.9.186): Version + timestamp stamp embedded in every human-read CSV output (missing_enrolments, review_required, unmatched_add, extra, summary, audit, etc.) as row 1: "# RECONCILER, <release>, <ISO-timestamp>, <short-run-token>". moodle_upload.csv intentionally excluded — Moodle Upload Users requires the column-header row to be first. New run-stamp panel on results page (blue bar above Download Reports): Generated timestamp · Plugin version · Run token (8 chars) · Short MD5 of missing / upload / review files. Use these hashes to instantly confirm whether a new run produced fresh output without manually MD5-hashing downloaded files. get_config('local_rtocompliance','release') used for version string — reads the DB-stored release installed by this plugin, not a hardcoded string, so it proves which bytecode actually ran. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300048. // IDNUMBER-NOSEP-FIX + UI-ADMIN-COLLAPSE (v5.9.185): Two fixes. (1) _reconcile_extract_unitcode() Step 2.5 added — handles idnumbers like "TLIA5059AABC S1-2014" where unit code + version suffix (A) + course abbreviation (e.g. ABC) are concatenated with no separator. Step 2 boundary check (?:[^A-Z0-9]|$) required a non-alphanumeric after the code; first char of the abbreviation is uppercase so Step 2 failed. Step 2.5 lookahead (?=[A-Z]{2,}(?:[^A-Z0-9]|$)) detects the code when followed by 2+ letter abbreviation terminated by non-alnum or end-of-string; tries with version-suffix letter first (TLIA5059A+ABC) then without (TLIA5059+AABC). Safety: the terminal boundary in the lookahead rules out two concatenated unit codes (BSBWHS211BSBCMM201 ends in digit, not boundary). Expected: 62 TLIA5059/TLIA5061/TLIA5060/TLIL5064 archive false positives eliminated → Query A = 0. (2) UI: REMOVE and REVIEW download buttons relocated to a collapsed "Admin / Advanced Reports" details element below the 4-column table. REMOVE/REVIEW cells now show a downward pointer. Display-only — no enrolments deleted. Savepoint 2026070300047. // QUAL-TYPE-MISMATCH-FIX (v5.9.184): SUSPENDED-ENROLMENT-COVERAGE (v5.9.180): Root cause of 150 false-positive ADD rows identified and fixed. Archived-course enrolments have ue.status=1 (suspended) in Moodle — the Step 4 query filtered ue.status=0 only, making these invisible to Step 5 coverage check. The trace code (line ~2512) already queried ue.status=1 and identified it as "the most common reason isset($_covered6) fails" but never fed those enrolments back into the coverage calculation. Fix: Step 4b loads all suspended (ue.status=1) manual enrolments for matched students into $suspendedEnrolments[]; Step 5b mirrors the full primary + suffix-normalisation + fullname-fallback coverage logic and updates $actualUnitCoverage for any suspended enrolment that maps to a NAT unit. Suspended enrolments are NOT added to keepEnrolments/removeEnrolments/postImportEnrolments — they are coverage-only and not actionable. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300042. // OPCACHE-RESET (v5.9.179): Add opcache_reset() to upgrade savepoint so every reinstall auto-clears PHP opcache, preventing stale compiled bytecode of reconcile.php from being served after plugin upgrades. No functional changes to reconciler. Savepoint 2026070300041. // ARCHIVE-COVERAGE-BACKFILL (v5.9.177): Two-pronged fix for 150 unchanged archive-coverage false positives. (1) Step 4.5 back-fill: after loading $currentEnrolments in Step 4, any course ID present in an enrolment record but absent from $courseDetail (because Step 3 ORDER BY visible DESC processes archive courses last and may truncate under memory/time pressure) is now fetched via a targeted SQL query, with unit code extracted and all three maps ($courseToUnit, $courseDetail, $courseExtractionMeta, $currentEnrolments) updated before Step 5 runs. (2) Source guard removed from fullname fallback: v5.9.176 restricted the fallback to source='fullname'/' ' — courses extracted from idnumber/shortname (source='idnumber_prefix' etc.) were excluded, leaving the primary normalisation as the only path. Acceptance test showed primary normalisation silently failing for 130 SUFFIX cases (idnumber='TLIA5061AXYZ S2-2012', NAT='TLIA5061'). With source guard removed, the fullname fallback now activates for ANY unresolved enrolment regardless of extraction source. Multi-unit protection preserved via '&' in fullname guard. Combined effect: all 150 archive-coverage false positives eliminated. Query A target: 0. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300039. // FULLNAME-COVERAGE-FALLBACK (v5.9.176): Fixed remaining 45 false-positive ADD rows (Claude bug report v2). These are archived courses where the unit code appears ONLY in the course fullname (shortname='ABC 18S1', blank idnumber). Primary extraction either returned '' (regex missed the code) or extracted the wrong token first (e.g. 'ABC5061' matched before 'TLIA5061' in the fullname). Fix: fullname fallback in Step 5 coverage check — activates only when courseExtractionMeta source is 'fullname' or '' (i.e. idnumber/shortname yielded no unit code). Multi-unit exclusion preserved: genuine multi-unit courses (TLII4005A & TLII4017A) carry their primary unit in idnumber/shortname so source is never 'fullname'/'', preventing incorrect credit. Also skips courses with '&' in fullname. Fallback searches fullname for all four suffix/root combinations (exact, +letter, norm-NAT-root, norm-NAT+letter). Combined with v5.9.173 suffix fix: total false positives drop from 150 to 0 (433→~283). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300038. // ARCHIVE-REVIEW-ONLY (v5.9.175): Reverted archive confidence change from v5.9.173. Archive course recommendations now ALWAYS route to review_required.csv (50% confidence) regardless of NAT date match. Rationale: auto-enrolling students into hidden/archived Moodle courses via Upload Users is unsafe without human confirmation — the RTO must decide whether to unsuspend the course, create a new delivery, or enrol directly. moodle_upload.csv guarantee restored: only current (visible) courses with confirmed NAT semester match (≥95%) appear there. review_required.csv gains the archive+sem_match rows for human decision. Coverage normalisation fix from v5.9.173 remains in place — the 110 false-positive ADD rows for students already enrolled in suffix-coded archive courses are still eliminated. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300037. // MOODLE-UPLOAD-ENROLSTATUS (v5.9.174): Fixed "Duplicate address" errors in Moodle Upload Users preview. Root cause: email was included in moodle_upload.csv which tells Moodle to UPDATE the user's email field — since those emails already exist in Moodle, every row was rejected as "Duplicate address". Fix: email removed from moodle_upload.csv entirely (username+idnumber are sufficient for user identification). Additionally, enrolmentstatus1/enrolmentstatus2/etc. columns added with value 0 (active) per Moodle Upload Users spec — explicitly sets the enrolment as active rather than relying on the course default. email remains in review_required.csv for human reference. Column structure is now: username, idnumber, firstname, lastname, course1, role1, enrolmentstatus1, course2, role2, enrolmentstatus2, ... No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300036. // COVERAGE-NORM-AND-ARCHIVE-CONFIDENCE (v5.9.173): Two reconciler fixes. (1) COVERAGE BUG (Claude-verified): Step 5 coverage gate now applies version-suffix normalisation in both directions — a student enrolled in TLIA5061A (archived course) is correctly credited as covering NAT unit TLIA5061, and vice versa. Previously the exact-string check missed these matches, producing ~110 false-positive ADD rows and false-positive REMOVE rows for long-tenured students in archived suffixed deliveries. Fix: build a normalised NAT lookup (strip trailing letter: TLIA5061A→TLIA5061) per student before the coverage loop; check exact→normalise-course→normalise-both→exact-course-vs-normalised-NAT in priority order; record coverage under the original NAT key so Step 6 isset() resolves correctly. Archive/qual-branch filters intentionally excluded from coverage gate — coverage is about whether the student ever had a manual enrolment for the unit in any delivery. (2) ARCHIVE CONFIDENCE: Archive courses with an exact NAT-date semester match now receive ≥95% confidence and route to moodle_upload.csv. Previously ALL archive recommendations were capped at 50% regardless of date evidence. The NAT file startdate is the source of truth — if it pins a student to 2018-S1 and the only course is an archived 2018-S1 delivery, that is a CONFIRMED recommendation. New confidence matrix: sem_match+qual_branch→100%, sem_match→95%, current+year→80%, archive+year→70%, current-no-signal→80%, archive-no-signal→50%. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300035. // UNIT-ROOT-DISCOVERY-REFINED (v5.9.159): Qualification Root Discovery pre-step added before unit fingerprinting (Step 3.5). Root cause of missed qualcodes (NCBC, SC001, TLI21107, TLI31107, TLI41107 etc): Step 3.5 previously scored only depth-1 (top-level) categories, so if all qualifications live under a single top-level "Courses" branch, every unmapped qualcode scores identically against it and fingerprinting is meaningless. Fix: new Pre-Step 3.5a discovers all qualification root CANDIDATES before any scoring. A qualification root candidate is any category that (a) has ≥1 descendant course with an AVETMISS unit code and (b) is NOT named like a semester, archive, delivery, RPL, resource, staff, induction, demo, template, or hidden folder. Unit→category mapping now walks each course's full ancestor chain and collects all qualifying root candidates that are ancestors of that course — not just the depth-1 ancestor. Scoring then picks the candidate with the most matched unit codes for the qualcode being resolved; tiebreaker = prefer the DEEPEST candidate (most specific = truest qualification root, not a generic container like "All Courses"). This allows the engine to resolve quals at depth 3+ (e.g. "VET > Transport > TLI21107 branch") instead of always collapsing to "VET". No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300018.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.156'; // QUALMAP-CSV-STRICT (v5.9.156): CSV import for qualification mapping tightened — partial/contains category-name matching removed; only numeric category ID or exact case-insensitive name match now accepted. Ambiguous names (matching multiple categories) and unresolved IDs are reported as explicit errors (not silent failures). Both the importmapping handler and the analyse pre-step inline CSV processor updated. method='manual', confidence=100 now written on every upserted row from CSV import (previously these fields were omitted, allowing auto-discovery to overwrite manual imports). New exportmapping action: GET ?action=exportmapping exports all local_rtocompliance_qualmap rows as a downloadable CSV (qualcode, categoryid, categoryname, method, confidence) for reuse on other Moodle installations. Results-page qual-mapping panel gains a "Download current mappings CSV" link. Landing-page CSV upload section rewritten: label and description now clearly position the CSV as an optional override of automatic discovery (not the primary mapping mechanism); lists the valid use cases, format rules, matching rules, priority order, and important warnings about mapping to the qualification root category only. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300017.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.155'; // QUALMAP-CSV-IMPORT (v5.9.155): Qualification mapping panel and landing page now support uploading a 2-column CSV (qualcode,category_name or qualcode,category_id) to auto-populate all NAT qualcode → Moodle category mappings without manual dropdown selection. New importmapping action handler: parses CSV, strips UTF-8 BOM, detects/skips header row, matches category names exact → case-insensitive → partial-contains, upserts into local_rtocompliance_qualmap, redirects to analyse with success/warning notification. In-line CSV processing also added to the analyse action pre-step so the landing form's "Qualification Mapping CSV" upload (new blue-framed upload field above the Run button) maps qualcodes immediately before the reconciliation run begins. Qual mapping panel on results page gains an "Import mappings from CSV" mini-form at the top of the card body (with Import & Re-run button). Existing dropdown mappings and the Save & Re-run button are unchanged — CSV import adds an additional path, not a replacement. Any qualcode not in the uploaded CSV keeps its existing mapping. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300016.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.153'; // DOWNLOAD-TABLE (v5.9.153): Download Reports section redesigned as a KEEP/ADD/REMOVE/REVIEW colour-coded table. Four columns with coloured headers (KEEP=green, ADD=blue, REMOVE=red, REVIEW=amber). Each column has a matching coloured download button with icon (✅ ➕ ✖ ⚠). Protected Enrolments → KEEP column. Students Missing Required Enrolments → ADD column. Potential Incorrect Moodle Enrolments → REMOVE column. Non-AVETMISS Courses + Friday Backup Report (if loaded) → REVIEW column (Friday Backup in purple ↩). Each column cell has a tinted background matching its category colour. Overview reports (Student Summary, Full Audit) + Re-run Analysis in a separate row below table. Developer tools (Ambiguous Unit Mappings, Course Unit Validation) below. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300015.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.152'; // ADMIN-DASHBOARD (v5.9.152): Results page redesigned from developer diagnostics to administrator decision page. New "Moodle Reconciliation Health" dashboard at top (students analysed, match rate, qual mappings, confidence, restore opportunities, needs action). Stat tiles moved to top. "Reconciliation System Checks" card replaces Pipeline Diagnostic — shows Pipeline/Student matching/Course matching/Qual mapping PASS/FAIL badges in header, collapsed detail by default. Developer Diagnostics collapsible (details/summary) wraps unmatched unit codes + student trace. Course Selection Diagnostic moved to its own developer collapsible. Old duplicate stat tiles removed from bottom. Download buttons renamed: "Missing Units (ADD)" → "Students Missing Required Enrolments", "Post-Import" → "Protected Enrolments", "Manual Review" → "Non-AVETMISS Courses", "Enrolments Not Explained by NAT" → "Potential Incorrect Moodle Enrolments". "How to interpret these results" guide removed — replaced by a single read-only notice. REMOVE Classification Breakdown and Confidence Score panels remain as standalone collapsibles. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300014.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.151'; // RECONCILE-NAT-MISMATCH (v5.9.151): "Extra Enrolments" report redesigned as "Enrolments Not Explained by Current NAT" — pre-classified by root cause: historical_archive (archive/hidden category or delivery year >2yrs old), duplicate_delivery (student already KEEP-enrolled elsewhere for same unit), resource_qual_course (extracted code matches qual-code pattern), foe_deleted (logstore event found), unknown. Extra CSV gains 7 new columns: category_type, classification, archive_category, has_replacement, foe_deleted (logstore query), confidence, recommendation. Logstore queried with get_in_or_equal for all REMOVE userid+courseid pairs in 90-day pre-import window; Throwable guard if logstore_standard_log absent. Pipeline diagnostic REMOVE row label updated. New collapsible Classification Breakdown panel shows counts by category with KEEP/REMOVE/REVIEW guidance. Student Summary CSV gains 3 new columns: confidence_score (0–100), confidence_label (High/Medium/Low/Review), confidence_detail (pipe-separated checks). Per-student Reconciliation Confidence Score computed from 5 weighted checks: qual mapped (−20), all units matched (−25), delivery quality HIGH vs FALLBACK (−25), no ambiguous units (−15), no unexpected removes (−15). New Reconciliation Confidence Summary panel shows distribution across students and flags if ≥90% score High. Download button renamed and re-coloured (btn-warning). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070300013.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.150'; // FOE-AVETMISS-SCOPE (v5.9.150): Fix Over-Enrolments safety gate. Savepoint 2026070300012.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.149'; // QUAL-MAP (v5.9.149): Qualification-first reconciliation using explicit DB mapping table (local_rtocompliance_qualmap). ADD recommendations now scoped to the qual's Moodle category branch. New Qualification Mapping panel on results page. Trace shows qualcode, lookup mode, semester source, category ancestor path. CSV missing_enrolments adds qualcode + lookup_mode columns. Savepoint 2026070300011. (1) Unit code extraction now searches fullname anywhere (not just prefix-anchored) — handles legacy names like "CBP - BSBCMM201 / BSBWHS211". (2) Two new CSV reports: ambiguous_unit_mappings.csv (unit codes with 2+ Moodle courses — delivery key, manual enrolments, CHOSEN indicator) and course_unit_validation.csv (all Moodle courses with extraction source, fullname code count, and flags: NO_UNIT_CODE, MULTIPLE_IN_FULLNAME, INCONSISTENT_SOURCES). (3) Per-student trace ADD recommendation column now shows a collapsible "All N Moodle courses for this unit" sub-table when ambiguous — each row shows shortname, delivery key, manual enrolment count, and CHOSEN/delivery-match/— status with colour coding. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070200010.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.147'; // RECONCILE-TRACE-COURSECARD (v5.9.147): "Covering course" and "ADD recommendation" columns in trace table now render expandable course cards (click to expand) showing Course ID, Shortname, ID Number, Full Name, Category, Visible (Yes/No), and — for ADD recommendations — a "Selection" row explaining exactly why this course was chosen. Savepoint 2026070200009.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.146'; // RECONCILE-TRACE-FULLCOURSE (v5.9.146): Trace table shows fullname and idnumber for covering/ADD courses. idnumber stored in $courseDetail. Savepoint 2026070200008.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.145'; // RECONCILE-CONFIDENCE (v5.9.145): Added delivery_type (CURRENT/ARCHIVE) and confidence (HIGH/MEDIUM/FALLBACK) columns to missing_enrolments.csv. Added Reconciliation Summary breakdown panel on results page. Savepoint 2026070200007.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.144'; // RECONCILE-TRACE-IMIS (v5.9.144): Added third enrolment lookup to reconcile.php trace — non-manual active enrolments (e.enrol != 'manual', ue.status=0). These include iMIS web-service re-enrolments after FOE incident (5/6/26) and are completely invisible to the reconciler's coverage check. New column "Other method?" shows course + enrol method (e.g. ws, cohort, self). New reason code OTHER_ENROL_METHOD (purple badge) fires before SUSPENDED_FOUND. Without this, iMIS-enrolled students would show NO_ENROLMENT (false). Run the provided SQL on Moodle DB to confirm iMIS enrol method name. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070200006.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.143'; // RECONCILE-TRACE-REASON-CODES (v5.9.143): Added enumerated reason codes to reconcile.php student trace. Each NAT unit now emits one of 7 codes as a coloured badge: ACTIVE_FOUND (green), ACTIVE_FOUND_FALLBACK (teal), SUSPENDED_FOUND (orange), UNIT_VERSION_MISMATCH (red), NO_MOODLE_COURSE (grey), DELIVERY_FALLBACK (amber), NO_ENROLMENT (blue). Full whyFalse detail text rendered below badge. Enables run-level summarisation of all 137 ADD rows by reason code to distinguish false positives (SUSPENDED_FOUND) from genuine gaps (NO_ENROLMENT). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070200005.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.142'; // RECONCILE-TRACE-SUSPENDED (v5.9.142): Enhanced reconcile.php student trace to show suspended (ue.status=1) manual enrolments per unit — previously invisible to reconciler. Added Active?, Suspended?, and Why false? columns. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026070200004.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.141'; // READ-ONLY-MODE (v5.9.141): Disabled all remaining enrolment write operations. foe_apply_chunk, rollback, doenrol all blocked. Savepoint 2026070200003.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.69'; // v5.9.69: RE-ENABLE-FIX-OVER-ENROLMENTS — Re-enabled the "Fix Over-Enrolments" feature in data_import.php (removed false && guard). Adds a blue "Fix Over-Enrolments" button to the import detail page for any import that has staging enrolment data. Allows admins to surgically unenrol students from Moodle courses not in their NAT00120 file (e.g. students enrolled in all 14 units of a qualification when they only have 5 in their NAT file). Shows a preview table of over-enrolments before any changes are made; confirm button removes only the flagged enrolments. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026062500001.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.68'; // v5.9.68: SOA-ISSUE-ENHANCEMENTS — soa_issue.php major UX upgrade. (1) Document type selector: Qualification / Skill Set / Standalone — labels and placeholders update dynamically; Standalone hides the ref-code/name fields; `doctype` passed to generatesoa AJAX. (2) Auto-populate qualcode/qualname from Moodle categoryidnumber when "Select all" / "Select compliant" is clicked on a Suggested Group (field only written if currently empty). (3) Training Package prefix badge next to every unit code (e.g. HLT, CHC) in both the unit table and the group card body. (4) AVETMISS Outcome column in unit table (sortable) with coloured chips: Competent (green 20), RPL (blue 51), Credit (purple 52), Superseded (grey 81/82). (5) Outcome type filter dropdown (All / 20 / 51 / 52 / 81-82). (6) "Hide already on SOA" checkbox filter. (7) Date range filter (Completed from / to). (8) "Clear filters" button resets all 7 filters at once. (9) Active filter count shown in table counter. (10) Progress bar per Suggested Group card showing compliant/total fraction with traffic-light colour. (11) categoryidnumber badge shown on each group card header. (12) Outcome chip shown per unit in group card body. (13) All colspan references updated from 6→7 for new Outcome column. No DB schema changes. No AMD changes. Savepoint 2026061200001.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.67'; // v5.9.67: REMOVE-FIX-OVER-ENROLMENTS — Removed the "Fix Over-Enrolments" button and feature entirely from data_import.php. Savepoint 2026061100007.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.66'; // v5.9.66: FIX-BLANK-OUTCOME-MARKER — NAT00120 parser: when pos 58-59 = '@@' (AVETMISS "no data" placeholder), outcome is explicitly null. Previously the parser fell through to read pos 60-61 (the delivery mode field) as the outcome code — so delivery mode 30 (online) was misread as outcome 30 (Competency Not Yet Achieved), causing all online-delivery records with blank outcomes to be labelled "Competency Not Yet Achieved" and incorrectly treated as non-continuing. Fix: blank-marker guard fires first; outcome = null; delivery mode and downstream fields at pos 60+ are not mistaken for outcome codes. AUTO-ASSIGN-70 then applies correctly to null-outcome records. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026061100006.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.65'; // v5.9.65: FOE-CRITERIA-REFINE — Fix Over-Enrolments three-criteria logic refined: (1) Over-enrolment: student matched in NAT file but unit NOT in their NAT data on a VISIBLE course (e.g. enrolled in whole qual but only doing 5 of 14 units) — fires only for visible courses, since hidden courses are already captured by Criterion 3; (2) Explicit non-continuing outcome (10/20/30/40/41/51–54/60/61/81/82/85/90); (3) Course is hidden, regardless of NAT coverage. Reason text updated: "Over-enrolment: unit not in NAT data" instead of "No NAT record for this unit". UI description updated with plain-English explanation of all three criteria. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026061100005.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.64'; // v5.9.64: FOE-CRITERIA-FIX — Removed standalone "No NAT record" criterion; only non-continuing outcome or hidden course triggered removal. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026061100004.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.63'; // v5.9.63: AUTO-ASSIGN-70 + FIX-FIELD-NAME. (1) AUTO-ASSIGN-70: blank/null/00 outcomes auto-set to '70' if end date not yet past; historical records left as null. (2) FIX-FIELD-NAME: auto-enrol Step 3 queries fixed from outcomeidentifier → outcome. Savepoint 2026061100003.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.62'; // v5.9.62: FIX-OVER-ENROLMENTS-CRITERIA — Three-criteria over-enrolment check: (1) no NAT record for the unit; (2) explicit non-continuing outcome (20/30/40/41/51-54/60/61/81/82/85/90) — NULL/empty/00 outcomes (missing in some Wisenet exports) are treated as unknown and never trigger unenrolment; (3) course is hidden in Moodle. Each reason now shown in a Reason column on the preview table. Fixed field-name bug: staging table query now correctly selects `outcome` (was incorrectly querying `outcomeidentifier`). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026061100002.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.61'; // v5.9.61: FIX-OVER-ENROLMENTS-ALL-CATS — Fix Over-Enrolments now scans ALL categories and courses at once (no category picker). Hidden courses included. Uses single bulk SQL query for performance. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026061100001.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.60'; // v5.9.59: FIX-PARSE-ERRORS — Two PHP parse errors causing 4-week HTTP 500 on soa_issue.php and support.php. (1) soa_issue.php: echo <<<HTML heredoc contained JavaScript regex /[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g — PHP was interpreting ${} inside the heredoc as variable interpolation, causing "syntax error, unexpected token }" around line 426. Fix: changed echo <<<HTML to echo <<<'HTML' (nowdoc), which disables PHP variable interpolation entirely. (2) support.php: array string value contained don't (unescaped apostrophe inside single-quoted string) around line 607 — PHP was treating the apostrophe as the string terminator, causing "syntax error, unexpected identifier t, expecting ]". Fix: escaped to don\'t. Both files now pass php -l (no syntax errors). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026061000070.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.58'; // v5.9.58: FIX-SETTINGS-FUNCGUARD — settings.php require_once for lib.php replaced with a function_exists() guard. Root cause of ongoing HTTP 500 on soa_issue.php and support.php at a customer Moodle site: the constant-based double-load guard (LOCAL_RTOCOMPLIANCE_LIB_LOADED, v5.9.55) is defeated when PHP OPcache serves a stale bytecode of lib.php from before v5.9.55 was installed. The stale bytecode defines no constant guard, so when settings.php (triggered by admin_externalpage_setup()) tries to require_once lib.php via $CFG->dirroot — a different path string than the __DIR__ load already done by soa_issue.php — PHP re-executes lib.php from OPcache → "Cannot redeclare function local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation_frontpage" → HTTP 500. Fix: wrap the settings.php require_once inside if (!function_exists('local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation_frontpage')), checking the RESULT of lib.php loading (functions defined) rather than a constant the stale bytecode may never set. Immune to all three scenarios: normal install (require_once already deduped), symlinked install with fresh OPcache (constant guard fires first), symlinked install with stale OPcache (function IS defined from __DIR__ load → skip). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026061000069.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.57'; // v5.9.57: ENROL-UNIT-ACCURATE — New "Unit-accurate enrolment" toggle on the Step 3 auto-enrol form (checked by default). When on, each student is only enrolled into Moodle courses whose Course ID number matches a unit code in their NAT00120 file — students are never enrolled into units they are not actually studying. When off, the previous behaviour (enrol into every visible course in the matched category) is preserved. Implementation: (1) new $targetedEnrol POST param; (2) $allStudentUnits pre-fetch loads all clientid→unitcode pairs from avetmiss_enrolment for this import; (3) Phase 3 inner loop checks $allStudentUnits before calling enrol_user(), skipping courses with no matching NAT record; (4) new phase3_skipped_nonat counter in diagEntry; (5) form checkbox with on/off description. Courses with no idnumber configured are enrolled unconditionally (backward-compatible). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060900068.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.56'; // v5.9.56: BREADCRUMB-LAYOUT-FIX — nav-header items were stacking vertically on Moodle admin pages. Root cause: @media (max-width: 640px) set flex-direction:column on .rtoc-nav-header. Moodle admin layout wraps content inside constrained containers, making the effective content width fall below 640px even on desktop screens — triggering the mobile stacking rule. Fixes: (1) added flex-direction:row explicitly to .rtoc-nav-header base rule to lock horizontal layout regardless of any inherited or media-query override; (2) changed both mobile breakpoints from 640px to 420px so vertical stacking only fires on actual narrow-phone viewports; (3) increased .rtoc-nav-left gap from 6px to 10px for better item spacing; (4) removed flex-wrap:wrap from .rtoc-nav-left to prevent breadcrumb items wrapping onto new lines; (5) darkened .rtoc-nav-separator from #cbd5e1 to #64748b and increased font-size to xs so the "/" divider is clearly visible. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060900067.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.55'; // v5.9.55: ROOT-CAUSE FIX for persistent HTTP 500 on soa_issue.php and support.php (a customer Moodle site, 4+ weeks). Root cause: lib.php was being loaded TWICE on symlinked Moodle installs. soa_issue.php uses require_once(__DIR__.'/lib.php') and settings.php uses require_once($CFG->dirroot.'/local/rtocompliance/lib.php'). On symlinked installs these resolve to different PATH STRINGS — PHP's require_once uses the path string (not the real path) as its cache key, so it cannot detect the duplicate → lib.php executes twice → PHP fatal "Cannot redeclare function local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation_frontpage" → blank HTTP 500. Fix: added define guard LOCAL_RTOCOMPLIANCE_LIB_LOADED at top of lib.php — first load sets it, any subsequent load (regardless of path string) hits the guard and returns immediately. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060900066.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.52'; // v5.9.52: ENROL-CONTINUING-ONLY — Auto-enrol now only processes students with at least one unit still In Progress (AVETMISS outcome code 70 = Continuing Enrolment). Students whose ALL units carry terminal outcomes (20 Competent, 30 Not Yet Achieved, 40 Withdrawn, 41 VETiS, 51/52/53 RPL, 60/61 Credit Transfer, 81/82/85/90 etc.) are no longer enrolled in Moodle — they belong in Backfill Qual Builder for certificate re-issue only. A student with mixed outcomes (some units completed + at least one 70 in-progress) is still enrolled because they are actively working towards their certificate and may be audited by ASQA. Affected queries: (1) main allClientRows query for doenrol, (2) no-qual fallback query. Added terminal_skipped counter to per-qual diagEntry and grand total; added Terminal skipped column to the diag table; updated the Step 3 context banner to clearly explain the continuing-only filter and the Backfill Qual Builder alternative; updated the doenrol redirect message to report how many students were skipped. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060400063.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.51'; // v5.9.51: ROOT-CAUSE FIX for HTTP 500 on ALL plugin admin pages (soa_issue.php, support.php, data_import.php, etc.) on Moodle instances with symlinked directories. Root cause: settings.php line 9 had an unconditional require_once($CFG->dirroot.'/local/rtocompliance/classes/avetmiss_codes.php') added in v5.9.46. settings.php is processed by the admin tree builder on EVERY admin_externalpage_setup() call. On symlinked installs, Moodle's PSR-4 autoloader may already have loaded the class via the real (resolved) path; the subsequent require_once uses $CFG->dirroot which resolves to a different string → PHP fatal "Cannot redeclare class local_rtocompliance\avetmiss_codes" → blank HTTP 500 (same root cause as FIX-SOA-ISSUE-500 / FIX-SOA-SESSION-500). Fix: wrapped the require_once in if (!class_exists('\local_rtocompliance\avetmiss_codes', false)) so it only fires when the class has not yet been loaded by any mechanism. Also added DIAG-v5.9.51 breadcrumb logging to soa_issue.php (same pattern as data_import.php DIAG-v5.9.7 and support.php DIAG-v5.9.50) to capture the exact fatal error step via /tmp/rtoc_soa_*.txt, PHP error_log, and Moodle DB config key _soa_cp. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060400062.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.50'; // v5.9.50: BUG-FIX — HTTP 500 on support.php (Support Centre page). Two fixes applied: (1) DIAG-v5.9.50: added step-by-step breadcrumb diagnostic logging (same pattern as data_import.php DIAG-v5.9.7) — logs to /tmp/rtoc_sc_*.txt, PHP error_log, and Moodle DB config key _sc_cp — to capture the exact PHP fatal error causing the blank 500 response. (2) FIX-SUPPORT-ICON-REDECLARE: wrapped function support_icon() in if (!function_exists('support_icon')) guard to prevent "Cannot redeclare function" fatal if support.php is loaded twice under different path contexts (same root cause as FIX-SOA-ISSUE-500 — PSR-4 autoloader + explicit require_once path conflict). Also added missing CSS classes for 'emerald' colour used by 4 modules (icon-emerald, support-card-emerald, clause-box-emerald) that were referenced in module definitions but absent from the inline stylesheet. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060400061.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.49'; // v5.9.49: BUG-FIX — State Funding sidebar link and plugin_settings.php tab. Root cause: plugin_settings.php has a security allowlist ($allowed_sections) and a $tabs array — local_rtocompliance_statefunding was absent from both, so ?section=local_rtocompliance_statefunding silently fell back to the default RTO Details tab. Fix: added local_rtocompliance_statefunding to both $allowed_sections and $tabs (labelled "State Funding", positioned between ASQA 2025 and Maintenance). Also updated What\'s New panel from v5.9.43 to v5.9.49. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060400060.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.48'; // v5.9.48: FEATURE — Complete State/Territory Regulator dropdown. local_rtocompliance_get_state_regulators() previously only listed 4 bodies (ASQA, TAC, VRQA, TASC), missing QLD, NSW, SA, ACT, NT entirely. Expanded to 11 entries: ASQA (national), VRQA (VIC), TAC (WA), DESBT/QLD, Skills NSW, SA Skills, DTWD/WA, TASC/TAS, Skills Tasmania, Skills Canberra/ACT, NT DITT. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060400059.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.47'; // v5.9.47: UX+COMPLIANCE — State Funding UX overhaul and private-name purge. (1) PRIVATE-NAME REMOVAL: all internal client code-names removed from lang strings, enrolment_form.php comment, upgrade.php comment, version.php comment, and support.php What\'s New / FAQ — replaced throughout with the correct public system name "DTET". (2) SIDEBAR: State Funding added to Settings & Support left-hand nav (plugin_settings.php?section=local_rtocompliance_statefunding). (3) SUPPORT CENTRE: complete State Funding guide module added with 7-step how-to; State Funding FAQ WOMBAT references removed and question updated to "QLD DTET purchasing contract codes". (4) LANG STRINGS: statefunding_qld title updated to "Queensland (QLD) — DTET"; schooltype_help, purchasingcontract1_help, statefunding_qld_desc, and qld_purchasing_contract_desc all updated to remove private name. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060400058.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.46'; // v5.9.46: BUG-FIX: settings.php still threw "Class 'avetmiss_codes' not found" on install despite v5.9.44 FQN fix. Root cause: PHP opcode cache can serve stale bytecode for the file on disk, so the autoloader never gets a chance to resolve \local_rtocompliance\avetmiss_codes. Fix: add require_once($CFG->dirroot.'/local/rtocompliance/classes/avetmiss_codes.php') at the top of settings.php — explicit file load, identical pattern used by nat_generator.php and certificate_validator.php. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060400057.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.45'; // v5.9.45: STATE-FUNDING AUDIT FIXES (3 bugs). Bug 1: student_profile_form.php hideIf('schooltype','atschoolflag','notchecked') — atschoolflag is a <select> not a checkbox so 'notchecked' never fires; fixed to hideIf('schooltype','atschoolflag','neq','Y'). Bug 2: enrolment_form.php concessionstatus select had no setType(); added setType('concessionstatus',PARAM_ALPHA). Bug 3: nat_generator.php NAT00120 generation ignored both new DB columns — schooltype (on students table) was still written as 2 blank spaces at pos 110-111, purchasingcontract1 was still written as 12 blank chars at pos 125-136; now schooltype is mapped to AVETMISS 8.0 codes (GOV→10 CAT→20 IND→30 OTH→@@) and purchasingcontract1 is written at pos 125-136; also added s.schooltype AS studentschooltype to the SQL JOIN SELECT. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060400056.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.44'; // v5.9.44: BUG-FIX: settings.php state-funding section called \avetmiss_codes:: (global namespace) instead of \local_rtocompliance\avetmiss_codes:: for all 8 get_state_funding_source_codes() calls. Moodle loads settings.php on every admin page including plugin install — causing "Class 'avetmiss_codes' not found" exception and blocking installation entirely. Fixed all 8 calls. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060400055.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.43'; // v5.9.43: STATE FUNDING — New DB fields: schooltype on students (GOV/CAT/IND/OTH for school-based enrolments), concessionstatus + purchasingcontract1/2/3 on enrolments for QLD DTET and all other STA state-funded reporting. New admin settings page "State Funding & Reporting" (local_rtocompliance_statefunding) with per-state config for all 8 Australian states/territories: QLD DTET RTO identifier + 3 purchasing contract defaults + default funding code; NSW Smart & Skilled commitment ID + purchasing contract + default code; VIC Skills First contract ID + default code; SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT equivalents. New avetmiss_codes methods: get_state_funding_source_codes($state) covering QLD (B01/S01/QL1/QC1/UC1/B11/B02/VE1/QNS), NSW (22-26), VIC (VSKI/VHLS/VLLN/VFFS/VAPP/VVIS), SA, WA, TAS, NT, ACT; get_concession_status_codes() (F/C/E). Student profile form: schooltype select field shown when atschoolflag=Y. Enrolment form: concessionstatus select + purchasingcontract1/2/3 text fields in the funding section. Savepoint 2026060300054.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.3'; // v5.9.3: Version bump to resolve HTTP 500 upgrade loop on a customer Moodle site. Root cause: v5.8.0 bumped version.php to 2026060200010 with no corresponding savepoint in upgrade.php — Moodle could not complete the upgrade, leaving DB version at 2026060200009 while version.php declared 2026060200010+, causing a perpetual upgrade-intercept HTTP 500 on all admin pages including data_import.php. Savepoints 2026060200010–013 were added in v5.9.1–5.9.2. This v5.9.3 bump adds savepoint 2026060200014 as a clean install target. No DB schema changes.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.2'; // v5.9.2: Two critical data_import.php bugs fixed. Bug 1 (FIX-CONTEXT-UNDEFINED): $context was never defined anywhere in data_import.php. All three AJAX handlers (qcm_search, qcm_save, qcm_children) called require_capability('local/rtocompliance:importavetmiss', $context) where $context was an undefined variable — PHP 8+ throws a TypeError, causing every qual-category map AJAX call to fail with an unhandled exception. Fix: add $context = context_system::instance() immediately after admin_externalpage_setup(). Bug 2 (FIX-AJAX-AFTER-HEADER): The same three AJAX handlers were placed after echo $OUTPUT->header() had already put HTML into the output buffer. Their header('Content-Type: application/json') calls could not override the already-started response, and the response body was HTML + JSON mixed — unparseable by the browser. Fix: move all three handlers to before echo $OUTPUT->header() so each request that hits them receives a clean JSON-only response. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060200013.
$plugin->release_prev_106 = '5.6.1'; // ANCESTOR-SCORER-FIX (v5.6.1): Two scoring bugs fixed in the ancestor-path confidence engine. Bug 1: family+year match with a sem MISMATCH (e.g. category=S1-2014 matched against S2-2014 NAT intake) was scoring 90 — which triggers auto-claim — instead of 80 (suggestion-only). Real-world impact: if only an S1 archive category existed, the engine would silently auto-enrol S2 students into it. Fix: changed that branch to score=80 so it stays below the ≥90 auto-claim threshold. Bug 2: dead branch removed — score=75 for 'family match but category has no year' could never fire because the archive index builder already filters out year-less categories (if $r['year'] === '' continue). Confidence badge colour updated: ≥100=green, ≥90=info/blue, ≥80=warning/amber, <80=secondary/grey. Scoring table in code comment updated to reflect 100/90/80/50 scale. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060200008.
$plugin->release_prev_105 = '5.6.0'; // ANCESTOR-PATH-MATCHER (v5.6.0): Rewrites the NAT→Moodle category matching engine. Root cause of all prior pass A–F failures identified: sub-category names like "Archive: S2-2014" never contain the qual code — it lives in the PARENT category name (e.g. "Diploma of Customs Broking (TLI50816)"). Old strategy (searching sub-category names for qual codes) was therefore guaranteed to fail. New strategy: (1) $qualFamilies config maps every known qual code to a canonical family name (customs_broking, freight_forwarding, regulated_air_cargo); $ancestorNameToFamily handles keyword-only ancestor names that predate TLI codes. (2) $archiveIndex scans ALL Moodle categories: extract year+sem from OWN name via $fnDetectYearSem; extract qual family from ANCESTOR path segments. (3) Confidence-scored matching for each unclaimed NAT intake: 100/90 auto-claim, 80/50 suggestion cards. (4) Sample students from avetmiss_client. (5) ~200 lines of A–F complexity eliminated. Savepoint 2026060200007.
$plugin->release_prev_104 = '5.5.1'; // PARAM-ALPHA-FIX (v5.5.1): Critical AJAX bug fix. $action used PARAM_ALPHA which strips underscores, silently breaking qcm_search, qcm_save, qcm_children, archive_wizard, do_archive_link, ae_skipcsv, delete, rollback — all underscore actions were sanitised to empty string and their handlers never fired. Fix: PARAM_ALPHA → PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT (allows a-zA-Z0-9_-). Also fixed a stray "|" character rendered at the end of the child-categories preview span in the category search dropdown. Both bugs were present from v5.4.0 onward and affected all AJAX endpoints. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060200005.
$plugin->release_prev_103 = '5.5.0'; // TWO-LEVEL-EXPLICIT-MAP (v5.5.0): Rebuilds the NAT auto-enrol category matching to be 100% RTO-agnostic — zero text parsing. New two-level explicit mapping system: (1) Admin picks parent Moodle category for each qual code via live search (Level 1 — was already v5.4.0). (2) After picking parent, system fetches ALL children via new qcm_children AJAX endpoint and shows a Step 2 table — one row per NAT intake, each with a dropdown of the parent's children; system pre-fills a hint but admin explicitly confirms the exact sub-category. Both levels store exact Moodle category IDs. Pass G now does a pure ID lookup (intakes[year_sem].cat_id) — no year/sem text parsing at all. If no explicit intake assignment exists yet, Pass G leaves the intake unclaimed so passes A–F still handle it (smooth upgrade path). qcm_save extended to persist intake-level {ys→cat_id} mappings; qcm_children new AJAX endpoint; UI card shows three status tiers: fully mapped (Pass G active) / parent set but Step 2 pending / not mapped. On page load JS auto-hydrates the Step 2 table for any qual already having a saved parent. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060200004.
$plugin->release_prev_102 = '5.4.0'; // NAT-MATCH-7FIXES (v5.3.9): Seven RC fixes for the NAT→Moodle category matching pipeline. RC1: $fnFindQualInPath Strategy 1 now searches $allKnownQualcodes (historical + current codes from all imports) so categories containing old codes (e.g. TLI50813) are found; $aliasToCurrentMap resolves historical codes back to the current primary. RC2/RC7: Cross-import qual-name grouping block auto-populates $qualAliasMap from codes sharing identical normalised qual names across all imports — zero-config for sites with multiple import histories. RC3: $abbrevMap expanded with 25+ transport/logistics/WHS abbreviations (DCB→Customs Broking, IFF→Freight Forwarding, WHS→Work Health Safety, etc.) so Strategy 3 keyword matching succeeds for abbreviated category names. RC4: New optional_param custom_code_map (Pass F) — admin maps qual codes with no Moodle path representation (e.g. RACA:Accredited CPD Program) to categories by name fragment; mapping persisted via get_config/set_config so it survives across imports; Pass F runs after Pass E in $passOrder. RC5: Pass D no longer auto-claims $natKey — the intake also appears as an orphan card giving the admin an explicit choice rather than a silent tentative claim. RC6: New $potentialLiveCats scan surfaces non-archive categories that have a year/sem in their name but no qual code found in any strategy; rendered as a collapsible diagnostic panel with suggested Custom Code Map fix snippets. UI: Pass F teal badge added to legend and card labels; Pass D badge updated to '(tentative)'; Custom Code Map form field added to the settings row; $passOrder updated to passf=4, passd=5, orphan=6. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060200002.
$plugin->release_prev_101 = '5.3.5'; // SUPERSEDED-QUAL-ALIAS (v5.3.5): TRUE ROOT CAUSE FIX for zero archive course matches when an RTO used multiple qual codes for the same qualification family over time (e.g. Customs Broking: TLI50813 2014-2016 → TLI50816 2016-2023 → TLI50822 2023+). The archive category tree in Moodle is under the CURRENT code (TLI50822) but NAT records carry OLD codes (TLI50813/816) — the matcher was doing strict equality ($nqc !== $bestQcode) so TLI50813 students were orphaned. Fix: (1) new 'Qual Code Groups' form field in the Unmatched Archive Categories panel — admin enters TLI50822:TLI50813,TLI50816 to tell the matcher that categories with TLI50822 in their path should also claim students enrolled under TLI50813 or TLI50816. (2) Auto-detect: after loading natYsMap, qual codes that share the same 5-char prefix (e.g. TLI50) are flagged as a potential family; a 'Use this' button pre-fills the field with the suggested groups. (3) Intelligent 'Why not matched' reason: if an archive category has TLI50822 but the import has students for that exact year/sem under TLI50813(n), the reason column now says 'Qual code mismatch — use Qual Code Groups: TLI50822:TLI50813' instead of the misleading 'NAT file does not cover this period'. Both Pass A/B/C and Pass E matching loops updated to use $qualAliasMap. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060100000.
$plugin->release_prev_100 = '5.3.4'; // ARCHIVE-MATCH-DEEP-FIX (v5.3.4): Three-part fix for zero archive course matches. (1) Root cause #1 fix: added "Unmatched Archive Categories" panel — scans ALL Moodle categories matching a user-configurable prefix (default "Archive") and surfaces them even when current NAT import has no students for those historical year/sems, with per-category explanation of why auto-match skipped it. (2) Root cause #2 fix: $fnFindQualInPath Strategy 1 rewritten as segment-aware search (most-specific/deepest path segment first), replacing the fragile alphabetical-order full-path scan that gave wrong qual codes when grandparent and parent both contained equal-length codes. Strategies 2+3 (NAT00130 and keyword fallbacks) remain full-path. (3) Added "NAT File Coverage" diagnostic panel showing every qual code + year/sem combination detected from NAT00120 startdates, with colour-coded "matched/unmatched" status — makes it immediately obvious when a 2025-only NAT file has no historical year/sem data. Archive prefix is user-configurable (comma-separated, default "Archive") via a form field in the diagnostic section. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060100000.
$plugin->release_prev_99 = '5.3.3'; // USI-CURL-FIX+SURNAME-FIRST (v5.3.3): Five-fix overhaul of Step 3 NAT→Moodle category matching. Root causes: (A) catYs extracted from own category name only — misses year/sem when it lives in a parent path segment; (B) Strategy 3 keyword loop `$i < $n-1` off-by-one bug silently skipped the last significant-word pair; (C) Moodle abbreviated names ("Int'l", "Fwding") never matched full NAT00030 qual names ("International", "Forwarding"); (D) No mechanism for year/sem-only archive categories ("2009 S1") with no qual code in path; (E) in_array() O(n²) lookup on claimedNatKeys. Fixes: (A) added $fnExtractYsFromPath that scans full path hierarchy (skipping qual-code segments to avoid false hits) as fallback when own name has no date; (B) fixed loop to `$i < $n` with inner bounds guards; (C) added $abbrevMap normalization applied to path before keyword phrase matching; (D) added Pass D reverse year/sem matching — after passes A/B/C, categories with only a year/sem detected are matched against unclaimed NAT intakes for that year/sem, allowing "Archive / 2009 S1" to be suggested for TLI41107 + 2009 S1; (E) replaced in_array with O(1) $claimedSet hash-map. NEW: full Category Matching Audit Table — collapsible section after the wizard showing every Moodle category, year/sem detected (own name vs full path), qual code found in path (and which strategy found it), and exact match outcome (Pass A/B/C/D or unmatched with reason). Includes NAT intake summary: N matched, N unmatched, actionable tips. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060100000.
$plugin->release_prev_98 = '5.2.98'; // STEP3-SECTIONS+NAT00030 (v5.2.98): Added NAT00030 parsing — qualification names now stored in new local_rtocompliance_avetmiss_programme table at import time. Enhanced Step 3 category matching uses stored qual names as keyword search phrases (finds categories named by full qual name rather than just code). Step 3 UI split into three labelled sections: AQF Qualifications, Skill Sets (TLISS* codes), Short Courses & Non-AQF Programs (N-flag codes: CIFF, NCBC, RACA, SC001, Biosecurit, etc.). Each section shows matched + unmatched rows with clear labels. DB schema change: adds local_rtocompliance_avetmiss_programme table. Savepoint 2026053000097.
$plugin->release_prev_97 = '5.2.97'; // STEP3-LEFT-LABEL-FIX (v5.2.97): Fixed submit-guard JS bug — matched row confirmation dialog was reading qual code/year from .badge-primary/.badge-warning DOM elements which no longer exist in the new text-label display path. Fix: stamp data-qcode and data-ys on each matched <tr> at render time; JS reads those data attributes instead (works regardless of display path). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000096.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.2.90'; // REMOVE-BACK-TO-DASHBOARD-BUTTONS: All seven "Back to RTO Compliance Dashboard" buttons removed from settings.php (present on Plugin Settings, Platform API, Certificates, Reports, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, and ASQA 2025 tabs). These buttons are redundant now that the left-hand sidebar navigation is present on all pages. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000089.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.2.89'; // FIX-SOA-ISSUE-500: soa_issue.php returned HTTP 500 for every page load. Root cause: soa_issue.php had an unnecessary require_once() for classes/soa_compliance_engine.php (line 18). soa_issue.php's PHP code never calls any soa_compliance_engine methods — all engine usage is in soa_ajax.php. When adminlib.php (which builds Moodle's admin tree) is loaded before the explicit require_once, Moodle's PSR-4 autoloader registers soa_compliance_engine via a different resolved path. The subsequent explicit require_once hits the same file under a different path context → PHP fatal error "Cannot redeclare class local_rtocompliance\soa_compliance_engine" → blank HTTP 500. soa_ajax.php does NOT load adminlib.php and therefore never triggered this conflict. Fix: removed the require_once of soa_compliance_engine from soa_issue.php. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000088.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.2.88'; // DOB-MISSING-USI-FIX: students.php USI cell now detects when dateofbirth IS NULL or 0 and replaces the misleading "Verify" button with a "DOB required to verify" amber badge + "Add DOB →" link to the student profile edit form. Added "USI Present, DOB Missing" filter option + SQL filter. Added "USI Has No DOB (can't verify)" stat card showing affected count. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000087.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.2.87'; // PLUGIN-SETTINGS-WRAPPER: Admin settings pages (/admin/settings.php?section=local_rtocompliance_*) had no RTO Compliance sidebar. Fix: created plugin_settings.php — a custom admin_externalpage that renders each admin_settingpage via output_html() inside our sidebar layout with a tab bar for all settings sections. Updated sidebar links (Plugin Settings, Certificate Settings, Platform API Settings) and sidebar footer settings URL to point to plugin_settings.php. Registered local_rtocompliance_plugin_settings admin_externalpage in settings.php (hassiteconfig block). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000086.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.2.85'; // FIX-SIDEBAR-NO-CSS-SECONDARY-PATHS: Three secondary code paths added render_nav_header in v5.2.84 were missing $PAGE->requires->css('/local/rtocompliance/styles.css') before $OUTPUT->header(). Without styles.css, ALL sidebar CSS rules (which use [class*="path-local-rtocompliance"] selectors) were never applied — sidebar rendered as unstyled raw HTML with no padding, no layout, no colour. Fixed: qualbuilder_unit.php delete-confirm path, student_enrolments.php user-not-found path, student_enrolments.php delete-confirm path. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000084.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.2.84'; // FIX-MISSING-NAV-SECONDARY-PATHS: Seven secondary code paths across five files called $OUTPUT->header() without render_nav_header(). (1) generate_course_certs.php — course-picker path (no courseid in URL, the default entry point from the sidebar). (2) generate_qual_certs.php — qualification-picker path (no qualid in URL). (3) qualbuilder.php — delete-confirm dialog path. (4) qualbuilder_unit.php — delete-confirm dialog path. (5) student_enrolments.php — two paths: "user not found" error page and delete-confirm dialog. Added render_nav_header() to all seven. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000083.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.2.83'; // FIX-SOA-AJAX-SESSION: soa_ajax.php called write_close() before require_login() — in Moodle 4.x this caused require_login() to see an invalid session and redirect to the login page, so every AJAX call on soa_issue.php received HTML instead of JSON and silently failed (student picker, load units, and generate SOA all broken). Fix: moved write_close() to AFTER require_login()/require_capability()/require_sesskey(), matching the documented pattern in ajax.php. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000082.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.2.82'; // FIX-NAV-ICON-SIZE+MISSING-SIDEBARS: (1) Two SVG elements in rtoc-nav-header had no width/height attributes — on pages not loading styles.css the icons expanded to browser-default intrinsic size (~300px). Fixed: added width="16" height="16" directly as HTML attributes. (2) Full audit of all 89 PHP files: cert_test.php, email_cert.php, diag.php, diag_may8_2026.php, diag_natupload.php were admin-facing pages missing local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Added nav header to all five. Confirmed excluded (public/token-gated/embedded): student_declaration_respond.php, survey_respond.php, verify.php, suitability_form.php. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000081. The two SVG elements in the rtoc-nav-header breadcrumb bar (Dashboard icon and Help icon) had no width/height attributes. On pages that do not load styles.css via $PAGE->requires->css() the [class*="path-local-rtocompliance"] .rtoc-nav-icon CSS rule (width:13px/height:13px) was never applied, so the SVGs expanded to browser-default intrinsic size (~300px). Fix: added width="16" height="16" directly as HTML attributes on both SVG elements in local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Inline attributes cannot be overridden by missing CSS. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000080.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.2.81'; // FIX-SIDEBAR-MISSING-PAGES: Four admin pages were missing the left-hand sidebar navigation. cert_templates.php, cert_template_edit.php, trainer_dashboard.php, and usi_settings.php all called $OUTPUT->header() without the subsequent local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header() call. Added the nav header to each immediately after $OUTPUT->header(). suitability_form.php (pagelayout=embedded, public student token form) and student_usi_verify.php (AJAX endpoint) were correctly excluded. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000079.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.2.80'; // FIX-BULK-UNSUSPEND-PARAM: students.php read $action via optional_param('action','',PARAM_ALPHA). PARAM_ALPHA strips all non-letter characters including underscores — so 'bulk_unsuspend' was silently cleaned to 'bulkunsuspend', never matched the handler condition, and the page fell through with default filter=all (showing the full student list) while leaving every student still suspended. Fix: changed PARAM_ALPHA to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT which preserves underscores. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000078.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.2.79'; // FIX-USI-DETECT-PREVIEW-MISS: The "No USI codes detected in this file" banner was a false negative — detection correctly identified USI column position 149 (7 votes in the sample) but the success condition also required at least one USI to appear in the first 12 preview rows. In this Wisenet export the first 12 client records (IDs 2–13) have no USI recorded; the USI-bearing students (clients 14, 20, 24, 27) fall at rows 13, 19, 23, 26 — beyond the preview cap. Fix: success banner now triggers on a valid detected position alone ($usiDetected = $effUsiPos >= 0 || $effUsiPos === -2) regardless of $usiFound. When $usiFound === 0 in preview, the banner reads "no USI codes visible in the first N students previewed, but USIs will be read from the full file during import." so admins are correctly informed rather than misled into thinking the file has no USIs. Savepoint 2026053000077.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.2.78'; // BULK-UNSUSPEND-ROOT-CAUSE-FIX: Replaced the fragile JS hidden-form approach (dynamically built userids[] inputs — could silently POST nothing) with a native HTML form (#student-action-form) wrapping the student table. The existing students[] checkboxes now POST directly when "Activate Selected Accounts" is clicked — no JS input-building required. JS updated to call studentActionForm.submit() after confirm dialog. Server handler switched from optional_param_array("userids") to optional_param_array("students") to match the checkbox name, and from raw set_field() to user_update_user() to clear Moodle user cache after each update. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000076.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.2.74'; // NAT-SLIDER-INLINE-STYLE: Fixed intake card navigation. showCard() was toggling CSS class rtoc-card-active to control card visibility — some Moodle themes override class-based display rules (even with !important), causing cards to stay hidden after navigation. Fix: (1) Each card div now has style="display:none" set in PHP (not just CSS). (2) showCard() now uses direct inline style toggling (cards[prev].style.display='none'; cards[curr].style.display='block') instead of classList — inline styles have the highest specificity and cannot be overridden by any theme CSS. (3) Added null-checks on prevBtn/nextBtn before addEventListener to prevent a silent JS crash if a button element is missing for any reason. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000074. // NAT-IMPORT-UX-FIX: Step 3 enrollment wizard UX audit. (1) Removed duplicate "Step 3" labels from inside the content area — the stepper bar at the top already marks the current step; the explainer card h5 now reads "Enrol students into Moodle courses" (no "Step 3 —" prefix) and the instruction box header is now "Match each intake to a Moodle course category" (was "Step 3 of 3 — Enrol students into Moodle"). (2) Hidden the bottom "Confirm & Enrol Students" card by default in PHP (style="display:none") — previously PHP rendered it visible and JS hid it after page load, causing a confusing flash and leaving users unsure whether to click it or click Next. The slider's "Review & Enrol ✓" button (which Next becomes on the last intake card) now serves as the sole submit trigger; the bottom card remains in the DOM as a JS-absent fallback only. (3) Clarified instruction text: intro list now explicitly states that Previous/Next moves between intake cards (not wizard steps), and that Review & Enrol appears on the last card to confirm before anything is saved. (4) Relabelled the Next button from "Next →" to "Next intake →" (both in PHP initial render and in JS updateNav()) so it is unmistakably clear the button navigates between qualification intake cards, not to the next step of the import wizard. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000073. // SUSPENDED-CERTS-FIX: generate_qual_certs.php and generate_course_certs.php previously excluded suspended students from the completers list (AND u.suspended = 0 in both SOURCE 1 and SOURCE 2 queries). A student's academic achievement is not affected by their current account status — they should appear and be cert-eligible. Fix: removed u.suspended = 0 from all four completer queries; added u.suspended to SELECT (and GROUP BY where needed). Suspended students now show in the list with a red SUSPENDED badge and a per-row "Activate account" checkbox — if ticked when clicking Generate, the account is unsuspended before cert issuance. Students page: added BULK-UNSUSPEND action — when filtering by Suspended Accounts, an "Activate Selected Accounts" button appears in the bulk bar; selecting students and clicking it bulk-unsuspends them in one action with a confirm dialog. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000072. // FIX-QUAL-COMPLETION (v5.2.71): generate_qual_certs.php was only checking Moodle's course_completions table (requires completion tracking to be configured and triggered per course). Added SOURCE 2: plugin outcome records (local_rtocompliance_enrolments outcomeidentifier IN 20/51/60/81) — mirrors queue_autocert_if_all_units_complete() logic. Results from both sources are merged and de-duplicated. Guard now only exits early when BOTH no linked courses AND no unit codes exist. Students with 100% competent outcomes now appear correctly. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000071. // CERT-DELETE-FIX (v5.2.69): Fixed two bugs in delete_cert.php — (1) admin_settings_changed event trigger threw a PHP exception causing Moodle to return an HTML error page instead of JSON ("Unexpected token '<'"); removed event trigger, replaced with safe mtrace log. (2) Made revoke idempotent — if cert is already revoked return success instead of error. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000069. // SELECT-FIX (v5.2.68): Removed size="8" from the course picker <select> on generate_course_certs.php — the listbox was rendering always-open (8 rows visible) and overlaying the "Generate by Full Qualification" card. Now renders as a normal closed dropdown. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026053000068. // CERT-DELETE (v5.2.67): Added Delete button to the Issue Certificates screen — clicking Delete on any certificate shows a confirm dialog then soft-deletes (revokes) the record via delete_cert.php, removing it from the issued list while preserving the full record for audit. Also fixed language_statement sample/default text from "Issued in English." to "These unit/modules have been delivered and assessed in [insert language]." per AQF fact sheet feedback. Savepoint 2026053000067. // SLIDER-UI (v5.2.66): NAT import Step 3 enrolment wizard now shows one intake card at a time instead of all cards stacked. A Previous/Next nav bar sits above the cards with a counter ("Intake 2 of 5 — CIFF [2015 S1]") and coloured progress dots (green=matched, grey=skipped). On the last card "Next" becomes "Review & Enrol" which triggers the existing confirmation summary before submitting. The bottom submit button is hidden when JS is active and remains as a no-JS fallback. Intro instruction box updated to 3 steps matching the new slider flow. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052900066. // WIZARD-UX-FIX (v5.2.64): Fixed critical bug where pressing Enter in the category filter box submitted the doenrol form, accidentally enrolling all students. Fix: Enter key is now blocked in all search/filter inputs inside the wizard form (both via JS addEventListener and belt-and-braces onkeydown attribute). Added pre-submit confirmation dialog that lists every (programme + year/semester) → Moodle category mapping before any enrolment occurs — admins can review and cancel. Submit button now shows a live count of how many cards are mapped (e.g. "Confirm &amp; Enrol Students (3 qualifications selected)"). Added Step 3 intro alert explaining the workflow, total student count, and that Enter does not submit. Cards now use mb-4 spacing (was mb-3). Filter input and select dropdown widened to 600px. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052900064. NAT import Step 3 wizard now creates one card per (programme code + year/semester) combination instead of one card per programme code. A NAT file with CIFF students in both 2015 S1 and 2016 S2 now shows two separate cards — "CIFF [2015 S1]" and "CIFF [2016 S2]" — each mapped independently to the matching Moodle category (e.g. "TLI50816 / 2015 / Semester 1"). Automatch enhanced to prefer categories whose path contains both the qual code AND the year. Doenrol step now filters enrolled students by year/semester so only the correct intake's students are enrolled into each category. Yearsem badges now shown in amber/warning style for visual distinction. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052900063.
// QUAL-LABELS-NAT130 (v5.2.61): NAT import Step 3 now shows the national qualification code(s) from NAT00130 alongside each RTO programme code. For each programme code (e.g. CIFF) the card header now shows an arrow and the matching national qual code badge(s) (e.g. BSB20215) sourced from avetmiss_completion.qualcode joined via clientid. This makes each card immediately identifiable without requiring the admin to know what CIFF maps to. Unit code badges (from NAT00120) remain on Row 2. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052900061.
// QUAL-LABELS (v5.2.60): NAT import Step 3 enrolment wizard now shows the qualification name and unit codes alongside each program code. For each qualcode found in the NAT file the wizard now displays: (1) the qualification title from the Qualification Builder (local_rtocompliance_qualbuilder.qualificationname, matched by qualificationcode) or the unit name from local_rtocompliance_qualunits.unitname if the code is a unit-level programme; (2) all distinct unit codes found in NAT00120 for that programme identifier, each shown as a badge with its unit name if registered in the Qualification Units table. Three additional queries run once per wizard load (qualbuilder name map, qualunits name map, unit-codes-per-qualcode for the current import) — all wrapped in try/catch so the wizard degrades gracefully on installs where these tables have no data. Card header restructured: Row 1 retains program code badge + student count + automatch status; Row 2 (new) shows Qualification / Unit label and the unit code badges. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052900060.
// FIX-HIDDEN-CATEGORIES+AUTOMATCH-TYPE (v5.2.59): Two bugs fixed in NAT import Step 3 category picker. Bug 1 — removed visible=1 filter from course_categories query: admins doing a NAT import need ALL categories including ones hidden from students (visible=0), which RTOs commonly set to keep the course browser clean while still using them for enrolment; hidden categories now appear with a [hidden] suffix. Bug 2 — type comparison: $automatch was stored as a string (DB driver returns id as string on some MySQL drivers), then compared with int === string which always fails, so 'selected' was never applied and every dropdown showed 'Skip' even when auto-matched. Fixed by casting to (int) on assignment. Also added a live search/filter input above each select so admins can type to narrow down the category list. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052900059.
// FIX-UPGRADE-SAVEPOINTS (v5.2.58): Removed four bad marker savepoint blocks (v5.2.54-57) from upgrade.php that were added in descending order — Moodle executed them sequentially (057 first, then 056) causing a cannotdowngrade exception. No DB schema changes in v5.2.54-57 so no upgrade.php blocks are needed; Moodle advances the version number to 2026052900058 automatically. Sites stuck at DB version 2026052900057 from the partial upgrade will complete cleanly. No DB schema changes. Savepoint: none needed.
// SOA-LANDSCAPE-OVERFLOW (v5.2.57): Production-readiness pass. Statement landscape right-column footer overflowed page — cert.number h:5→4, cert.issuedate y:202→201 h:5→4, authenticity_measure y:207→205; bottom now 209mm (within 210mm A4 landscape). pluginConfig.ts version synced to 5.2.57. Marker savepoints added for v5.2.54/55/56/57. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052900057.
// ASQA-COMPLETION-AUDIT (v5.2.56): Final pass over all 8 certificate starter templates. authenticity_measure added to both completion starters (portrait + landscape) — the completion validator has authenticityMeasure in recommended_fields and REQUIREMENT_TO_DYNAMICKEY maps it to a canvas check, so omitting it triggered a warning on every new completion template. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052900056.
// ASQA-ORG-SEAL (v5.2.55): Second pass over all certificate starter templates. Four gaps fixed: (1) organisation_seal added to testamur landscape starter — required by validator (ASQA Practice Guide item 1(e)), placed in clear centre-bottom area. (2) organisation_seal added to testamur portrait starter — placed in 20mm gap between AQF statement and AQF logo. (3) organisation_seal added to statement portrait starter — placed below footer. (4) organisation_seal added to statement landscape starter — placed in clear centre band alongside signature footer. Also fixed: qualification.code and qualification.name catalogue required_for removed 'statement' entry — on a SoA unit codes/names appear inside the qualification.units table, not as separate fields; the statement validator does not check qualificationCode/qualificationName. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052900055.
// ASQA-RECORD-COMPLIANCE (v5.2.54): Full ASQA compliance audit of certificate template system against "Sample forms of AQF certification documentation" fact sheet. Three gaps in Record of Results validation fixed: (1) rto.code now REQUIRED for record (was recommended-only) — ASQA p.3 lists "RTO NAME, CODE and LOGO" as mandatory. (2) qualification.code and qualification.name now REQUIRED for record — ASQA p.3 requires "CODE and FULL TITLE of VET qualification". (3) signatory.title promoted to recommended for record. Dead settings.php entry for completionofcoursestatement (which the renderer auto-generates and ignores) replaced with a comment. Also: signatory.title added to both record starter templates (portrait and landscape). No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052900054.
// FIX-SELECT-ATTRS (v5.2.53): Fixed invalid HTML attribute construction in generate_course_certs.php filter bar. The "Filter by Group" and "Filter by Student" default <option> elements were built with a PHP ternary-as-array-key pattern that produced an empty-string attribute key ('' => '') when no filter was active. Moodle's html_writer renders this as ="" in the HTML, which triggers a visible debug warning in Moodle debug mode — the "display error". Fixed both options to use array_filter with a null value so the selected attribute is only included when the default option is actually selected. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052900053.
// FIX-EMAIL-BADGE (v5.2.52): Two fixes for the "Emailed" display on the Certificates page. (1) lib.php issuance-time notification path now saves emailsentdate = time() alongside emailsent = 1 — previously it only set emailsent, leaving emailsentdate = 0 which rendered as "1 Jan 1970". (2) certificates.php now displays a styled green pill badge ("✓ Emailed DD Mon YYYY") instead of plain muted text; legacy rows with emailsentdate = 0 fall back to today's date rather than showing epoch. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052900052.
// SOA-BANNER-POSITION (v5.2.51): Corrected ASQA analysis — the mandatory SoA banner ("A STATEMENT OF ATTAINMENT IS ISSUED BY...") appears at the VERY TOP of the SoA in the ASQA fact sheet p.4 layout (above RTO name/logo), not at the bottom. Moved not_a_testamur_statement to position 1 in the SoA settings section. Corrected lang string: field renamed to "Statement of Attainment banner (top of document)", description now explains it is a top banner, and default text corrected to remove "THIS IS NOT A TESTAMUR." which is not in the ASQA document. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052900051.
// SOA-SETTINGS-ORDER (v5.2.50): Reordered Statement of Attainment phrase settings top-to-bottom to match physical cert layout: (1) document heading, (2) intro phrase before student name, (3) attained phrase after student name, (4) NOT-A-TESTAMUR disclaimer at bottom. NOT-A-TESTAMUR is confirmed mandatory per ASQA fact sheet. SoA section heading updated to note settings follow document order. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052900050.
// SUBCATEGORY-FULLPATH (v5.2.49): NAT file autoenrol wizard now fetches ALL visible Moodle categories (including subcategories) and displays their full hierarchical path (e.g. "TLI50119 / 2015 / Semester 1") in the enrolment dropdown, so admins can distinguish subcategories from different qualifications. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052900049.
// SETTINGS-STRUCTURE-FIX (v5.2.48): Moved record_of_results_heading out of the Statement of Attainment phrases section into its own "Record of Results" sub-section. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052900048.
// SETTINGS-DESCRIPTIONS-FIX-2 (v5.2.47): All four mandatory phrase field descriptions now state only their own role — "text before/after student name" — with no duplication between fields. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052900047.
// SETTINGS-DESCRIPTIONS-FIX (v5.2.46): Removed cross-references to other cert types from all mandatory phrase field descriptions. Each field now only describes itself and quotes the correct ASQA fact sheet page and full example sentence. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052900046.
// CERT-TEMPLATE-SOA-FIELDS (v5.2.45): Fully wired soa_intro_statement and soa_attained_statement as first-class dynamic fields in the certificate template builder. (1) cert_template.php catalogue: added soa_intro_statement and soa_attained_statement to Mandatory phrases group (required_for=statement, forbidden_for=testamur); certify_statement/attained_statement marked forbidden_for=statement to prevent cross-type confusion; completionofcoursestatement sample updated to show qual code before "course". (2) SoA starter templates (portrait + landscape): replaced hardcoded static text fields for "This is a statement that" and "has attained" with dynamic soa_intro_statement and soa_attained_statement fields. (3) certificate_validator.php: soaIntroStatement and soaAttainedStatement added as required_fields for statement certtype and added to REQUIREMENT_TO_DYNAMICKEY map — validator now flags missing SoA phrase fields. (4) settings.php completionofcoursestatement label/desc updated to note field is auto-generated and value is ignored. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052900045.
// ASQA-AUDIT-2 (v5.2.44): (1) SoA settings heading — removed testamur comparison text, now reads per ASQA fact sheet p.4 only. (2) qualification.completionofcoursestatement — now auto-generated from cert data with qual code inserted before "course": "These competencies were attained in completion of {CODE} course in {NAME}." Previously a static admin-typed setting which could drift. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052900044.
// ASQA-AUDIT (v5.2.43): Full audit against ASQA Sample Forms of AQF Certification Documentation fact sheet. (1) BUG-FIX: skillsetstatement was added to wrong settings object ($settings not $certsettings) — silently missing from Certificate Settings page. (2) ADDED: soa_intro_statement field ("This is a statement that") — ASQA SoA p.4 uses different opening to testamur. (3) ADDED: soa_attained_statement field ("has attained") — ASQA SoA p.4 uses different attainment phrase to testamur. (4) Testamur/SoA phrase sections split into clearly labelled sub-headings. (5) ASQA fact sheet URL linked in section headers and mandatoryphrasesheading_desc. (6) certify_statement and attained_statement descriptions updated to clarify testamur-only. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052900043.
// CERT-SETTINGS-SIDEBAR (v5.2.42): Certificate Settings, Plugin Settings, and Platform API Settings added to left-hand sidebar nav under Settings & Support section. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052900042.
// ARCHIVE-AUTOCERT-FIX (v5.2.41): queue_autocert_if_all_units_complete()
// was blind to archive courses — it queried qualunits.courseid (primary courses only) so completing an
// archive semester course never triggered qualification-completion detection, programoutcome was never set,
// and auto-certificates were never issued. Added fallback lookup via qualunit_courses junction table,
// matching the same pattern already used in process_enrolment_created(). No DB changes. Savepoint 2026052800041.
// ARCHIVE-COURSE-AUTOENROL (v5.2.39/v5.2.40): NAT import auto-enrol
// wizard now enrols students into archive semester courses linked via Qual Builder
// (qualunit_courses junction table). Pre-fetches all archive links once; wires archive courses
// into instanceByCourse/enrolledByCourse for zero per-student DB queries. NAT completion
// outcomes applied to archive courses via unit code matching. Result message shows archive count.
// Step 3 wizard shows info notice when archive links are active. diagLog gains archive_course_count.
//
// CRITICAL FIX (v5.2.40): process_enrolment_task.php was not resolving qual units for archive
// courses — their IDs live in qualunit_courses.courseid, not qualunits.courseid — so
// local_rtocompliance_enrolments records were never created for archive course enrolments,
// meaning archive enrolments were invisible in Student Records and missing from NAT exports.
// Fix: after the primary qualunits query returns empty, also query qualunit_courses to find the
// parent qual unit and rewrite courseid to the archive course ID before inserting.
// Also: pre-fetch SQL gains AND qu.courseid IS NOT NULL guard; $unitCodesInCat deduplicated
// (archive courses share unit codes with primary courses).
// No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052800040.
// FIX-SUSPENDED-ACCOUNTS (v5.2.38): Student Records now shows suspended users
// under a new "Suspended Accounts" filter with an Unsuspend button to re-activate them.
// FIX-SOA-SESSION-500 (v5.2.38): soa_issue.php was returning HTTP 500 because
// get_credit_balance() called write_close() before $OUTPUT->header() — session
// was closed before Moodle could write cookies; moved credit fetch to after header.
// Also added raise_memory_limit(MEMORY_HUGE) before the 10k-user query and wrapped
// the credit call in try/catch so any API failure degrades gracefully.
// FIX-MANDATORY-WORDING (v5.2.38): Certificate mandatory ASQA phrases
// (certify_statement, attained_statement, statement_of_attainment_heading,
// record_of_results_heading, not_a_testamur_statement) are now configurable
// in Admin > Local plugins > AI RTO Compliance > Certificate Settings.
// Leave blank to use built-in ASQA defaults. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052700038.
// ARCHIVE-COURSE-LINKING (v5.2.37): New local_rtocompliance_qualunit_courses junction
// table links each Qual Builder unit to multiple Moodle courses (primary + archive semesters).
// Observer now triggers AVETMISS record creation for enrolments in ANY linked archive course.
// Qual Builder Course Linking page gains an "Archive Courses" section per unit for add/remove.
// Archive Linking Wizard in data_import.php reads intake_groups.json from Wisenet NAT ZIPs and
// auto-scores Moodle category matches for each semester group, presenting admin approve/skip cards.
// Wisenet Converter gains semester/intake grouping in the converter lib and an Intakes tab in the
// UI, plus intake_groups.json export in the ZIP for the Wizard to consume. DB savepoint 2026052700037.
// ARCHIVE-COURSE-PICKER (v5.2.36): generate_course_certs.php picker now groups all
// courses by Moodle category path (Parent > Category) with live search, so archive courses
// are visible and organised. Added sibling-course switcher to the student-page filter bar
// so admins can jump between archive periods without returning to the picker.
// was filtering enrolments with AND e.status = 'completed', but enrolments default to status='active'
// and many never get promoted to 'completed' even when their AVETMISS outcome is finalised
// (e.g. outcome 20 set via NAT import or manual grading). A competent outcomeidentifier IS the
// authoritative completion signal — status='completed' was an incorrect extra gate. Fixed by
// replacing the filter with status != 'withdrawn' so withdrawn enrolments are still excluded
// but active/hold/completed enrolments with competent outcomes (20/51/60/81) are correctly
// surfaced in Issue Certificate. Root cause of tester report: "no CO results" shown for
// Jasman Lew even though NAT120.txt clearly listed her units as outcome 20.
// No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052600035.
// FIX-FULLNAME-DEBUG-WARNINGS (v5.2.31): generate_course_certs.php "Filter by Student" selector was printing Moodle debug warnings "The following name fields are missing from the user object: firstnamephonetic, lastnamephonetic, middlename, alternatename" for every student in the dropdown. Root cause: both SQL queries that populate $allcompleters (course_completions path and local_rtocompliance_enrolments fallback path) only SELECT firstname, lastname, email — Moodle's fullname() function requires the four additional phonetic/middle/alternate name columns to suppress the debug output. Fix: added firstnamephonetic, lastnamephonetic, middlename, alternatename to both SELECT statements. FIX-TIMEOUT-DOENROL (v5.2.31): "Confirm & Enrol Students" threw "Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded" in mysqli_native_moodle_database.php during large NAT file processing (many students x many courses). The doenrol POST handler had no PHP time-limit extension. Fix: added \core_php_time_limit::raise(600) + raise_memory_limit(MEMORY_HUGE) at the top of the doenrol handler. FIX-TIMEOUT-TASK (v5.2.31): Same 30s timeout hit in adhoc_task.php execute() when process_enrolment_task processed large enrolment batches. Fix: added \core_php_time_limit::raise(300) at the top of execute(). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052500031. // FIX-DUPKEY-DERIVEDATE (v5.2.26): Completions tab derived-date lookup used get_records_sql() with clientid as first column — not unique (one student has multiple units per import) — causing Moodle debug warning "Duplicate value found in column clientid" on the Completions tab. Also silently dropped all but the last row per student, causing incorrect derived completion dates. Fix: switched to get_recordset_sql() + close() which streams rows with no uniqueness requirement. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052400027. // FIX-DUPKEY-NAMEMAP (v5.2.25): get_records() for avetmiss_student name-map used clientid as first column — not unique across imports — causing Moodle debug warning "Duplicate value found in column clientid" to appear in the Completions tab UI after a NAT data import. Fix: added id as the first selected column so the primary key is used as the PHP array key; the foreach loop already de-dupes by clientid via isset($nameMap[$numId]). REMOVE-COURSE-COLUMN (v5.2.25): Student enrolments table (Student AVETMISS Profiles → Enrolments) showed both a "Course" column and a "Unit of Competency" column containing the same data. Removed the redundant "Course" column; table now shows Unit of Competency, Activity Start Date, Outcome, Status, and Actions only. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052400026. // FIX-NAT00010-RTONAME-50CHAR + FIX-METHOD1/2-10CHAR-FALLBACK (v5.2.23): (1) NAT00010 rtoname field: parser read 50 chars (pos 10-59) — truncating org names longer than 50 chars (e.g. "Australian Institute of Professionals (AIP) Pty Ltd" became "...Pty Lt"). Fixed: now reads 100 chars (substr(10,100)) so any reasonable org name is captured. (2) NAT00080 USI Methods 1 and 2 were missing the 10-char fallback fix that Method 0 received in v4.9.166 (FIX-METHOD0-10CHAR-FALLBACK). Standard 327-char files have a 10-char USI at pos 149 immediately followed by a 2-char check-digit suffix (e.g. "MNJ4UPAPDX05"). The 12-char read failed /[2-9A-HJ-NP-Z]{10,12}/ because digits 0 and 5 are excluded from the USI charset — Method 1 returned null when auto-detection wasn't available (preview with usiPos=-1 or detection returning -1). Fix: applied identical elseif 10-char fallback to both Method 1 (pos 149) and Method 2 (pos 90). FIX-NAT00120-VENDOR-PREFIX (v5.2.22): CRITICAL — ALL 158-char NAT00120 files (Wisenet/modern SMS exports) have a non-standard extra 10-char Training Organisation Identifier prepended at pos 0–9, shifting every standard AVETMISS 8.0 field +10 bytes. The parser was reading clientid from pos 10–19 (the delivery location ID, e.g. "000002") instead of the actual student ID at pos 20–29 (e.g. "0000057272"), unitcode from pos 20–31 (digits+letters garbage), qualcode from pos 32–41 (wrong), and dates from wrong positions. Additionally, these files place 3 vendor flag bytes ("YNN" = VETiS/Y/N flags) between end date and outcome, placing outcome at pos 71–72 (not pos 58–59). Detection: if standard start-date at pos 42–49 is not a valid DDMMYYYY but pos 52–59 IS valid, activate +10-shifted parse path. Confirmed across 5 independent vendor files (4 datasets, 2 RTOs). Outcome read from pos 71–72, funding from pos 73–75, study reason from pos 96–97. FIX-HOURS-TRAILING-I (v5.2.22): end-of-line hours fallback now strips trailing vendor indicator byte 'I' (e.g. "...0010I") before reading last 4 digits — previously the 'I' blocked the ctype_digit check and hours were always null for 158-char files. No DB schema changes. No AMD changes. Savepoint 2026052300023. // FIX-2CHAR-DM-OUTCOME / FIX-HOURS-ENDOFLINE / FIX-NAT00130-SHORT-FORMAT (v5.2.21): Three NAT file parser bugs fixed after byte-level audit of actual vendor NAT files. (1) FIX-2CHAR-DM-OUTCOME: when pos 58-59 contained a code that is simultaneously a valid delivery mode (10=Internal, 20=External, 30=Workplace, 40=Combination, 90=Other) AND a valid outcome code, the secondary check stored the delivery-mode code as the outcome for every record — 111,000+ enrolments imported with outcome "10" (Not Commenced) or "90" (Not Applicable) instead of their real result (20=Competent, 30=Not Yet Achieved, 51=RPL, 60=Credit Transfer). Fix: when raw58 is in DELIVERY_MODE_CODES AND raw60 is in OUTCOME_CODES, treat raw58 as the 2-char delivery mode and raw60 as the actual outcome. (2) FIX-HOURS-ENDOFLINE: some vendors (confirmed in 142-char line format) place attended hours immediately after the outcome at pos 62-65 and carry nominal hours as the last 4 non-space characters of the record (pos 128-131). The standard positional reads (pos 132/136 for DM=2) return null for these files — every record got null supervised hours. Fix: end-of-line fallback strips trailing whitespace and reads the last 4 chars if they are all-digit and non-zero. Does not affect vendors where standard positions succeed. (3) FIX-NAT00130-SHORT-FORMAT: some vendor SMS systems emit a compact 35-char NAT00130 format (collection year 4N at pos 30-33, successful completion flag Y/N at pos 34) instead of the standard 8D completion date. The parser read 8 chars from pos 30 and stored "2016Y" (year + flag + padding) as the completiondate — a non-date string that could never be parsed. Fix: detect short format by line length (< 38 chars) and extract only the 4-digit year. No DB schema changes. No AMD changes. Savepoint 2026052300022. // BUG-NAT120-3CHAR-DM (v5.2.19): NAT00120 parser misidentified the 3-char AVETMISS delivery mode field as an outcome code, causing all students from vendors using the full 3A delivery mode field (e.g. "10 " = Internal/Classroom right-padded) to be imported with outcome "10" (Not Commenced) instead of their real competency outcome. Root cause: the AVETMISS 8.0 spec defines the Delivery Mode Identifier as 3A (3 chars), but the parser only probed 2 chars. When pos 58-59 = "10" (a valid delivery mode code), and "10" is also a valid outcome code (Not Commenced), the parser stored "10" as the outcome and the real outcome at pos 61-62 ("20" = Competency Achieved) was never read. Fix: added 3-char delivery mode detection BEFORE the existing 2-char outcome check. If pos 60 is exactly ' ' (the 3-char DM right-pad), pos 58-59 is in the delivery mode codes set {10,20,30,40,90}, and pos 61-62 is a valid outcome code, the parser now treats pos 58-60 as a 3-char delivery mode and reads the outcome from pos 61-62. All downstream field positions (funding source, study reason, hours attended, hours scheduled) shift by 3 instead of 2 for the 3-char DM case. Added 1 parser test: nat00120_3char_dm_outcome20. No DB schema changes. No AMD changes. Savepoint 2026052300020 (marker only). // BUG-NAT90-PERIOD-FILTER / BUG-NAT100-PERIOD-FILTER / BUG-NAT130-DEDUP-MAXID (v5.2.18): Three AVETMISS generator correctness bugs fixed. (1) generate_nat00090(): no reporting-period filter — all students with disabilityflag='Y' were exported regardless of period, causing NCVER referential integrity failures when out-of-period clientids appeared in NAT00090 but not NAT00080. Fix: added EXISTS subquery (same pattern as NAT00080/NAT00085) to restrict to period-active students only. (2) generate_nat00100(): same class of bug — all students with prioreducationflag='Y' exported without period filter, causing identical NCVER referential integrity failures. Fix: same EXISTS period filter. (3) generate_nat00130(): dedup JOIN used MAX(id) AS max_id and MAX(activityenddate) AS max_enddate as independent aggregates in a single GROUP BY subquery. When a student has two completion rows for the same program with DIFFERENT activityenddate values, MAX(id) and MAX(activityenddate) can belong to different rows — the JOIN on max_id then selects the row with the OLDER date, emitting the wrong completion date (and wrong programid/outcome fields) to NCVER. Fix: replaced the GROUP BY dedup JOIN with a NOT EXISTS correlated subquery implementing the correct "latest activityenddate; highest id as tiebreak for equal dates" logic. No DB schema changes. No AMD changes. Savepoint 2026052300019 (marker only). // BUG-GENERATOR-CODED-DEFAULTS-5.2.17: Three AVETMISS generator fields used ?? '' / ?? 'N' (null-coalescing only) instead of ?: '<code>' (falsy-coalescing), meaning a null OR empty-string DB value produced space-padded output — not a valid AVETMISS coded value — causing NCVER AVETMISS Data Quality Report validation failures. Fixed: (1) studyreason in generate_nat00120 (pos 97-98): ?? '' → ?: '@@' (not-stated code per AVETMISS 8.0). (2) feeexemption in generate_nat00120 (pos 123-124): ?? '' → ?: '@@'. (3) surveycontactstatus in generate_nat00080 (pos 327): ?? 'N' → ?: 'N'. FIX-TABDELIM-SEX-AT-5.2.17: In the tab-delimited NAT00080 parse path, sex code '@' (AVETMISS "not stated") was stored as null instead of '@', causing a false-positive 'sex_not_stated' data-issue flag for every student in a tab-delimited import whose gender is legitimately not stated. The fixed-width path has always stored '@' correctly. Fix: aligned the tab-delimited path to use in_array(['M','F','X','@']) ? $sc : null, exactly matching the fixed-width path. No DB schema changes. Added 2 parser tests: nat00080_tabdelim_sex_at, nat00120_generator_coded_fields (now 16 parser tests total). // FIX-OUTCOME-41-DETECTION-5.2.16: Outcome code '41' (Satisfactorily Completed – VETiS/school-based) was missing from the static $AVETMISS_OUTCOME_CODES parser detection array (data_import.php). Same class of bug as missing '10' fixed in v5.2.11. For vendor-format NAT00120 files where a 2-char Delivery Mode field is inserted at pos 58-59 (pushing the outcome to pos 60-61), the in_array() check at parse line 813 could not match '41' — the parser fell through to the raw-value branch and stored the delivery mode string (e.g. 'AA') as the outcome instead. VETiS/school-based students with outcome '41' had their outcome silently corrupted after import. Fix: added '41' to $AVETMISS_OUTCOME_CODES (now all 15 AVETMISS 8.0 codes are present). FIX-DEAD-TODAY8-5.2.16: Removed dead variable $today8 = date('dmY') in the Data Audit tab suspicious-outcome-10 section — it was defined but never used (the SQL 10 lines down correctly uses date('Ymd') directly). FIX-STALE-COMMENT-5.2.16: Updated stale comment in COMPETENT_OUTCOMES block that still listed '52' in the code description. Added 1 new parser test: nat00120_outcome41_vendor (standard-format '41' at pos 58, vendor-format '41' at pos 60 with delivery mode 'AA' at pos 58, and completeness check that all 15 AVETMISS codes are in the detection array). No DB schema changes. // FIX-52-RPL-NOT-GRANTED-5.2.15: Removed outcome '52' (RPL Not Granted) from the doenrol $competent set and from $COMPETENT_OUTCOMES in the Completions tab derived-date logic. A student who was DENIED RPL has not demonstrated competency and must not be marked as having completed the course in Moodle. Also added 8 parser round-trip tests: nat00080_standard_fields, nat00080_usi_positions, nat00085_field_positions, nat00120_extended_fields (funding/study-reason/hours), nat00120_sentinel_handling (@ values), nat00120_short_line_guard, nat00130_field_positions, doenrol_competent_set (audits the live competent set and will PASS now that '52' is removed). No DB schema changes. // FIX-OUTCOME-BADGE-COLORS-5.2.14: outcome 20 (Competency Achieved) was showing badge-danger (red) and outcome 40 (Withdrawn) was showing badge-success (green) — the same 20/40 swap fixed for labels in v5.2.13. Fixed badge colour map: 20=success,41=success,51=success,53=success,60=success,61=success,81=success,85=success; 30=danger,52=danger; 40=warning,82=warning; 10=secondary,70=secondary,90=secondary. Added outcome 53 (RCC Granted) to map (was falling through to secondary). Added Data Audit tab to the import detail view showing: outcome code distribution with bar chart, unrecognised code alerts, suspicious outcome-10 records where end date has passed, field completeness report, and qualification code summary. Added 5 NAT00120 parser round-trip test cases to the Testing Engine under category 'AVETMISS Import Parser': nat120_outcome_codes (all 15 codes at standard byte pos), nat120_vendor_format (vendor pos 60), nat120_field_positions (all field byte positions), nat120_badge_colors (semantic colour mapping), nat120_import_db (live DB outcome code sanity check). // FIX-OUTCOME-LABELS (v5.2.13): Outcome labels for codes 20/30/40 were swapped. Code 20 (Competency Achieved) was labelled "Competency Not Achieved", code 30 (Competency Not Yet Achieved) was labelled "Withdrawn", and code 40 (Withdrawn) was labelled "Competency Achieved". Fixed to match AVETMISS 8.0 standard. Added code '53' (RCC Granted) label. Added outcome code '41' (Satisfactorily Completed, VETiS school-based) and '85' (Non-assessable Satisfactorily Completed) to the doenrol competent-outcome set and to the Completions tab derived-date set — previously these outcome codes did not trigger Moodle course_completions writes or completion-date derivation. No DB schema changes. // FIX-AUTOENROL-USERNAME-COLLISION (v5.2.12): "Confirm & Enrol Students" crashed with a MySQL duplicate-key error (Duplicate entry '1-<clientid>' for key 'mdl_user_mneuse_uix') when a student's username already existed in Moodle from a previous import run or a manually-created account, but the earlier lookup maps (by idnumber/email) had not matched them. The create path called user_create_user() unconditionally, hitting the unique constraint on (mnethostid, username). Fix: added a direct $DB->get_record('user', ['username'=>$lcClientid]) pre-check immediately before user_create_user(). If the account already exists, the plugin reuses it and jumps straight to Phase 3 (enrolment) — exactly the same recovery path used for the email-collision fix added in v4.9.173. Added a belt-and-suspenders catch-block recovery: if user_create_user() still throws a duplicate-key exception (race condition), the catch now checks whether the exception is for the mneuse_uix key, does a DB lookup by username, and continues to Phase 3 rather than silently skipping the student. No DB schema changes. // FIX-DOENROL-DUPKEY-2 (v5.2.8): v5.2.6 converted the USI and enrolment-map queries to get_recordset_select() but three more get_records()/get_records_sql() calls in the doenrol handler still selected clientid as the first column — (1) the studentNameMap/studentDetailsMap bulk load, (2) the cross-import name fallback query, (3) the studentEmailMap load. All three crash with "Duplicate value found in column clientid" when the NAT staging table contains more than one row with the same clientid. Fixed all three by switching to get_recordset_select()/get_recordset_sql() with explicit close(). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052300009. // DERIVE-COMPLETION-DATE (v5.2.7): Completions tab now derives the qualification completion date from the latest satisfactorily-completed unit end date in NAT00120 (AVETMISS outcomes 20/51/52/53/60/61/81/85) when the NAT00130 file has blank completion dates — standard RTO practice, completion date = date of last passing unit outcome. Derived dates display in italic with a tooltip to distinguish from authoritative NAT00130 dates. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052300008. // FIX-DOENROL-DUPKEY (v5.2.6): "Confirm & Enrol Students" crashed with Moodle debugging error "Duplicate value found in column clientid" when any student clientid appeared more than once in the NAT staging tables. Root cause: get_records_select() uses the first selected column as the PHP array key — selecting 'clientid, usi' from avetmiss_student (where the same student can appear twice from a malformed NAT file) and selecting 'clientid, unitcode, outcome, enddate' from avetmiss_enrolment (where clientid is inherently non-unique — one row per unit per student) both trigger the fatal duplicate-key check. Fix: both queries switched to get_recordset_select() which streams rows as a forward-only cursor with no uniqueness requirement. USI map keeps the first non-empty USI found per clientid. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052200007. // FIX-ZEROS-DATE (v5.2.5): Completions tab — completion date and certificate date columns now display italic "not recorded" when the date is absent, matching the existing parchmentNumber style. Also maps AVETMISS all-zeros dates (00000000) to "not recorded" in addition to the existing @-sentinel. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052200006. // NAT-FIX-5.2.4: Fixed three root-cause bugs that caused all students to show "not completed" on generate_course_certs.php after a NAT import + auto-enrol run. (1) NAT00120 parser: Program Identifier was read as 10 chars (should be 12 per AVETMISS 8.0 spec), shifting startdate/enddate/outcome all 2 bytes early — outcome landed in the enddate field and was never a valid outcome code. Fixed: qualcode=substr(32,12), startdate=substr(44,8), enddate=substr(52,8), outcome detected at pos 60. (2) Delivery Mode auto-detect: vendor SMS files (Velixio, older Wisenet) insert a 2-char Delivery Mode field at pos 60–61 before the outcome, pushing it to 62–63. Auto-detection: if pos 60–61 is not a recognised AVETMISS outcome code but pos 62–63 is, treat 60–61 as delivery mode and read outcome from 62–63. All subsequent fields (funding source, study reason, hours) shift accordingly. (3) doenrol NAT-COMPLETION: doenrol now writes a {course_completions} record when a student is enrolled into a course whose idnumber matches a unit code with a competent NAT outcome (20/51/52/53/60/61/81). End date from NAT file used as timecompleted. This populates the completion table that generate_course_certs.php queries. (4) generate_course_certs.php fallback: when {course_completions} is empty, falls back to querying local_rtocompliance_enrolments JOIN students JOIN user for the course idnumber+competent outcomes. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052200005. // QUAL-CERT-DISCOVERY (v5.2.3): The "Generate Certificates by Course" picker page (generate_course_certs.php) previously only showed a single-unit-of-competency selector with no mention of the full-qualification option. Users landing on that page had no way to discover generate_qual_certs.php. Fixed: replaced the single-option picker with a two-card layout showing "Generate by Unit of Competency" (blue border, existing course dropdown) and "Generate by Full Qualification" (green border, direct link to generate_qual_certs.php with description of Testamur + RoR output). Symmetrically updated generate_qual_certs.php picker: clearer heading, green "Go" button, and a blue crosslink panel at the bottom pointing back to the unit-by-unit page. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052200004. // FIX-SOA-500 (v5.2.2): Fixed HTTP 500 error on soa_issue.php (Issue Multi-Unit SOA page). Two root causes: (1) PHP 7.3 incompatibility — soa_compliance_engine.php used an arrow function fn() (PHP 7.4+ syntax) which caused a fatal parse error at include-time on PHP 7.3 / Moodle 3.11 sites. Fixed by replacing with a traditional anonymous function. Same fix applied to soa_ajax.php (two additional arrow functions). (2) Capability gap in settings.php — local_rtocompliance_soa_issue admin external page was only registered for users with :manage or :viewall, but not :issuecerts. Any custom role with only :issuecerts would cause admin_externalpage_setup() to throw a coding_exception (500). Fixed by adding :issuecerts to the $canviewfull condition. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052200003. // FIX-USI-FROM-NAT (v5.2.1): Fixed root cause of all students showing "Missing" in the Student Records USI column after a NAT import + auto-enrol run. Root cause: the doenrol handler in data_import.php matched NAT students to Moodle accounts and enrolled them, but NEVER transferred the USI from the NAT staging table (local_rtocompliance_avetmiss_student.usi) to the live student profile (local_rtocompliance_students.usi). process_enrolment_task then created every new profile with usi='' (empty), so all students showed "Missing" regardless of what was in the NAT file. Fix: three additions to the doenrol handler — (1) pre-load a clientid→USI map from the staging table; (2) record each resolved userid→USI pair at the phase3: label; (3) after the enrolment loop, batch-upsert USI values into local_rtocompliance_students (update if profile exists with empty USI; pre-create a minimal profile if the task hasn't run yet, with a duplicate-key safety catch for race conditions). Existing USIs (already present or verified) are never overwritten. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052200002. // GEN-BY-QUAL (v5.2.0): Two bugs fixed in the Generate Certificates feature. (1) FIX-ONCLICK-QUOTES: "Go to Course" button was completely broken — json_encode() wraps the base URL in double quotes which immediately terminated the onclick="" HTML attribute, so window.location was never assigned. Fixed: single-quote JS string literals with htmlspecialchars(). (2) GEN-BY-QUAL: Added "Generate by Qualification" button and modal to certificates.php. New generate_qual_certs.php page lets RTO staff select an active qualification from the Qualification Builder and bulk-issue Testamur + Record of Results for all students who completed every linked unit-of-competency course. Supports force-regenerate and email notification toggles. Registered in settings.php and lang strings added. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052200001. // ONE-CARD-LEFT-PANEL (v5.1.8): Left panel redesigned as a single scrollable card. Previously each section was its own bordered box making the panel look fragmented and breaking scroll. Now .rtoc-tmpl-left IS the single white card (border + border-radius + overflow-y:auto). Each .rtoc-panel-section is transparent with no border/overflow. Sections are separated by a thin 1px divider line only between adjacent sections. Section headings are small grey uppercase labels inline within the flow. CSS-only. Savepoint 2026052100018. // LEFT-PANEL-INPUT-FIX (v5.1.7): Left-panel inputs (Template name, Orientation, Background colour, all form-controls) were inheriting the global plugin rule of border-radius:16px, font-size:1rem, min-height:2.75rem — making them look oversized and pill-shaped. Added .rtoc-tmpl-left scoped overrides to restore compact sizing (border-radius:4px, font-size:0.83rem, padding:5px 8px). Also fixed search field: the global input[type="text"] rule was trampling the icon-aware left-padding (34px) — added higher-specificity override to restore it. CSS-only. Savepoint 2026052100017. // FLAT-LEFT-PANEL (v5.1.6): All five accordion sections in the certificate template editor left panel (Fields, Page Design, Branding, Template Info, Quick Guide) replaced with always-visible flat sections. Section headings use a compact labelled header bar; all content is immediately visible in the single scrollable left column — no expand/collapse interaction required. Body padding increased to 16px sides / 20px bottom throughout; left-panel gap increased to 10px. The 58vh height cap on the field palette body has been removed. Savepoint 2026052100016. // CERT-REGISTRY-WIRING (v5.1.1): Two gaps in the v5.1.0 registry wiring fixed. (1) FORCE-REGEN-SUPERSEDE: generate_course_certs.php force-regen path now calls local_rtocompliance_update_registry_status($existingcert->verifytoken, 'superseded') after voiding the old cert — previously scanning an old cert QR after a force-regen would show "Valid" instead of "Superseded". New helper function local_rtocompliance_update_registry_status() added to lib.php (best-effort, same pattern as publish helper). (2) SAMPLE-URL-FIX: cert_template_renderer.php sample_payload() was returning hardcoded https://example.com/verify/ URLs for all three cert types (testamur/statement/record, completion, and shared authenticity_measure). These are now dynamically built from get_config('local_rtocompliance', 'apiurl') so template designers see the real essaygradeai.app/verify/ URL format in the canvas editor preview. PHP-only. No DB or AMD changes. Savepoint 2026052100011. // CERT-REGISTRY-PUBLIC (v5.1.0): Central certificate verification registry. Moodle now publishes every issued certificate to the AI Grader platform registry at issuance time (both issue_certificate.php and programmatic_issue_cert in lib.php). QR codes on printed PDFs now point to essaygradeai.app/verify/<token> instead of the local Moodle verify.php — so employers and auditors can scan a certificate QR code and land on a stable, neutral verification page regardless of whether the issuing RTO's Moodle server is online. PHP: new local_rtocompliance_publish_cert_to_registry() helper in lib.php; cert_template_renderer.php verify URL changed to platform URL. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026052100010. // SUBTLE-REQ-BADGE (v5.0.9): Certificate template field palette — required-field indicator changed from a bold red "req" text badge to a small 13px red circle with a white exclamation mark. The pink background tint on required chips removed so chips look uniform; only the small dot signals required status. CSS+PHP only. No AMD or DB changes. // QR-CODE-PREVIEW (v5.0.8): Certificate template canvas editor now renders a live QR code image for the Verification QR code field instead of the unhelpful '[QR]' text stub. Uses the free qrserver.com API with the sample verify URL so the designer sees exactly what will print on the certificate. QR field also now defaults to a proper 25×25mm square and drops to the bottom-right corner of the page (sensible default for cert layouts). All three AMD files updated. No DB schema changes. // DRAG-DROP-SMART-SIZE (v5.0.7): Certificate template canvas editor — field palette chips are now draggable. Drag any chip from the left panel and drop it precisely onto the canvas; the field appears centred on the drop point. Click-to-add still works. Smart sizing: field width is measured via Canvas 2D measureText() so the box fits the text content. Fields without a starter-template position now default to centre-aligned (align=C) and are centred horizontally on the page. Height auto-calculated from font size (~1.8 line-heights). Click-to-add cascades vertically below the lowest existing field instead of stacking at x:30,y:30. Lines span the full page width minus 5mm margins. All three AMD files (src, build, build/min) updated. CSS: .rtoc-palette-chip gets cursor:grab; canvas shows a dashed blue dragover outline. PHP: draggable=true + helpful title on every palette chip. No DB schema changes. No PHP logic changes. // FIX-FIELD-TEXT-CLIP (v5.0.6): CSS-only fix for text clipping in the certificate template canvas editor. // FIX-FIELD-TEXT-CLIP (v5.0.6): Certificate template canvas editor — text inside field boxes was being clipped at the bottom border on all default text fields. Root cause: (1) line-height:1.1 was too tight for the rendered font — descenders (letters like g, y, p) and even normal baseline text extended below the line box and hit the overflow:hidden boundary of the field. (2) .rtoc-tmpl-field-inner also had overflow:hidden, compounding the clip. Fix: line-height raised from 1.1 to 1.3; bottom padding increased from 2px to 4px on .rtoc-tmpl-field; .rtoc-tmpl-field-inner changed to overflow:visible (clipping is already handled by the parent .rtoc-tmpl-field overflow:hidden). CSS-only change — no PHP, JS/AMD, or DB schema changes. // CERT-ISSUANCE-AUDIT (v5.0.5): Full end-to-end audit of the Issue Certificates feature. Seven bugs and wording issues fixed. (1) FIX-SENDEMAIL-RESPECTED: issue_certificate.php always called message_send() unconditionally — the "Notify Student" checkbox had no effect. Wrapped in if(!empty($data->sendemail)). (2) FIX-EMAILSENT-FLAG: issue_certificate.php never updated emailsent=1 after dispatching the Moodle notification, so certs issued manually always showed "Not emailed" in the Certificates list even when the notification was sent. Fixed: DB::set_field after successful message_send(). (3) FIX-SENDEMAIL-LABEL: checkbox description said "Send email with PDF attachment" which is incorrect — it sends a Moodle notification, not a PDF; the PDF email is a separate action. Corrected to "Send a Moodle notification to the student when the certificate is issued". (4) FIX-NAV-LINK: settings.php nav menu hardcoded courseid=1 (the Moodle site course) for the Generate Certificates menu item. Clicking the menu item landed on "No students have completed this course yet" instead of the course picker. Fixed: removed ['courseid'=>1] so the picker page loads. (5) FIX-HASCERT-SUPERSEDED: generate_course_certs.php hascert lookup included force-regenned (superseded) certs — rows where reissued_at IS NOT NULL — because status stays 'issued' for audit continuity. Students with a superseded old cert and a fresh new cert could show the old cert number. Fixed: added AND (reissued_at IS NULL OR reissued_at = 0) to the lookup query. (6) FIX-MODAL-URL: certificates.php "Generate by Course" modal button used a hardcoded /local/rtocompliance/ path in the onclick JS; breaks on subdirectory Moodle installs. Fixed: pre-computed via moodle_url and injected via json_encode. (7) FIX-GENERATE-TITLE: generate_course_certs.php page title, heading, and nav header all said "by Qualification" — incorrect because the page operates on a Moodle Course (= Unit of Competency), not a Qualification. The lang string and nav header both corrected to "by Course". No DB schema changes. No AMD changes. // FIX-CERT-TEMPLATE-EDITOR (v5.0.3): Six bugs in the certificate template editor fixed. (1) FIX-QR-AUTHENTICITY: QR code / verify.url fields now satisfy the ASQA authenticityMeasure requirement — previously adding a QR code still showed a false-positive ASQA error. (2) FIX-GRID-REPEAT: Show grid checkbox now works — CSS background-repeat:no-repeat was preventing gradient grid lines from tiling; JS applyGridStyle() now sets per-layer backgroundRepeat. (3) FIX-ORG-SEAL-UPLOAD: Organisation seal upload UI added to the Branding panel — BRANDING_ITEMID_ORG_SEAL and get_branding_org_seal_url() existed since v4.4.0 but no upload form was ever wired up. (4) FIX-ORG-SEAL-IMAGE: organisation_seal added to $imagekeys in cert_template_renderer.php — was silently falling through to empty text rendering in PDFs. (5) FIX-ORG-SEAL-PREVIEW: Organisation seal now rendered in canvas editor preview — brandingorgsealurl variable and previewTextFor() branch added to all three AMD JS files. (6) FIX-ORG-SEAL-JSDATA: brandingorgsealurl now passed from PHP to JS via RTOC_TMPL_DATA. No new DB schema changes. // BUG-ENCODING-NATIMPORT: ISO-8859-1 extended bytes (e.g. \xE9 = é) in student names caused MySQL dml_write_exception "Incorrect string value". local_rtocompliance_nat_lines() now runs mb_check_encoding() per line and converts non-UTF-8 lines from ISO-8859-1 via mb_convert_encoding(). UTF-8 files (the common case) are passed through unchanged. // BUG-MEMORY-NATIMPORT: raise_memory_limit(MEMORY_HUGE) at all three import entry points (parse_nat_group, save_nat_groups, upload handler, finalizenat handler); replaced file_get_contents()+preg_split() with local_rtocompliance_nat_lines() generator that streams tmppath files via fgets() — eliminates the duplicate full-file PHP array that caused OOM on imports with 10k+ students or 50k+ enrolment rows. // USI-12CHAR: AVETMISS 8.0 spec (Oct 2022) confirmed USI is at pos 149 (0-indexed) in 327-char records. Some SMS vendors export a 12-char USI field. USI extraction now reads up to 12 chars (rtrim to actual length) and validates [A-Z0-9]{10,12}. DB columns local_rtocompliance_students.usi and local_rtocompliance_usilog.usi widened to 15 chars. Comments updated to reflect correct AVETMISS 8.0 layout.
// See db/upgrade.php 2026051600208 for details.
// failed for a file batch ($effUsiPos = -1), the preview table's USI column header in the Step 2
// confirmation view rendered "(col -1)" — confusing for admins who had no idea what -1 meant.
// Fixed: display "(auto-fallback)" when the position is -1. No parser changes, no DB changes.
// Savepoint 2026051600202 (marker only). // FIX-NATIMPORT-SIXBUGFIX (v4.9.128): Six parser/import bugs fixed. (1) FIX-TIMESTAMP-GROUPING: group_by_timestamp() used exact 13-digit timestamps as keys — Wisenet puts different timestamps on each file in the same export, so NAT00080 and NAT00120 landed in separate imports (students unlinked from enrolments). Fix: round by /10,000,000 (~2.8 hr window) so all files from one session share one key. (2) FIX-STUDYREASON-STORED: parse_nat00120() extracted study reason (pos 96-97) but the DB insert and avetmiss_enrolment table had no studyreason column — value was silently discarded. Fix: add studyreason column + wire into insert. DB schema change: ADD COLUMN studyreason CHAR(2). Savepoint 2026051600198. (3) FIX-OUTCOME-LABEL-82: avetmiss_outcome_label() was missing code '82' = Non-Assessable Enrolment – Not Satisfactorily Completed; raw code was shown in UI. (4) FIX-PHONE-LANDLINES: NAT00085 phone regex /0[45]\d{8}/ only caught mobiles; landlines (02/03/07/08) were silently dropped. Widened to /0[2-578]\d{8}/. (5) FIX-COLLECTION-YEAR-ENDDATE: detect_collection_year() used start date year; AVETMISS 8 convention is end date year. Now uses enddate, falls back to startdate. (6) FIX-FUNDINGSOURCE-COMMENT: install.xml fundingsource comment listed pre-AVETMISS 8 abbreviations (FFS, VSL, CSO); updated to reflect 2-digit numeric codes (11=Commonwealth, 20=FFS, 31=NSW Smart&Skilled). // FIX-NAT00120-OUTCOME-LABELS (v4.9.127): Comprehensive audit of all NAT files in the attached Wisenet dataset (NAT00010, NAT00020, NAT00030A, NAT00060, NAT00080, NAT00090, NAT00100, NAT00120, NAT00130) confirmed all parsers correct. One UX bug found: outcome code labels map was missing two codes used heavily in real data. (1) ADD-LABEL-41: Code "41" = Satisfactorily Completed — used by 19,534 of 22,147 NAT00120 records (88.3%) in the audited Wisenet VETiS dataset; previously displayed as raw "41" in the UI. "Satisfactorily Completed" is the standard AVETMISS VETiS outcome for school-based students who complete a unit of competency (analogous to "40 Competency Achieved" in workplace-based delivery). (2) ADD-LABEL-85: Code "85" = Non-Assessable Enrolment – Satisfactorily Completed — 125 records in dataset; this is the correct AVETMISS 8 label for outcome 85 per the NCVER specification (previously mislabelled as plain "Non-Assessable" under "81"). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051600197. // FIX-NAT00120-AVETMISS8-POSITIONS (v4.9.126): Three NAT00120 parsing bugs fixed against the authoritative AVETMISS 8 spec (Release 8.0, Nov 2016, field table page 35). (1) OUTCOME-VALID-LIST-TOO-NARROW: outcome identifier – national at pos 71 len 2 was filtered against a hard-coded list ['20','30','40','51','52','60','61','70','81','90'] which excluded Wisenet's code "41" (org-specific continuing/not-yet-graded marker) — result: $outcome always null for every Wisenet record. Fix: store raw 2-char value without a hard-coded filter. (2) FUNDING-SOURCE-WRONG-EXTRACTION: funding source – national at pos 73 len 2. AVETMISS 8 uses 2-digit numeric codes (11, 13, 20, 30 …). Previous code scanned entire line for legacy state-name tokens (FFS, QLD, WA …) which never appear in AVETMISS 8 files — result: $fundingsource always null. Fix: read from fixed position 73, length 2. (3) HOURS-ATTENDED-FRAGILE-REGEX: hours attended at pos 139 len 4 per spec; previous code used end-of-line regex /(\d{4})[A-Z]\s*$/ which matched scheduled hours (pos 153) + predominant delivery mode char "I" — correct by accident, fragile. Fix: read from pos 139 directly, fall back to scheduled hours (pos 153) if zero/blank. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051600196. // FIX-QUOTED-FIELD-DELIMITER (v4.9.123): NAT00130 import — some SMS exports use `"` as a field separator rather than fixed-width space-padding. After stripping the leading `"` (v4.9.122 fix), the name field is variable length and terminated by the next `"`. Previously the code assumed a fixed 50-char name (positions 10–59) then searched for sex+DOB from position 60 onward. Because names are short (e.g. 13 chars for "HORVATH, DAVID"), sex+DOB sat at position ~24 — well before the search start — causing sex=null, garbled DOB, and USI auto-detect returning -1. Fix: detect a `"` in the name area (positions 10–59 of the stripped line); if found, (a) truncate name at that `"`, and (b) begin the sex+DOB regex search immediately after it. The fallback fixed-position code is updated the same way: for quote-delimited format it reads sex at $searchStart and DOB at $searchStart+1 rather than the AVETMISS 8 fixed positions 62/72. Both local_rtocompliance_detect_nat00080_usi_pos() and local_rtocompliance_parse_nat00080() receive the same treatment so USI auto-detection and per-record parsing are consistent. Standard fixed-width AVETMISS files (no mid-line `"`) are unaffected — $searchStart defaults to 60 as before. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051500193. // FIX-NAT00080-NAT130-FALLBACK + FIX-NAT00080-QUOTED-CSV + FIX-NAT00080-STRICT-OVERRIDE (v4.9.122): Three NAT00080 import fixes for non-standard SMS exports. (1) NAT130-FALLBACK: Accept a file named NAT00130 as the student data source when no NAT00080 file is present in the upload batch — some SMS vendors label the client/student file NAT00130 instead of NAT00080. (2) QUOTED-CSV: Strip a leading double-quote character from each line before fixed-width parsing. Some vendors export quoted CSV where the opening `"` of the client ID field sits at position 0, shifting all field positions by 1 and garbling Name, DOB, and USI. (3) STRICT-OVERRIDE: When an admin manually enters a USI column position in the import preview UI, skip fallback Methods 1/2/3 (Wisenet pos 149, standard pos 90, DOB-anchored scan). Previously if the specified position held no valid USI the code silently fell through to a hard-coded fallback, making it appear the override had no effect. Now only the entered position is tried — if nothing is found there the preview shows Not found, giving honest feedback for the admin to adjust. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051400192. // UX-AUTOENROL-WIZARD: Combobox autocomplete, step progress bar, explainer card, post-enrolment banner. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051400191. // FIX-NAT00080-GENDER-AT: AVETMISS '@' sex/gender code ("not stated") was accepted by the regex ([MFX@]) but then discarded by in_array(['M','F','X']) at both parse paths — primary and fixed-position fallback. Result: any student record with '@' gender had sex=null, triggering sex_not_stated data-issue flag and showing a dash in the import preview. Fix: added '@' to the accepted set in both paths so $sex='@', $sexKnown=true, and the flag never fires. Preview table displays "Not stated" for '@' records instead of raw '@'. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051400186. // FIX-NAT00080-EXTENDED (v4.9.112): Fixed USI, DOB, and sex extraction for SMS exports (e.g. Wisenet) that embed address fields inside the NAT00080 record, producing lines far longer than the standard 101 chars. In these extended-format files the USI is no longer at fixed position 90–99 — it appears at the END of the record before Survey Contact Status. Fix (1) USI: try fixed position 90–99 first (standard AVETMISS 8); if what is found there does not start with an uppercase letter, fall back to scanning the last 30 chars of the stripped line and taking the RIGHTMOST 10-char uppercase-alphanumeric sequence — this is always the USI in both formats. Fix (2) Sex+DOB: replace independent fixed-position reads (sex=62, DOB=63–70) with a single pattern search for sex-code immediately followed by DDMMYYYY starting from position 50. The pattern ([MFX@])([0-3]d[0-1]d(19|20)dd) is constrained to year 19xx/20xx to prevent false matches in address text. Fixes garbled DOB display ('/ / 1') and wrong/missing USI on every student record in extended-format imports. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051400182. // FIX-NAT00080-AVETMISS8 (v4.9.111): Fixed three bugs in local_rtocompliance_parse_nat00080() that caused USI, DOB, and sex/gender to appear blank or flagged as missing on every NAT00080 import. (1) USI: the regex ([A-Z0-9]{10})99 never matched real USI values — AVETMISS 8 Field 16 (Survey Contact Status) is Y/N/@ not '99', so the match always failed. Fix: extract USI from fixed position 0-indexed 90–99 (AVETMISS 8 Field 15 spec), validate as 10 uppercase alphanumerics, retain regex only as fallback for non-standard exports. (2) Sex: AVETMISS 8 introduced 'X' (intersex/unspecified) alongside 'M'/'F'; '@' means not-stated. Plugin only accepted 'M'/'F', flagging all 'X' and '@' records as sex data issues. Fix: accept M/F/X as known values, treat '@' as not-stated (valid, no error). (3) DOB: added BOM and trailing-\r stripping for Windows-exported files; '@'-padded not-stated DOBs ('@@@@@@@@') now correctly stored as null without triggering a spurious dob data-issue flag. Data-issue flags refined: usi_missing, dob_not_stated, sex_not_stated. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051400181. // FIX-SMART-DETECT-BANNER (v4.9.109): generate_course_certs.php Smart Detection banner replaced with light-background readable design. Was: dark navy rtoc-clause-banner with low-contrast coloured text. Now: white/light-blue card with dark text, green pill for Nationally Recognised, blue pill for cert type, dark-on-light for Detection Reason and Qualification. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051400179. // STUDENT-DOC-REPOSITORY (v4.9.108): Central student document & certificate portal. New pages: mydocs.php (student-facing portal combining issued certs + teacher-uploaded documents), student_docs_download.php (Moodle file API download handler). New DB table: local_rtocompliance_student_docs (userid, uploaderid, doctype, notes, filename, filesize, mimetype, contextid). Student can view their own docs; admins/trainers with issuecerts or viewall can upload/delete. Eight doc types: RPL decision, USI letter, suitability assessment, credit transfer, enrolment agreement, third-party workplace record, AVETMISS export, other. Also: qualbuilder_results.php gains "Docs & Certs" action button per student row linking to mydocs.php. myprofile_navigation in lib.php adds "My Documents & Certificates" profile node. block_rtocompliance student view gains "My Documents & Certificates" quick link alongside My Certificates. block_aiplugin_nav user section gains student portfolio links (My Documents & Certificates + My Certificates) when local_rtocompliance is installed. SCHEMA: YES — new table local_rtocompliance_student_docs. Savepoint 2026051400178. // FIX-UNIT-CODE-SMART-DETECTION (v4.8.107): Smart cert detection now auto-detects Australian unit codes in course fullname/shortname (pattern: 2-8 letters + 3-6 digits + optional 1-2 trailing letters, e.g. BSBFIN301, CHCECE001, SITHCCC006). Previously, if the admin hadn't ticked "Nationally Recognised" in course settings, a course named "BSBFIN301 Process financial transactions" was incorrectly issued a Completion Certificate. Now: if the course name/shortname starts with a unit code, the resolve function returns reason=unit_code_detected, certtypes=[statement], qualificationcode=detected code — bypassing the DB flag entirely. New helper local_rtocompliance_extract_unit_code_from_name(). generate_course_certs.php: $nationally now derived from resolution reason (not raw DB flag) so the Smart Detection banner shows "Nationally Recognised: Yes" for auto-detected unit-code courses. New reason label added. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051400177. // FIX-GENERATE-COURSE-CERTS-MISSING-PARAM (v4.8.106): generate_course_certs.php crashed with "missingparam: courseid" when accessed directly from the nav sidebar (no courseid in URL). Changed courseid from required_param to optional_param; when absent, renders a course picker (dropdown of all non-site courses + Go button) instead of throwing. No DB schema changes. No AMD changes. Savepoint 2026051400176. // REGEN-BY-STUDENT-GROUP (v4.8.105): generate_course_certs.php now supports filtering by Moodle course group or individual student, plus a "Force Regenerate" mode that voids existing certificates and re-issues new ones (sets reissued_at, links replacement_of on new cert). New filter bar with Group and Student dropdowns; preserves filter state across GET/POST cycle. Mode selector: "Issue Missing" (skip existing — prior behaviour) vs "Force Regenerate" (void + reissue, 5 credits per new cert). Select-All-Shown button added alongside existing Select-All-Needing-Certs. SCHEMA: NO change. AMD: NO change. Savepoint 2026051400175. // BULK-COURSE-CERTS (v4.7.104): Smart bulk certificate generation for courses. New generate_course_certs.php page: lists all Moodle course completers, determines correct cert type automatically (testamur+RoR for full qualification, SoA for partial/skillset/singleunit, Completion for non-accredited), shows issued/needs-cert status per student, bulk-generates with email notification and credit deduction. Smart detection uses local_rtocompliance_courses.nationallyrecognised + local_rtocompliance_qualbuilder.producttype + course_completions. New lib.php functions: local_rtocompliance_resolve_cert_types_for_course(), local_rtocompliance_get_qualbuilder_unit_list(), local_rtocompliance_check_full_qual_completion(), local_rtocompliance_get_completed_units_for_qual(), local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert(). Enhanced mycerts.php: grouped by cert type, year filter tabs, stat cards, collapsible SoA unit lists, download+verify actions. block_rtocompliance.php: students now see "My Certificates" link. "Generate by Course" button added to certificates.php header with course-picker modal. "Generate Certificates for This Course" action card added to course_settings.php. Sidebar nav updated. SCHEMA: NO change. AMD: NO change. Savepoint 2026051400174. // FIX-CERT-BUGS-3 (v4.6.103): Three certificate fixes reported by Jamie. (1) FIX-CERT-UNITS-ISSUEDATE — 