// v4.4.19 - SAVEPOINT-ORDER-FIX (3 May 2026): Critical upgrade-path bug
// fix. The v4.4.11..v4.4.18 savepoint blocks (091..098) had been appended
// to db/upgrade.php in DESCENDING order. Moodle executes upgrade.php blocks
// top-to-bottom, capturing $oldversion once at entry. So a site upgrading
// from any pre-091 version would: (a) hit the 098 block first, write 098
// to the DB via upgrade_plugin_savepoint, (b) then hit the 097 block,
// where upgrade_plugin_savepoint(097) sees DB already at 098 and throws
// downgrade_exception "Cannot downgrade local_rtocompliance from
// 2026050200098 to 2026050200097". Fix: reordered all 8 blocks (091..098)
// into ascending numeric order so each savepoint is monotonically
// increasing. v4.4.19 itself is a marker savepoint (2026050200099) that
// gives any site whose DB recorded 098 mid-aborted-upgrade a clean path
// forward. SCHEMA: NO change. AMD: NO change.
