// Attainment fact sheet.  Audit findings:
//   #1 NRT (Nationally Recognised Training) logo missing from every
//      accredited cert.
//   #2 No authorised signatory block — required signature line +
//      printed name + title.
//   #3 AQF statement used the wrong wording: "is issued under the
//      Australian Qualifications Framework" — ASQA mandates "is
//      recognised within the Australian Qualifications Framework".
//   #4 Attainment wording wrong: "has successfully completed all
//      requirements for the qualification" — ASQA mandates "has
//      fulfilled the requirements for".
//   #5 No authenticity measure on the cert — required so a third
//      party can verify the cert is genuine (verify URL + cert
//      number bottom-right).
//
// ROOT CAUSE: cert_template renderer was already correct, but the
// legacy hard-coded TCPDF fallback in lib.php (which silently ran
// whenever no active template existed for a cert type) was missing
// all five elements — and the previous release shipped with TWO
// duplicated copies of the legacy generator (one inline in
// send_certificate_email(), one in render_certificate_pdf_string()).
// On a fresh install no default template is seeded, so the broken
// fallback was the only renderer ever hit — exactly what produced
// the non-compliant cert.
