// FIX-MAY2-LEGACY-FATAL (v4.2.56): hotfix for a fatal error reported by
// the tester when submitting the legacy 16-question suitability
// checklist: "Exception - Call to undefined function
// local_rtocompliance_notify_admin_failure()" thrown at line 55 of
// suitability_form_legacy.php.  Root cause: the helper function was
// defined at the BOTTOM of the same file, wrapped in
// if (!function_exists(...)) { function ... }.  PHP does NOT hoist
// function definitions that sit inside any conditional block, so when
// the POST handler near the top reached the call site at line 55 the
// function had not yet been declared.  Fix is structural: the same
// guarded definition is moved verbatim to the top of the file (just
// below defined('MOODLE_INTERNAL') || die();) so it is in scope by the
// time any code in the POST handler runs.  No behaviour change beyond
// the function now being callable.  Same release also corrects a long-
// standing $plugin->release string drift: the release string was still
// '4.2.48' even though numeric_version had been bumped through every
// release from 4.2.49 to 4.2.55, so Moodle's plugin admin page was
// showing the wrong human-readable version next to the correct numeric
// version.  Now bumped to '4.2.56' alongside numeric 2026050200056.
