// UI-POLISH-MAY2-PASS3 (v4.2.57, six tester-reported UI items: trainer Delete dropdown truncation; Trainer/Assessor Role + Vocational Competency Evidence list misalignment; convert those two lists from boxes to a plain vertical list; three TAS Industry Consultation AI buttons made more prominent; consultation evidence file not displaying after save). FIX-MAY2-LEGACY-FATAL — see header comment for full notes.  Originally drifted from 4.2.48 — tester compliance escalation: the previous "Pre-Enrolment Suitability Checklist" (16 Yes/Unsure/No questions answered by the student plus a "I confirm I meet this" declaration) is NOT compliant with Standard 2 PI 2(a) and PI 2(b) of the 2025 Standards for RTOs.  Those PIs require the RTO to (a) conduct a structured review of the student's prior skills, LLN, digital literacy and entry requirements, and (b) generate a documented suitability decision and provide plain-language advice to the student BEFORE enrolment.  Self-declaration ("I confirm I meet this") puts the assessment in the student's hands and fails (b).  Full rebuild in this release: (1) suitability_send.php now captures admin-side context (required prerequisite qualification, required ACSF LLN level, student's previously assessed LLN level if known) and seeds a single suitability record per send — no more 16 answer rows.  (2) suitability_form.php replaced with a 5-section evidence-collection flow (Section 1 — qualification, schooling, industry experience, digital-literacy checklist, optional reasonable-adjustment disclosure; Section 2 — read-only LLN context; Section 3 — auto-rendered system decision; Section 4 — auto-generated advice; Section 5 — declaration "I confirm the information provided is true and accurate to the best of my knowledge").  (3) lib.php gains local_rtocompliance_calculate_suitability() (decision engine: prereq check fails -> NOT_SUITABLE; LLN below required or not-yet-assessed -> SUITABLE_WITH_SUPPORT; <3 of 5 digital skills -> SUITABLE_WITH_SUPPORT; disability disclosure adds reasonable-adjustment support note) and local_rtocompliance_format_suitability_advice() which builds the plain-language explanation + next-steps the student sees on screen (and that goes into the audit PDF).  (4) suitability_view.php rebuilt: shows the captured evidence, the system decision with reasons + support, the advice text sent to the student, and a 3-outcome trainer override (Suitable / Suitable with Support / Not Suitable) with mandatory reason — meeting PI 2(b)'s "documented advice" / human-judgement-on-the-record expectation.  (5) NEW suitability_pdf.php — TCPDF-rendered audit PDF for ASQA (Student & Course summary, Section 1 evidence, Section 2 LLN, Section 3 outcome with coloured outcome banner, Section 4 advice text, trainer override block).  (6) NEW suitability_form_legacy.php — pending records created on v4.2.46 or earlier still have rows in local_rtocompliance_suitability_answers and continue to render the old 16-question form so in-flight checklists are not broken by the upgrade.  (7) install.xml + db/upgrade.php savepoint 2026050200047 add 14 columns to local_rtocompliance_suitability (qualification, experience, experience_years, industry_type, school_level, digital_skills, disability_disclosure, req_prereq, req_lln_level, lln_actual_level, reasons, support_required, advice, override_outcome) and widen the status column from 30 to 40 chars to fit override_suitable_with_support.  (8) Admin email notification rewritten to surface the new system outcome label (SUITABLE / SUITABLE WITH SUPPORT / NOT SUITABLE) plus reasons + support + reasonable-adjustment disclosure.  Backward-compat: legacy answer-row records still notify via local_rtocompliance_notify_admin_failure.  No external API changes; certificates / verify / USI / TAS flows unchanged. // BUG-MAY1-AUDIT-PASS3 — tester feedback on v4.2.45: when a student's USI is unverified, the View / Download / Email buttons on the Certificates list (and the Download PDF / Email to Student buttons on verify.php) should NOT render as greyed-out unclickable controls.  Tester wants the buttons to look normal and click-active, but the click should pop a clear "USI not verified" alert explaining that Clause 12 requires a verified USI before a Testamur or Statement of Attainment can be downloaded or emailed.  certificates.php $buildActions and verify.php verify-actions both rebuilt to render an active <a class="btn btn-primary"> with an inline onclick that fires alert() then returns false to suppress navigation.  Server-side gates in download_cert.php and email_cert.php are unchanged — they remain as defence-in-depth against direct URL access.  No DB schema change; savepoint 2026050200046. // BUG-MAY1-AUDIT-PASS2 — second pass over Errors_1_May_2026 picked up four items the v4.2.44 release didn't cover. (1) suitability_form.php intro paragraph rewritten to use the tester's exact "To be enrolled in this qualification you must meet all of the following requirements... Yes / Unsure / No" definitions plus the missing privacy / reasonable-adjustment notice. (2) Declaration text simplified to the tester's exact wording: "I confirm that my responses above are true and accurate to the best of my knowledge." (3) Category #3 renamed from "Entry Requirements" to "Entry Requirements & Prior Skills" everywhere it appears (suitability_form.php $categoryMap + suitability_send.php $previewGroups). (4) trainer_currency.php industry-currency activities list converted from <table class="generaltable"> to the same flat <ul.rtoc-vc-list> no-box stacked layout already used on trainer_voccomp.php — closes the tester's request that the simple-list pattern apply "throughout various stages of entry of data under Trainers and Assessors", not just on the voc-comp screen. No schema change; savepoint 2026050200045. // BUG-MAY1-AUDIT — full audit + fix of every bug in Errors_1_May_2026 tester report. (1) styles.css: trainer detail rows aligned with min-height + flex-stretch (Bug #2/#3); verify-card / verify-detail-row / verify-detail-label / verify-detail-value CSS added so labels and values no longer collide on the certificate verification page (Bug #12); .rtoc-vc-list (no-box stacked list for trainer Vocational Competency activities — Bug #4); .rtoc-suit-group heading style for the new 7-category Suitability Checklist; .verify-actions button row. (2) trainer_voccomp.php: replaced generaltable with the new .rtoc-vc-list (Bug #4 — list, not table). (3) tas_consultation.php: confirmed file_get_unused_draft_itemid + file_save_draft_area_files already correctly persist evidence file (Bug #7 — verified, no further code change needed). (4) students.php: Send Checklist row now hides for guest / no-email accounts and shows a "No email" badge instead of a broken send button (Bug #8). (5) qualbuilder_edit.php + amd/src/qualbuilder_edit.js: Save button defaults to btn-primary (blue) and flashes "Saved ✓" green for 2s on success then returns to blue, no longer permanently green (Bug #9). (6) Pre-enrolment Suitability Checklist FULL REWRITE (Bug #10): suitability_send.php seeded with the tester-supplied 16-question set in 7 categories (Foundation Skills, Digital Literacy, Entry Requirements, Course Readiness, Practical & Workplace, Resources & Delivery, Compliance & Support); preview block on the Send screen now shows category headings; suitability_form.php emits .rtoc-suit-group headings via $categoryMap; evidence textarea now appears on YES (was on Unsure/No) with new wording "If you selected Yes, please list the evidence you have to support this (optional)"; final disability question (Q16) uses the distinct prompt "list the disability and the additional support that you will need"; Q16 = Yes is informational (admin notified for reasonable adjustment) and does NOT mark the student unsuitable; suitability check now considers Q1-Q15 only; admin failure notification reports the disability question as "DISABILITY DISCLOSED" rather than a Q1-Q15-style failure. (7) certificates.php View action now opens download_cert.php in a new tab so staff get the PDF directly instead of being thrown to the public verification page (Bug #11). (8) verify.php: when accessed by an authenticated staff member with the issuecerts capability, now renders Back-to-Certificates / Download PDF / Email-to-Student buttons (Bug #14); public QR-scan visitors still see only the verification result. (3 May 2026).
