// USI-SETUP-FULL-FIX (v4.2.38, usi_settings.php + lang strings + classes/usi/usi_platform_client.php):
//   Honest audit found that the per-tenant USI Settings page (introduced
//   v4.2.30) was technically correct but UX-incomplete: a brand-new RTO
//   admin landing on the page would get stuck on at least three real-world
//   gotchas — wrong file extension in help text (.pfx vs keystore.xml from
//   modern RAM downloads), no mention of the myID Credential Chrome extension
//   prerequisite (without which the RAM "Create" button does nothing), and
//   no guidance for the RAM authorisation flow (principal authority must
//   invite non-PA users with "Machine credential administrator" permission).
//   v4.2.38 ships:
//     1. New form field "Expiry notification email" — sent to the platform
//        and stored in client_rto_configs.usi_notification_email so the
//        platform can email 60/30/7-day expiry warnings.
//     2. Status panel now shows: credential subject (CN), expiry date,
//        days remaining (colour-coded green/amber/red), notification email,
//        and an inline expiry-warning banner when ≤60 days remain. Server
//        decodes the PKCS#12 on upload via node-forge to extract notAfter +
//        subject CN; results stored in two new client_rto_configs columns
//        (usi_cert_expiry timestamp, usi_cert_subject text).
//     3. File <input> accept extended to .xml/.pfx/.p12 and help text now
//        explicitly mentions that modern RAM downloads are keystore.xml.
//     4. New "Step 0 — API Connection required" gate: if the plugin's
//        api_url/siteid/apikey are not yet set, the upload form is disabled
//        and a prominent CTA links to Site administration → RTO Compliance
//        → API Connection. Eliminates the previous failure mode where new
//        installs hit the page first and got a generic error.
//     5. Help panel rebuilt from 4 generic steps to 5 sections covering:
//          - Prerequisites (TOID lookup, USI Office subscriber status, myID
//            app, myID Credential Chrome extension, principal authority)
//          - Create the credential (5 steps with explicit business-selector
//            warning to prevent the wrong-ABN credential mistake)
//          - Upload here (4 steps with EVTE → PROD switch instructions)
//          - Renewal — every 2 years (with notification email mention)
//          - Troubleshooting (4 most common dead-ends with fixes)
//   Server side (lms-labs.com):
//     - shared/schema.ts adds usiCertExpiry, usiCertSubject, usiNotificationEmail
//       to client_rto_configs. Migrated via npm run db:push.
//     - server/routes.ts adds extractCertMetadata(certBase64, password) helper
//       using node-forge to decode PKCS#12 keystores. Returns {expiry,subject}
//       or {null,null} for unparseable inputs (does not throw — graceful).
//     - /api/rto/usi-cert/upload now accepts notification_email and persists
//       extracted metadata. Returns certExpiry + certSubject + notificationEmail
//       in the response.
//     - /api/usi/status now returns certExpiry, certSubject, notificationEmail,
//       daysToExpiry, expiryWarn (≤60 days), expired (<0 days). certReady is
//       false when expired.
//   No breaking changes; old uploads (from v4.2.30–v4.2.37) continue to work
//   — they simply have no expiry/subject metadata until re-uploaded.
//   Plugin DB: schema-free version bump. Savepoint 2026050100038.
