// BUG-SURVEY-AI-NOSHOW-2 (v4.2.35, ai_analysis.php):
//   A customer reported on 1 May 2026 that the v4.2.34 one-click survey AI flow
//   "still just goes back to the screen after the button is clicked and
//   after 30 seconds" with nothing visible on a customer Moodle site — yet the
//   lms-labs.com deployment logs PROVED the API worked perfectly:
//   five successful POSTs to /api/rto/ai-survey-analyze (200 OK in 5-7s
//   each, credits deducted 98006 → 97981).  The OpenAI completion
//   succeeded every time; the result simply never appeared on her screen.
//   Root cause was the redirect-on-success path: after analyze_survey_responses()
//   returned with analysis_id > 0, ai_analysis.php redirected to
//   ai_analysis.php?id=N which did a second HTTP round-trip with a
//   second DB fetch.  Any failure mode in that second trip — silent
//   get_analysis() returning null because of theme-injected output before
//   the redirect, session-lock conflicts queueing the GET behind a
//   double-clicked POST, the browser not following the 303 because the
//   form was submitted via JS .form.submit() inside an onclick that
//   returned false too late, or simply the green success toast being
//   below the theme's nav bar and the analysis section being below the
//   fold — presented to the user as "nothing happened, page just reloaded".
//   v4.2.35 ELIMINATES the redirect entirely on success.  The analysis
//   blob is ALWAYS rendered inline on the same request that produced it,
//   regardless of whether DB persistence to local_rtocompliance_ai_survey
//   succeeded.  Persistence becomes a side effect that only feeds the
//   "Previous Analyses" history table on subsequent page loads.  Also
//   adds a high-contrast green "AI analysis completed successfully"
//   banner with response-count + survey-type + year confirmation, plus
//   inline JS that scrollIntoView()'s the results section on render so
//   it cannot be missed on small screens or themes that hide Moodle's
//   standard NOTIFY_SUCCESS toast.  No DB schema change.
// BUG-SURVEY-AI-2CLICK (v4.2.34, surveys.php):
//   A customer's 1 May 2026 screenshot showed the Quality Indicator Surveys
//   page with three buttons that all just navigate to the AI Survey Analysis
//   page where she has to click ANOTHER "Run AI Analysis — 5 Credits" button
//   to actually run it: two clicks for one action.  The per-card "Run AI
//   Analysis (1 responses)" buttons looked like they should run the analysis
//   themselves — that's their entire purpose.  Fix: surveys.php now renders
//   the per-card buttons as POST forms that submit directly to
//   ai_analysis.php?action=analyze with sesskey + type + year, guarded by a
//   JS confirm() that names the response count + 5-credit cost so the user
//   can back out before spending credits.  On confirm, the same spinner UX
//   from v4.2.33 (disable + label swap to "Analysing responses (please wait
//   30-60 seconds)...") runs immediately.  The standalone "AI Survey Analysis"
//   button at the bottom of the page is left as a navigation link because it's
//   the generic entry point that lets her switch survey type / year first.
// BUG-SR-OUTCOME-SAVE-5 (v4.2.33, classes/form/enrolment_form.php + student_enrolments.php):
//   A customer's 1 May 2026 screenshot proved the v4.2.32 fix was insufficient
//   — clicking Save on the enrolment edit form bounced her to the dashboard
//   with a blue "No student was specified. Please select a student from the
//   student list." toast.  That message comes from the early-redirect at the
//   top of student_enrolments.php which fires when $userid=0.  Root cause:
//   the form ONLY had hidden inputs for id+studentid, relying on the URL
//   query string (?userid=N&action=edit&enrolid=M) attached to the form's
//   action attribute to round-trip those page-level params.  Some Moodle
//   4.5+ themes / page layouts strip the query string from form actions
//   when re-rendering, so the POST URL became /student_enrolments.php with
//   NO query string, PHP saw $userid=0, and the early "select a student"
//   redirect fired BEFORE the save block ever ran.  The form appeared to
//   silently revert because the user was bounced back to the student list
//   with the info toast — easy to mistake for a save that didn't take effect.
//   Fix: add hidden userid+action+enrolid inputs to enrolment_form.php and
//   pass them in via $customdata from student_enrolments.php so the POST
//   BODY always carries them — optional_param() then picks them up
//   regardless of whether the URL query string survived.  Belt-and-braces.
// BUG-SURVEY-AI-NORESP-2 (v4.2.33, ai_analysis.php):
//   A customer's 1 May 2026 screenshot showed the "Run AI Analysis — 5 Credits"
//   button rendered correctly with 1 completed Employer survey response
//   available — clicking did not produce any visual feedback for the 15-60
//   second OpenAI round-trip (the platform endpoint /api/rto/ai-survey-analyze
//   hits OpenAI's gpt-4o-mini synchronously), so to the user the button
//   appeared dead.  Compounding this: a frustrated double-click would fire
//   a second POST while the first was still in flight, which Moodle's session
//   lock will queue (the second request waits for the first to complete
//   before its own session unlocks), making the second redirect arrive even
//   later — feeling like nothing happens for an even longer time.  Fix:
//   native onclick handler that disables the button immediately, swaps
//   the label to a "Analysing responses (please wait 30-60 seconds)..."
//   message with an inline spinner, and submits via .form.submit().  No
//   AMD/JS module dependency to keep this 100% Moodle-version-agnostic.
// BUG-SR-OUTCOME-SAVE-4 (v4.2.32, classes/form/enrolment_form.php + student_enrolments.php):
//   A customer reported on 1 May 2026 that the Outcome=Competent + Status=Completed save
//   silently failed across THREE login roles (admin, teacher, manager) — exactly
//   the same symptom the v4.2.21 / v4.2.26 / v4.2.27 fixes were meant to
//   eliminate.  Root cause turned out to be a fourth, independent code path:
//   the courseid <select> on enrolment_form.php is built from a JOIN against
//   local_rtocompliance_qualunits OR local_rtocompliance_coursesettings.nationallyrecognised=1.
//   When EDITING an existing enrolment whose course is no longer in either
//   linkage (qual builder linkage was deleted, course was unflagged as
//   nationally recognised, or course was hidden), the dropdown silently
//   defaulted to '' (Choose...) on render.  On Save, the form's
//   `if (empty($data['courseid']))` validation check failed — the form
//   re-rendered with a tiny inline error on the courseid field that managers
//   focused on Outcome / Status never noticed.  Two-layer fix:
//   (a) enrolment_form.php — when editing, ALWAYS include the existing
//       enrolment's courseid in the select options regardless of whether
//       qual builder linkage exists.  Hidden / deleted courses are
//       labelled appropriately so the FK round-trips intact.
//   (b) student_enrolments.php — on POST without get_data() (i.e. validation
//       failed), surface a prominent top-of-page error notification listing
//       every failing field by name, so users never again see "click Save,
//       nothing happens" without any visible explanation.  Also moved the
//       set_data() call into the !$ispost branch so re-renders after
//       validation failure preserve the user's POSTed values rather than
//       reverting to the OLD record (the same ordering bug v4.2.26 fixed
//       for the SUBMITTED branch — same fix now applied to the FAILED branch).
// BUG-SURVEY-AI-NORESP (v4.2.32, surveys.php + ai_analysis.php):
//   A customer also reported on 1 May 2026 that "Run AI Analysis does nothing" across
//   all login roles for both Learner and Employer surveys.  Root cause was a
//   UX silent-fail: the surveys.php "Run AI Analysis" link landed on
//   ai_analysis.php which then rendered a small grey disabled <span> ("No
//   responses to analyse") next to the credit-cost badge whenever the calling
//   user had no completed survey responses for the year — a state that was
//   easy to miss next to all the other working buttons on the page.  Fix:
//   (a) surveys.php — pre-check $learnercount / $employercount and render the
//       button as a disabled tooltip-rich <span> when responsecount === 0,
//       so the disabled state is visible WITHOUT navigating away.
//   (b) ai_analysis.php — promote the empty-state disabled <span> to a
//       full-width yellow alert with a direct "Send survey →" CTA so the
//       reason is unmistakable and the next action is one click away.
// USI-DISCOVERABILITY (v4.2.31, settings.php + index.php + lang):
//   The v4.2.30 ship had two USI menu entries with near-identical names
//   ("USI Verification Settings" and "USI Verification — Machine Credential"),
//   the new upload page was buried at the bottom of the menu after Maintenance
//   Settings, and the dashboard had no visible signal that USI wasn't yet
//   configured.  v4.2.31 fixes the discoverability:
//   1. The Upload Machine Credential page now sits FIRST in the menu (directly
//      above the legacy USI page), renamed to "USI — Upload Machine Credential
//      (★ start here)".
//   2. The legacy local-file-path page is renamed to "USI Verification (legacy
//      local file — not recommended)" and now shows an amber redirect banner
//      at the very top pointing customers at the upload page instead.
//   3. The RTO Compliance dashboard (index.php) shows a blue "USI verification
//      is not yet set up for your RTO — Set up USI verification →" CTA card
//      to site-admins whenever neither usi_organization_id nor
//      usi_certificate_path is set.
//   No DB schema change.
// PER-TENANT-USI (v4.2.30, classes/usi/usi_platform_client.php + usi_settings.php + db tables on the platform):
//   Each customer RTO now uploads its OWN myGovID Machine Credential (.pfx) +
//   password + TOID via Site Administration → RTO Compliance → USI Settings.
//   The credential is sent to the lms-labs.com platform's new
//   /api/rto/usi-cert/upload endpoint and stored in client_rto_configs scoped
//   to this site's siteid.  Subsequent /api/usi/verify calls use THIS RTO's
//   credential (resolved from client_rto_configs by the calling siteid)
//   rather than a shared platform credential — so each RTO verifies students
//   against ITS OWN registered TOID, which is the architecture aXcelerate /
//   Wisenet / VETtrak use.  The previous shared-platform-credential model
//   resolved every verification to a single TOID (52499 — VETiS Consulting,
//   cancelled), causing every USI lookup to return the wrong RTO context.
// ROLE-SPLIT (v4.2.30, db/access.php + lib.php + trainer_dashboard.php):
//   Capability map split into three tiers — manager (full :manage + :viewall),
//   trainer (NEW :viewtrainer for editingteacher / teacher archetype, scoped
//   to own classes / students / surveys / currency profile), and student (own
//   profile only).  Trainers / assessors no longer see Governance & ADC, Fee
//   Protection, Insurance Register, NAT export, AI Survey Analysis credits,
//   or other trainers' student records.  New trainer_dashboard.php landing
//   page surfaces the trainer-scoped views (My Classes, My Students with USI
//   status, My Currency Profile, Read-only Validation Schedule).
// NAV-PRIMARY (v4.2.30, lib.php local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation):
//   The dashboard previously lived ONLY in the Site Administration tree,
//   which Moodle's standard themes (Boost, Classic) only surface to users
//   holding moodle/site:config — meaning a role-mapped manager / trainer
//   HAD the local/rtocompliance:manage cap but no nav menu entry to discover
//   or click through to the dashboard.  v4.2.30 registers an "RTO Compliance"
//   entry in Moodle's global navigation tree (Boost primary nav top bar via
//   showinflatnavigation = true) that role-routes:
//     siteadmin / manager → /local/rtocompliance/index.php
//     trainer             → /local/rtocompliance/trainer_dashboard.php
//     student (no caps)   → no nav entry shown
//   Site Administration → RTO Compliance is preserved for the actual
//   configuration / secrets pages (unchanged).
// BUG-RESULTS-NOID-BOUNCE (v4.2.29, qualbuilder_results.php):
//   The "Student Results" item in the Site Administration tree
//   (settings.php:54-59 → admin_externalpage 'local_rtocompliance_results')
//   AND the side nav (lib.php:882) both linked to qualbuilder_results.php
//   with NO ?id=N query parameter — the only place that ever passed an id
//   was the per-row "View Results" button on qualbuilder.php.  The previous
//   no-id behaviour was redirect() → qualbuilder.php with the
//   "invalidqualification" red error toast, so every top-level click on
//   "Student Results" appeared to fail with a confusing error message and
//   the page was effectively unreachable from any nav menu.  Fix: when no
//   id is supplied, render an "All Training Products" picker view listing
//   every qualification / skill set / single unit with its enrolled-student
//   count, unit count, status badge and a "View Results" button that drills
//   into the per-product report.  Search box filters by code or name.  The
//   original per-id report below the picker block is unchanged.
// BUG-SURVEY-AI-NOSHOW (v4.2.29, ai_analysis.php + survey_analyzer.php):
//   The v4.2.25 flow was POST → analyze → DB insert → redirect-with-id →
//   GET → fetch-by-id → render.  Server-side platform logs confirmed the
//   /api/rto/ai-survey-analyze API was returning 200 OK with full JSON and
//   credits were being deducted on every click, but users still reported
//   "Run AI Analysis does nothing" — root cause was the silent fall-through
//   inside survey_analyzer::analyze_survey_responses() at the inner DB
//   insert: if local_rtocompliance_ai_survey is missing or has a column-type
//   mismatch on the user's installation, the catch{} block swallows the
//   error and returns analysis_id=0.  The redirect then carried ?id=0 and
//   the "if (\$id > 0)" rendering block never fired, so the page reloaded
//   showing only the green "completed successfully" toast and an empty
//   results area — the user had paid 5 credits and saw nothing.  Fix:
//   capture the analysis result in \$inlineanalysis and render it on the
//   SAME request when persistence returns 0; surface a NOTIFY_WARNING that
//   tells admins the history could not be saved.  When persistence
//   succeeds the existing POST-redirect-GET path is preserved so the URL
//   stays bookmarkable and a hard browser refresh does not re-trigger the
//   analysis.  No DB schema change.
// BUG-SR-OUTCOME-SAVE-3 (v4.2.26, student_enrolments.php):
//   Editing a Student Records enrolment, changing Outcome to "Competency
//   achieved/pass" (20) and Status to "Completed", then clicking SAVE produced
//   NO error and NO success toast — the form simply re-rendered with the OLD
//   values "Continuing activity" (70) and "Active" still selected.  Root cause
//   was the long-standing Moodle anti-pattern at line 330: $form->set_data()
//   was being called UNCONDITIONALLY before $form->get_data(), including on
//   POST requests.  When set_data() runs after Moodle's formslib has parsed
//   the submitted POST, it overwrites the already-resolved element values
//   with the OLD database record for any element that has an explicit
//   setDefault() in the form definition — and the enrolment_form.php sets
//   defaults on outcomeidentifier ('70'), deliverymode, fundingsourcenat,
//   vetflag, vetinschoolsflag, commencingprogramid, feecharged, status
//   ('active').  get_data() then returned the OLD values, the save block
//   "successfully" wrote the OLD record back with a fresh timemodified, and
//   the user saw a perfectly silent revert.  Three-part fix:
//   (a) set_data() moved out of the unconditional path and into the
//       else-branch that runs ONLY on initial display (form not submitted,
//       not cancelled).  This is the canonical Moodle 4.x+ Form API pattern.
//   (b) Added an error_log() diagnostic just before update_record() that
//       prints submitted_outcome / submitted_status / submitted_id with the
//       prefix "[rto/enrolment-save-debug]" so server admins can confirm the
//       form actually transmitted the user's selection (vs. browser/JS
//       interference) — same diagnostic pattern as v4.2.18 USI fix.
//   (c) Added a post-save re-fetch of the row that surfaces the persisted
//       outcome + status in the success toast ("Enrolment saved successfully
//       (outcome=20, status=completed)") so the user can verify the save
//       took effect without reopening the edit form.
//   No DB schema change.
// BUG-SURVEY-AI-NOOP-2 (v4.2.25, ai_analysis.php):
//   The v4.2.24 fix used $OUTPUT->single_button() with ->add_confirm_action()
//   to replace an inline-onclick anchor that was being CSP-blocked.  However,
//   add_confirm_action() relies on the Moodle AMD module core/notification:confirm
//   to render its modal — and on some Moodle 4.5+ installations that AMD chunk
//   fails to load silently (theme override, custom JS bundle order, or browser
//   caching of an older AMD manifest).  Result: clicking the button produced
//   NO confirmation modal AND no form submission, the same "click does nothing"
//   symptom the v4.2.24 fix was supposed to cure.  Additionally,
//   single_button($url, $label, 'post', true) emits a Moodle 4.5 debug warning
//   ("$primary deprecated, use $type") rendered visibly above the button when
//   debugging is enabled.
//   Fix: replace the entire single_button + confirm-action stack with a plain
//   <form method="post"> + hidden sesskey/action/type/year inputs + native
//   <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">.  Zero JavaScript, zero
//   AMD dependency, zero deprecated constructor arguments — works identically
//   on Moodle 4.0 through 5.x.  The credit cost is already shown in the
//   "5 credits per analysis" badge AND in the button label "— 5 Credits"
//   so the confirmation modal was redundant UX noise anyway.
// BUG-TAS-OVERLAP-3 (lib.php + tas_consultation.php):
//   The v4.2.21 BUG-TAS-OVERLAP-2 flex-wrap checkbox grid still overflowed on
//   the Industry Consultation EDIT view because the helper was inserted via
//   $mform->addElement('static', ...), which wraps it in a Moodle .fitem /
//   .felement form-row whose layout effectively constrained the helper's
//   visible height — checkbox rows past the first ~5 items rendered past the
//   blue border and visually overlapped the next field's label (Key Feedback /
//   Impact on Training Delivery / Impact on Assessment Design).
//   Two-layer fix:
//   (a) lib.php local_rtocompliance_render_quickadd_helper() rewritten to
//       wrap the entire helper in a native <details>/<summary> element
//       collapsed by default with an item-count hint in the summary, and the
//       checkbox grid switched from flex-wrap (which could wrap into hidden
//       second columns) to a plain block layout with one option per row so
//       the helper grows predictably with the number of items.
//   (b) tas_consultation.php switched all three call sites from
//       addElement('static', ...) to addElement('html', ...) so Moodle does
//       not wrap the helper in a form-row at all — eliminating the parent
//       wrapper that caused the height clipping.
// BUG-DASH-FIRST-ENROL (index.php + student_enrolments.php):
//   The dashboard "Setup Progress" card's "Create Your First Enrolment" tile
//   linked to /local/rtocompliance/student_enrolments.php with NO ?userid=N
//   query parameter.  That target page requires a userid and, on receiving none,
//   rendered a hard error wall reading "No student was specified.  Please
//   select a student from the student list." with only a "Student AVETMISS
//   Profiles" button, blocking the entire onboarding step for new admins.
//   Two-layer fix:
//   (a) The dashboard tile URL changed from student_enrolments.php to
//       students.php so users land on the student picker first, then click
//       through to "Manage Enrolments" from the student row.  The hint copy
//       was updated to reflect the new flow.
//   (b) student_enrolments.php now redirects to students.php with a friendly
//       NOTIFY_INFO toast when ?userid is missing, instead of rendering the
//       error wall — defensive coverage for stale bookmarks, external links,
//       or any future link that forgets to pass userid.
// BUG-SR-OUTCOME-SAVE-2 (student_enrolments.php):
//   Editing a Student Records enrolment and clicking SAVE could fail with an opaque
//   "Could not save enrolment" toast that hid the underlying root cause.  Two
//   long-standing causes were identified and fixed:
//   (a) Moodle's date_selector with optional=true returns boolean FALSE (not null)
//       when the "Enable" checkbox is unchecked.  Inserting FALSE into the int(10)
//       activitystartdate / activityenddate / holduntil / assessmentdate columns
//       fails on strict MySQL/Postgres configs.  All four nullable date columns
//       are now coerced to strict null via the new field-cleaning loop.
//   (b) Optional select elements like deliverylocationid / programcode / unitcode
//       returned the empty-option key '' as a string for char-FK columns; some DB
//       drivers reject this.  All nullable char/int/float columns are now coerced
//       to strict null when empty, and every value is explicitly cast to its
//       expected scalar type before update_record() / insert_record().
//   The catch block now also surfaces the underlying dml_exception::$error and
//   ::$debuginfo (e.g. "Data too long for column 'unitcode'" or "cannot be null")
//   in the user-facing toast AND writes the full exception class + trace to
//   error_log() prefixed with "[rto/enrolment-save]" so admins can grep for
//   future failures.  Same diagnostic pattern as v4.2.18 USI fix.
// BUG-TAS-OVERLAP-2 (tas_consultation.php + lib.php):
//   The three "Quick-add" helpers above the Feedback / Training / Assessment
//   textareas used a fixed-height <select multiple size="5"> listbox.  On the
//   EDIT view of an existing consultation record, the surrounding Moodle
//   form-control wrapper applies a narrower width than on ADD, and the listbox
//   plus its action-button row escaped the column boundary, visually overlapping
//   the Update / Cancel buttons below.  v4.2.18 attempted a flex-wrap CSS fix
//   that was incomplete on certain Boost themes.  Now replaced entirely with a
//   flex-wrap checkbox grid (no fixed listbox height) rendered by a new shared
//   helper local_rtocompliance_render_quickadd_helper() in lib.php and a
//   companion JS function rtocAppendChecked() that reads ticked checkboxes and
//   appends each label to the destination textarea.  Same UX, more robust
//   layout that can never overflow the form column.
// BUG-SURVEY-AI-MSG (classes/ai/survey_analyzer.php + ai_analysis.php):
//   "Run AI Analysis" was showing triple-wrapped useless error toasts like
//   "Analysis failed: Error communicating with AI service: AI analysis failed:
//   <real reason>" because (a) call_platform_api threw \moodle_exception with
//   the 'ai_api_error' lang string ("Error communicating with AI service: {$a}")
//   wrapping the underlying message, (b) the server already prefixed its body
//   with "AI analysis failed: ", and (c) ai_analysis.php added "Analysis failed:"
//   on top.  Same root-cause pattern as the v4.2.18 BUG-USI-PLATFORM-MSG fix.
//   Now (i) call_platform_api throws plain \Exception with a single-layer
//   "AI analysis failed (HTTP {code}): {server_message_or_body_snippet}"
//   message — also handles non-JSON response bodies (e.g. Express HTML error
//   pages) by including a 200-char strip_tags() snippet — and (ii)
//   ai_analysis.php redirects with the message verbatim, no extra prefix.
// BUG-SURVEY-BTN-PURPLE (surveys.php):
//   The two per-card "Run AI Analysis" buttons (Learner Questionnaire +
//   Employer Questionnaire) had inline style="background: linear-gradient(135deg,
//   #6366f1 0%, #8b5cf6 100%)" forcing an indigo→purple gradient that did not
//   match the solid blue Send Survey button on the same row.  Inline style and
//   the btn-outline-primary base class both removed; both buttons are now
//   plain btn btn-primary so they render solid blue and visually match the
//   Send Survey button next to them.
// BUG-VALIDATION-METHODS-PERSIST (validation_edit.php):
//   The Validation Register form's methodology and risk-factor checkbox grids
//   were being saved as a concatenated text blob in the methodologies /
//   riskfactors columns ("tool_review, evidence_review\nfreeform notes here"),
//   then on edit re-load the entire blob was poured back into the textarea
//   field — which meant (a) the checkboxes appeared unchecked even though the
//   data WAS in the database and (b) every re-save appended the keys onto the
//   notes textarea, producing duplicated/garbled text after multiple edits.
//   Fixed by storing both fields as JSON ({"keys":[...],"notes":"..."}) and
//   adding a backwards-compatible decoder that pre-populates the individual
//   checkbox fields (method_<key>, riskfactor_<key>) and a clean notes
//   textarea on load.  Legacy concatenated-text rows are auto-migrated on
//   first edit.  No DB schema change required (column is TYPE="text").
// BUG-SR-OUTCOME (student_enrolments.php + classes/form/enrolment_form.php):
//   (a) DB update/insert and audit_logger calls are now wrapped in separate try/catch
//       blocks — any dml_exception now redirects with a user-readable error notification
//       instead of crashing with a raw Moodle error page.
//   (b) Empty deliverylocationid is coerced to null before the DB write to avoid
//       empty-string / nullable char(10) column type mismatches on strict MySQL configs.
//   (c) setDefault for outcomeidentifier corrected from '00' (invalid AVETMISS) to '70'
//       (Continuing Enrolment), matching the AVETMISS 2.3 Activity End Reason code set.
//   (d) Missing setType('deliverylocationid', PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT) added to enrolment_form.
// BUG-TAS-OVERLAP (tas_consultation.php):
//   rtocAppendDropdown() JS helper function moved from a raw echo '<script>…</script>'
//   block at the bottom of the page (blocked by Moodle 4.x CSP nonce enforcement) to
//   $PAGE->requires->js_init_code() called before $OUTPUT->header() — the function is
//   now executed with the correct nonce so "Add Selected" / "Clear field" buttons work.
// BUG-WFD-FIELD (workforce_management.php):
//   (a) "Number of hours in each assessment" row (wfm-assess) relabelled to
//       "Number of assessments per qualification" — matches the wfmRun() variable
//       assessPerQual and eliminates the duplicate/confusing label pairing.
//   (b) "Primary assessment type" <select> row relabelled to "Number of hours in each
//       assessment" and converted to <input type="number" step="0.5"> so trainers can
//       enter their actual average marking hours rather than selecting from preset
//       category approximations. parseFloat() in wfmRun() handles the new input unchanged.
// BUG-SURVEY-AI (ai_analysis.php + classes/ai/survey_analyzer.php + surveys.php):
//   (a) get_recent_analyses() in survey_analyzer.php is now wrapped in try/catch so the
//       local_rtocompliance_ai_survey table missing on pre-upgrade installs no longer
//       crashes the page at load time.
//   (b) count_records() call for responsecount in ai_analysis.php is now wrapped in
//       try/catch (defaults to 0) to prevent page crash on older schema versions.
//   (c) surveys.php: "Run AI Analysis" buttons added to both Learner and Employer survey
//       cards linking directly to ai_analysis.php?type=learner / type=employer.
// BUG-USI-NAMESPACE (classes/usi/usi_verification_service.php + classes/form/enrolment_form.php):
//   Bare class references inside namespaced files resolved with leading backslash.
//   (a) usi_verification_service.php lines 76 and 215: `core_user::get_user()` →
